asr-000064
00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.330
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Good morning.

asr-000065
00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:37.090
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I again have the honor of welcoming our friends

asr-000066
00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:37.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: from the D.C.

asr-000067
00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.270
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: for the Department of Energy and the ERC

asr-000068
00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:43.290
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and the entire energy family

asr-000069
00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:48.450
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: for the briefing of their proposed budget for fiscal year 2027.

asr-000070
00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:53.550
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 153 pesos and 70 centavos.

asr-000071
00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:57.550
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: This was the highest price of diesel

asr-000072
00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.450
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: when the conflict between the United States and Iran

asr-000073
00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.750
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: caused the effective closure of the Strait of Hormuz.

asr-000074
00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:06.870
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Transport operations,

asr-000075
00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:07.750
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: food production,

asr-000076
00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:12.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: businesses and households' budgets came under severe strain.

asr-000077
00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:18.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Deadline inflation reached 7.2% in April 2026,

asr-000078
00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:23.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: while grid alerts heightened concerns over power reliability.

asr-000079
00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:28.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The President responded by declaring a State of National Energy Emergency

asr-000080
00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:31.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: under Executive Order No. 110.

asr-000081
00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:35.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The order recognized what the crisis meant for us,

asr-000082
00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: geopolitical countries,

asr-000083
00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:41.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: political conflict had disrupted global energy supply chains

asr-000084
00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:45.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and placed upward pressure on fuel prices,

asr-000085
00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:52.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: threatening the adequacy and stability of our domestic energy supply.

asr-000086
00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:57.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But while a declaration and emergency procurement can stabilize a crisis,

asr-000087
00:07:57.110 --> 00:08:02.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: they cannot substitute for preparedness built before the shock arrives.

asr-000088
00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:06.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Leadership, competence and strong institutions matter.

asr-000089
00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:13.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That is why the Energy Family deserves both our support and our careful scrutiny.

asr-000090
00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:16.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Under the able leadership of the President,

asr-000091
00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:18.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the Uplift Committee,

asr-000092
00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:24.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and particularly through the efforts of our good Secretary Sharon Garin,

asr-000093
00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:28.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the Energy Family acted swiftly to stabilize supply

asr-000094
00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and limit further the domestic disruption.

asr-000095
00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: These efforts deserve recognition,

asr-000096
00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: even as they require our support.

asr-000097
00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:42.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It is time for us to ask why extraordinary emergency measures became necessary.

asr-000098
00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:44.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: DOE acted immediately,

asr-000099
00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:47.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: conserving critical inventories,

asr-000100
00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:49.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: improving fuel dispatch,

asr-000101
00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:56.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: securing more than 178 million liters of diesel to build an emergency fuel buffer,

asr-000102
00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:58.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: managing price adjustments,

asr-000103
00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:01.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: supporting targeted assistance,

asr-000104
00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:04.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: guarding against hoarding and profiteering,

asr-000105
00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and strengthening conservation measures.

asr-000106
00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:10.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: This was a significant corrective measure,

asr-000107
00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:14.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: but it must now be converted into a permanent,

asr-000108
00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:17.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: rules-based preparedness mechanism.

asr-000109
00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:22.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The ERC intensified market oversight and adopted measures

asr-000110
00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:26.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: to caution consumers from abrupt fuel shocks.

asr-000111
00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:30.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Its heightened data requirements helped identify generation costs,

asr-000112
00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:33.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: pressures and the interventions needed.

asr-000113
00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:36.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: For fiscal year 2027,

asr-000114
00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:41.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: this capacity should be strengthened through real-time monitoring,

asr-000115
00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:43.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: faster regulatory action,

asr-000116
00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:47.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and automatic protection for qualified lifeline consumers.

asr-000117
00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:51.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The Energy Family stood on the front line of the response

asr-000118
00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:54.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and reduced the risk of a deeper disruption.

asr-000119
00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:58.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: At the same time, the crisis revealed an implementation gap.

asr-000120
00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:02.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: A strategic petroleum reserve had been established in policy,

asr-000121
00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:04.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: since 2021,

asr-000122
00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:08.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and supported by a completed study in 2022.

asr-000123
00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:12.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Although it was not fully operational when the shock arrived,

asr-000124
00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the lesson is clear.

asr-000125
00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:18.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Policy declarations must become funded,

asr-000126
00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:23.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: measurable and operational capabilities.

asr-000127
00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:25.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: In a State of the Nation address,

asr-000128
00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:29.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the President spoke at length about the energy industry.

asr-000129
00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:30.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: He aptly said,

asr-000130
00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:35.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the past few months have reminded us that we need to increase

asr-000131
00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:41.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the amount of electricity we are receiving.

asr-000132
00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:45.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: This is a sign of a strong country.

asr-000133
00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:50.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The President called for stronger energy security,

asr-000134
00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:54.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: improved investment conditions for local and foreign capital,

asr-000135
00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:58.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and an expedited shift toward indigenous renewable energy.

asr-000136
00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:07.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Together with energy storage and more reliable transmission.

asr-000137
00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:13.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: His emphasis on these priorities reflects the central role of the Energy Family

asr-000138
00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: in advancing his vision of a stronger,

asr-000139
00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:20.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: more resilient and more prosperous Philippines.

asr-000140
00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: To my fellow legislators,

asr-000141
00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:26.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: a country that needs energy security cannot afford,

asr-000142
00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:27.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and under an unprecedented crisis,

asr-000143
00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:30.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: an underfunded energy sector.

asr-000144
00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:35.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have just witnessed what a war happening thousands of miles away

asr-000145
00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:37.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: can do to our energy supply.

asr-000146
00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:40.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And we must now prepare for El Nino,

asr-000147
00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:45.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: related risk to hydropower, peak demand and reserve margins.

asr-000148
00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:50.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But we have also seen what the Energy Family can accomplish

asr-000149
00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:53.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: when institutions act decisively.

asr-000150
00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:56.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The challenge now is to institutionalize the capacity

asr-000151
00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: before the next emergency.

asr-000152
00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Swift action matters.

asr-000153
00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:04.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Intelligent policy interventions matter.

asr-000154
00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:07.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Regulatory capacity, technical capacity,

asr-000155
00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:10.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and consumer protection all matter.

asr-000156
00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:13.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And all of these require sustained,

asr-000157
00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:18.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: well-targeted public support backed by measurable performance.

asr-000158
00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:22.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The combined proposal budget of the Energy Family

asr-000159
00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:25.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: in the amount of 56.1 billion

asr-000160
00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:28.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: is not simply an expenditure.

asr-000161
00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:32.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It is an investment in national resilience,

asr-000162
00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:35.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: an insurance policy against disruption,

asr-000163
00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:38.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and a catalyst for the reliable, affordable,

asr-000164
00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:42.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and secure energy system our economy requires.

asr-000165
00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:46.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The budget should specify targets for strategic fuel reserves

asr-000166
00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and days of supply,

asr-000167
00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:52.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: diversified import sources,

asr-000168
00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:54.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: emergency procurement lead times,

asr-000169
00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: lead reserve margins,

asr-000170
00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:59.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: transmission and storage completion,

asr-000171
00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:01.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: off-grid fuel security,

asr-000172
00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:03.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: renewable capacity,

asr-000173
00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:05.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and consumer protection.

asr-000174
00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:09.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Let us provide the Energy Family with the resources

asr-000175
00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:11.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and the laws it needs,

asr-000176
00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:14.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: not only to respond to the next crisis,

asr-000177
00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:17.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: but to prepare before it arrives.

asr-000178
00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:19.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

asr-000179
00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:21.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Mr. President.

asr-000180
00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Secretary Sharon Garin,

asr-000181
00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:26.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: we may now proceed with your presentation.

asr-000182
00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And after you,

asr-000183
00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: DRC.

asr-000184
00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.110
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir.

asr-000185
00:13:29.110 --> 00:13:30.110
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Good morning, Chair.

asr-000186
00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:31.110
