asr-000346
00:28:16.620 --> 00:28:27.840
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And with me in the commission are four other commissioners, Commissioner Florescinda Digal, Marco Fuentes, Amante Liberato, and Paris Real.

asr-000347
00:28:28.300 --> 00:28:44.840
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Our mandate is to promote market competition, ensure consumer choice, protect consumer interests, keep retail rates based on prudent and reasonable cost recovery, and penalize abuse of market power.

asr-000348
00:28:44.840 --> 00:28:59.200
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We regulate and oversee the full electricity value chain, the regulated sectors, namely the transmission and the distribution sectors, as well as the competitive sectors, the generation and supply.

asr-000349
00:28:59.800 --> 00:29:10.180
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And at the center of everything we do are the consumers, upholding the rights and interests of our consumers, both captive and contestable.

asr-000350
00:29:10.180 --> 00:29:15.910
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: The slide four is on the...

asr-000351
00:29:16.570 --> 00:29:22.770
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: In the sector that we regulate, it is currently valued at around 4.19 trillion.

asr-000352
00:29:24.510 --> 00:29:34.170
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And this is just to emphasize the scale of the sector that our proposed budget of 944 million must support.

asr-000353
00:29:35.270 --> 00:29:45.330
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: For ERC accomplishments, we have issued so far for a period from January 2025 until June 2026,

asr-000354
00:29:45.330 --> 00:29:46.330
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: 4,000...

asr-000355
00:29:46.570 --> 00:29:49.130
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and 611 decisions and orders.

asr-000356
00:29:50.470 --> 00:29:54.910
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have imposed 157 millions in fines.

asr-000357
00:29:55.210 --> 00:29:59.970
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have directed the refund of around 71.3 billion.

asr-000358
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:14.900
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: P70 billion of that came from Meralco's filing of its actual weighted average tariff for the lapsed years during the time when its rates were not reset by the earlier commission.

asr-000359
00:30:16.160 --> 00:30:21.200
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have approved 292 power supply agreements.

asr-000360
00:30:21.340 --> 00:30:27.440
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: These are the agreements between distribution utilities and generation companies for the supply of electricity.

asr-000361
00:30:27.440 --> 00:30:32.300
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And 184 of that with the final authority.

asr-000362
00:30:32.800 --> 00:30:52.300
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Comparing that to the performance of ERC during the entire 2024, we have approved in 2024 only two power supply agreement applications and five CAPEX applications.

asr-000363
00:30:52.300 --> 00:30:57.300
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: For the lifeline rate program in...

asr-000364
00:30:57.440 --> 00:31:11.240
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: response to the call of the president to expand the scope and coverage of the lifeline program under IPIRA as extended by law.

asr-000365
00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:25.640
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have actually launched a national lifeline program, expanded its coverage to up to 50 kilowatt hours for the marginalized end users.

asr-000366
00:31:25.860 --> 00:31:27.240
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And right now, the coverage...

asr-000367
00:31:27.440 --> 00:31:31.540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: is up by 85.33%.

asr-000368
00:31:31.540 --> 00:31:39.640
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And right now, we are able to cater to around 620,000 qualified marginalized end users.

asr-000369
00:31:40.500 --> 00:31:49.520
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Net metering also, in response to the call of the president, net metering registrations are up 51.77%.

asr-000370
00:31:49.520 --> 00:31:57.420
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And so far as the implementation of retail competition or ARCOA, with even the lowering of the threshold...

asr-000371
00:31:57.440 --> 00:32:24.960
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: to 100 kilowatt, where those with demand of 100 kilowatt can now choose their own supplier, we've seen and estimated that the cost savings to these customers that opted to avail of their choice and contracted with retailers, the estimated cost savings to them already amounted to 19.87 billion.

asr-000372
00:32:24.960 --> 00:32:26.960
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, among the landmark...

asr-000373
00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:39.420
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: decisions that we have issued, aside from the lowering of the contestable threshold to 100 kilowatt, we have issued the first ever transmission wheeling rules for the off-grid.

asr-000374
00:32:39.420 --> 00:32:56.420
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: This is the first time that we would have a regulatory framework for the transmission service to be provided in the off-grid areas, starting with Mindoro and Palawan as soon as this is established.

asr-000375
00:32:56.420 --> 00:32:57.420
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have...

asr-000376
00:32:57.440 --> 00:33:14.860
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: restarted the rate reset of our private distribution utilities and directed the private distribution utilities to respectively file their actual weighted average tariff filings.

asr-000377
00:33:14.860 --> 00:33:27.260
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And we have also addressed thousands of CAPEX filings and point-to-point transmission proposals.

asr-000378
00:33:27.440 --> 00:33:30.420
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have disposed of thousands of them.

asr-000379
00:33:31.260 --> 00:33:48.960
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And we have supported the push for renewable energy by performing our part in the J-UP program of the Department of Energy.

asr-000380
00:33:48.960 --> 00:33:52.720
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have set the reserve price for the off-grid.

asr-000381
00:33:53.460 --> 00:33:56.960
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: For the offshore wind, we have also...

asr-000382
00:33:57.440 --> 00:34:03.220
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: set the reserve price for the Pioneer Waste to Energy Projects.

asr-000383
00:34:03.220 --> 00:34:18.900
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have established for the first time the Green Energy Auction Allowance to be able to support the new capacities that are being built under the J-UP program of the Department of Energy.

asr-000384
00:34:21.170 --> 00:34:26.790
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have also updated our rules on the advanced metering infrastructure...

asr-000385
00:34:29.010 --> 00:34:34.190
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: so that we can finally modernize our grid.

asr-000386
00:34:34.910 --> 00:34:41.210
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have addressed long-standing issues in the generation sector, such as the public offering requirement,

asr-000387
00:34:41.990 --> 00:34:44.630
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: the fit adjustment issue.

asr-000388
00:34:44.630 --> 00:34:46.630
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have updated the fit allowance.

asr-000389
00:34:47.610 --> 00:34:54.430
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have updated the UCME as well as the SAGAR in some of the off-grid areas.

asr-000390
00:34:55.230 --> 00:34:58.630
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And every one of these, among others, was delivered within...

asr-000391
00:34:59.010 --> 00:35:03.010
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: our approved budget for 2026.

asr-000392
00:35:03.010 --> 00:35:25.170
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And for 2027, our priorities remain to have fair and evidence-based rate setting, timely resolution of pending cases, robust oversight to foster competition, and a stable and enhanced regulatory environment to attract investment in our sector.

asr-000393
00:35:25.170 --> 00:35:28.170
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And all these are anchored in proactive consumer finance.

asr-000394
00:35:29.010 --> 00:35:53.170
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: For our thrust on fair and evidence-based rate setting, aside from setting the gear prices for our J-UP, we have already issued the draft rules governing the regulatory framework for our gas auction.

asr-000395
00:35:53.170 --> 00:35:55.670
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We will soon be finalizing that.

asr-000396
00:35:56.290 --> 00:35:58.170
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We are targeting to...

asr-000397
00:35:59.010 --> 00:36:12.490
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: enforce more strictly the distribution utilities' least-cost supply obligations under our revised 2026 CSP guidelines.

asr-000398
00:36:12.650 --> 00:36:24.770
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And soon, the guidelines that we will issue on the review of the terms of reference to be used by our distribution utilities that will be conducting their CSPs.

asr-000399
00:36:24.770 --> 00:36:28.770
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And that will also include our target of conducting more timely...

asr-000400
00:36:29.010 --> 00:36:32.690
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: audits of the de-use implementation of their pass-through charges.

asr-000401
00:36:33.350 --> 00:36:46.830
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We will also complete the reset of the rates of the distribution utilities, both the private distribution utilities and the electric cooperatives.

asr-000402
00:36:47.330 --> 00:36:50.250
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: This has not been done in more than 10 years.

asr-000403
00:36:50.910 --> 00:36:55.670
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: There has been no new rates approved for our distribution utilities.

asr-000404
00:36:55.670 --> 00:36:58.270
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: But only just last month.

asr-000405
00:36:59.010 --> 00:37:12.910
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have already approved the final determination for the rate reset of one of our private distribution utilities belonging to the Group A under the performance-based regulation.

asr-000406
00:37:13.230 --> 00:37:17.870
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And all the other distribution utilities in Group A will follow suit.

asr-000407
00:37:17.870 --> 00:37:27.870
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We are targeting to complete the rate reset of Group B within the year and for Group C and D for the private distribution utilities.

asr-000408
00:37:29.010 --> 00:37:31.550
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: All this will happen in 2027.

asr-000409
00:37:32.070 --> 00:37:36.050
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So this is something that was not done in more than a decade.

asr-000410
00:37:36.290 --> 00:37:44.390
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And we are targeting to finish the rate reset of the private distribution utilities in 2027.

asr-000411
00:37:44.850 --> 00:37:55.770
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Also, the new rates of our electric cooperatives, we target that they would have already their new rates to be implemented starting January.

asr-000412
00:37:55.770 --> 00:37:58.850
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Again, this is something that has not been done.

asr-000413
00:37:59.010 --> 00:38:00.630
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: For more than a decade.

asr-000414
00:38:00.990 --> 00:38:08.550
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: The last rate setting for our electric cooperatives happened in early 2010.

asr-000415
00:38:09.010 --> 00:38:14.670
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So after more than a decade, we will soon have their new rates.

asr-000416
00:38:14.670 --> 00:38:23.850
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And this is in time also for the push now for our distribution utilities to address their system losses.

asr-000417
00:38:24.690 --> 00:38:28.970
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And prepare them for the eventual removal of the system losses.

asr-000418
00:38:29.010 --> 00:38:32.950
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: As indicated by the President.

asr-000419
00:38:35.370 --> 00:38:47.110
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: For the trust on consumer-focused leadership, we have just approved the revised Magna Carta for electricity consumers.

asr-000420
00:38:47.110 --> 00:39:00.590
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And we intend to conduct an extensive information and education campaign across the country to be able to educate and inform.

asr-000421
00:39:00.590 --> 00:39:05.510
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Our consumers as regards their rights under the Magna Carta.

asr-000422
00:39:06.470 --> 00:39:11.250
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: For our budget, our budget for 2027.

asr-000423
00:39:13.250 --> 00:39:26.030
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Or over the years, our GAA grew modestly from 911.6 million in 2024 to 931 million in 2026.

asr-000424
00:39:26.030 --> 00:39:29.190
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Or increases of roughly 2%.

asr-000425
00:39:29.190 --> 00:39:30.130
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And then.

asr-000426
00:39:30.590 --> 00:39:32.150
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: 0.04%.

asr-000427
00:39:32.150 --> 00:39:47.270
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We have proposed a budget of 1.7 billion to be able to cover all the plans and programs that we intend to implement for 2027.

asr-000428
00:39:47.270 --> 00:39:58.690
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Unfortunately, the NEP only reflects 944.065 million or 44.67% below what we proposed.

asr-000429
00:39:59.170 --> 00:40:00.390
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: The variance.

asr-000430
00:40:00.590 --> 00:40:00.810
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Is.

asr-000431
00:40:02.150 --> 00:40:06.690
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Concentrated mainly in the MOOE and capital outlay.

asr-000432
00:40:06.690 --> 00:40:26.010
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And in the MOOE included there is the budget for the consultancy services that we intended supposedly to assist us complete the rate reset of our private distribution utilities and electric cooperatives as well as NGCP for 2027.

asr-000433
00:40:27.430 --> 00:40:30.390
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Our overall utilization rate has climbed.

asr-000434
00:40:30.590 --> 00:40:31.190
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Steadily.

asr-000435
00:40:31.190 --> 00:40:42.850
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So that will show our absorptive capacity and our ability to responsibly manage a larger budget.

asr-000436
00:40:43.490 --> 00:40:55.270
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So from a low of 28.08% in 2021, it has risen to 46.81 in June of 2026.

asr-000437
00:40:55.430 --> 00:40:59.090
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So that covers the first semester of the year.

asr-000438
00:40:59.090 --> 00:40:59.750
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And.

asr-000439
00:41:00.590 --> 00:41:13.490
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: On an annual basis, our full year utilization last year was already at 84.20% up from a low of 62%.

asr-000440
00:41:13.490 --> 00:41:30.370
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: In 2023, our revenues, we have consistently brought in more to the to the government in terms of the supervision fees, as well as the permit fees and fines that we collect.

asr-000441
00:41:30.590 --> 00:41:31.250
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And.

asr-000442
00:41:31.250 --> 00:41:31.550
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: The.

asr-000443
00:41:31.550 --> 00:41:32.370
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And.

asr-000444
00:41:32.370 --> 00:41:33.590
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: In 2025.

asr-000445
00:41:34.130 --> 00:41:52.090
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: With a budget of 20 of 931 million, we were able to bring to the government a total of 2.354 billion in revenue or 121% above our, our projection.

asr-000446
00:41:52.710 --> 00:41:59.210
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And definitely way above the budget that was allocated for us in 2025.

asr-000447
00:41:59.210 --> 00:42:00.270
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And.

asr-000448
00:42:00.590 --> 00:42:30.570
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We expect that we will hit the same level for 2027 so bottom line is the ERC is a net revenue generator for the government and this budget request of 1.7 billion would have been offset by what we return to the treasury and unfortunately our NEP stands out.

asr-000449
00:42:30.590 --> 00:42:38.490
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: It stands only at 944 million. That will be the end of my presentation. Your honors, thank you very much.

asr-000450
00:42:38.490 --> 00:43:01.960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Chair. This is going to be a working lunch. Para lang malaman ng colleagues natin, we distributed a presentation of NEA, NAPOCOR, PNOC, PNOC-EC, PISAM, and TRANSCO.

asr-000451
00:43:01.960 --> 00:43:08.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So nasa inyo na po yung briefer po nila. Para po mas mabilis po tayo.

asr-000452
00:43:08.480 --> 00:43:30.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But before I call on to the interpreter, I would like to recognize Congressman Salvador Plato, Vice Chair Bernadette Barberis, Vice Chair Maria Cristina Talavera Lopez, Deputy Minority Leader Presley Desus, Congressman John Chan,

asr-000453
00:43:31.960 --> 00:43:56.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Congressman Julio Cesar Vergara, Congressman Steve Solon, Congressman Dibutuan, Congressman Ernel Ceniza, Congressman Munir Arbizon, Congressman Joseph Yu, Vice Chair Isabela Zagadbaria, Representative Catherine Guraceta.

asr-000454
00:43:56.640 --> 00:43:59.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you for your presence.

asr-000455
00:44:01.960 --> 00:44:16.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The interpellation may remind our distinguished colleagues that each member is allotted five minutes for questions or interpellation, excluding the response of the resource person.

asr-000456
00:44:17.380 --> 00:44:29.290
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: When the bell sounds, the members have 30 minutes to conclude or wind up.

asr-000457
00:44:30.110 --> 00:44:34.670
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Consistent with the longstanding practice of the House, the Chair shall recognize minority.

asr-000458
00:44:35.410 --> 00:44:40.970
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Independent and majority members in an alternating manner when practicable.

asr-000459
00:44:41.550 --> 00:44:47.730
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The Chair first recognizes the Honorable Percy Zendanya from the minority.

asr-000460
00:44:48.590 --> 00:44:49.810
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pag-uswang Percy, you have the floor.

asr-000461
00:44:50.730 --> 00:44:57.190
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chair. Magandang umaga po sa DOE family led by Secretary Sharon.

asr-000462
00:44:57.990 --> 00:44:59.830
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ito po mga nakakaraang araw.

asr-000463
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:03.260
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: karami-rami na po tayo ng mga hinarap ng mga budget briefings.

asr-000464
00:45:03.400 --> 00:45:08.200
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At kadalasan po, yung mga budget briefings na ito ay mga grievance mechanisms

asr-000465
00:45:08.200 --> 00:45:14.060
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: para po sa mga departamento na nakaranas ng matinding mga pagbabas sa kanilang budget.

asr-000466
00:45:14.680 --> 00:45:18.900
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At siguro po, in so many days, this is the first time na wala akong gano'ng narinig

asr-000467
00:45:18.900 --> 00:45:22.220
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: na grievance from our colleagues from the executive.

asr-000468
00:45:22.560 --> 00:45:27.780
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Napansin ko rin po na across all areas, from PS, MOOE hanggang CO,

asr-000469
00:45:27.780 --> 00:45:36.200
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: ay may increase po tayo with an overall increase of more than a little over 25%.

asr-000470
00:45:36.200 --> 00:45:39.080
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Secretary Green, why is this the case po for DOE kaya?

asr-000471
00:45:40.460 --> 00:45:48.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I think, Mr. Chair, I think because the increases are focused on three things.

asr-000472
00:45:49.260 --> 00:45:53.700
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's the gradiometry, mobile energy system, and the automation.

asr-000473
00:45:53.700 --> 00:45:55.600
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Just briefly lang.

asr-000474
00:45:56.100 --> 00:45:57.700
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yung gradiometry.

asr-000475
00:45:57.780 --> 00:46:02.460
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kasi wala tayong data on what we have as resources here in the Philippines

asr-000476
00:46:02.460 --> 00:46:04.300
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: on oil and gas and other matters.

asr-000477
00:46:04.700 --> 00:46:08.600
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, this should have been done 10, 20 years back.

asr-000478
00:46:08.700 --> 00:46:10.840
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That's why we don't have any new exploration.

asr-000479
00:46:11.040 --> 00:46:12.900
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We only have malampaya until today.

asr-000480
00:46:13.500 --> 00:46:17.120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, with that new data, investors will see what we have.

asr-000481
00:46:17.440 --> 00:46:19.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We cannot sell something that we don't know what's in it.

asr-000482
00:46:19.980 --> 00:46:22.700
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, that's why we need the gradiometry study.

asr-000483
00:46:22.820 --> 00:46:25.580
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It will take about 2 billion pesos.

asr-000484
00:46:25.580 --> 00:46:27.580
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: This is a continuing project, 2026.

asr-000485
00:46:27.780 --> 00:46:28.500
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: 2026 was funded.

asr-000486
00:46:29.060 --> 00:46:34.960
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, another budget was allotted for 2027, sir.

asr-000487
00:46:35.020 --> 00:46:36.580
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: This is for energy security.

asr-000488
00:46:37.060 --> 00:46:40.860
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Now, the MES is a mobile energy system na parang siyang container.

asr-000489
00:46:41.200 --> 00:46:50.640
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Tapos may mga solar panels with battery and maybe turbina ng for diesel or whatever technology there is.

asr-000490
00:46:50.980 --> 00:46:53.680
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That will address that whenever there's an emergency,

asr-000491
00:46:53.680 --> 00:46:57.760
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: we can deploy these units to, for example,

asr-000492
00:46:57.780 --> 00:47:04.620
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: the usual path would be like Masbate, Bicol area, and up to the north.

asr-000493
00:47:04.740 --> 00:47:11.080
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we'll deploy it strategically in some parts also, in some islands na wala talagang connection.

asr-000494
00:47:11.280 --> 00:47:13.780
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We can put it there like what we did in Kalayaan.

asr-000495
00:47:15.380 --> 00:47:16.160
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kalayaan ba tama?

asr-000496
00:47:16.540 --> 00:47:17.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pag-asa pala.

asr-000497
00:47:17.820 --> 00:47:18.620
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pag-asa.

asr-000498
00:47:19.180 --> 00:47:22.760
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The third one, sir, is the ISSP.

asr-000499
00:47:23.280 --> 00:47:24.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: DOE needs to be automated.

asr-000500
00:47:24.820 --> 00:47:27.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Otherwise, there are more contracts.

asr-000501
00:47:27.780 --> 00:47:32.040
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Every year and every month, actually, but the system is still manual.

asr-000502
00:47:32.560 --> 00:47:41.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, for us to have a more data-driven data analysis also of what we need as policies,

asr-000503
00:47:41.520 --> 00:47:47.060
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: we need it to be automated so we can move faster and be more transparent.

asr-000504
00:47:47.280 --> 00:47:51.960
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, this is to automate from front to back end, Mr. Chair.

asr-000505
00:47:51.960 --> 00:47:57.200
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, those are the three that contributed to the 25% increase, Mr. Chair.

asr-000506
00:47:59.480 --> 00:48:04.840
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kaya ako po tinanong, kasi mapapasana all po pala tayo when we listen to the budget of the DOE.

asr-000507
00:48:04.980 --> 00:48:09.240
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sana yung equally critical agencies natin, lalong-lalong yung social services,

asr-000508
00:48:09.380 --> 00:48:16.620
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: would also enjoy the same increase in their budget and not a significant cut as we have seen the past few days.

asr-000509
00:48:16.900 --> 00:48:20.180
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Thank you, Madam Secretary, for the very comprehensive explanation.

asr-000510
00:48:20.740 --> 00:48:23.980
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Alam ko po, bahagi ito na isang malaking programa at isang malaking plano.

asr-000511
00:48:24.060 --> 00:48:27.780
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Pero po para sa ating mga kababayan na nakikinig, given all this po,

asr-000512
00:48:28.100 --> 00:48:29.460
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: bababa na po ba ang presyo ng kuryente?

asr-000513
00:48:29.480 --> 00:48:34.420
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, just before that, Mr. Chair,

asr-000514
00:48:34.600 --> 00:48:41.760
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: the 25% increase in comparison to the other agencies is 25% of 2.5 billion.

asr-000515
00:48:41.960 --> 00:48:44.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's really very small compared to the other agencies.

asr-000516
00:48:45.340 --> 00:48:50.480
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Now, to lower the price of electricity, it's a very multifaceted issue.

asr-000517
00:48:51.620 --> 00:48:55.180
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We are, if we have, generally, yes, sir.

asr-000518
00:48:55.500 --> 00:48:58.000
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If you ask me, yes, it will lower the price.

asr-000519
00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:01.840
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If we have more oil and gas that are indigenous, yes, it will lower it.

asr-000520
00:49:01.880 --> 00:49:05.260
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If we have more renewable, yes, it will lower it.

asr-000521
00:49:05.320 --> 00:49:10.980
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If we have a good coordination between the policy and then the regulation,

asr-000522
00:49:12.300 --> 00:49:16.740
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: those are several, we need several things to make it lower and lower.

asr-000523
00:49:17.080 --> 00:49:22.980
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And all these policies, eventually, the intention of all the policies that DOE is doing now,

asr-000524
00:49:23.360 --> 00:49:25.520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: the intention really is to lower the rates, sir.

asr-000525
00:49:26.680 --> 00:49:27.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-000526
00:49:28.000 --> 00:49:33.080
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Maraming salamat po, Madam Secretary, for giving that assurance sa mga kababayan po nating nanonood.

asr-000527
00:49:33.240 --> 00:49:37.040
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At araw-araw po ay kinakabanting makakatanggap ng kanilang electric bill.

asr-000528
00:49:37.520 --> 00:49:41.280
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Alam na po siguro ng NEA na itatanong ko ang question na ito.

asr-000529
00:49:41.420 --> 00:49:42.900
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sukin nyo na po ako taon-taon.

asr-000530
00:49:43.220 --> 00:49:45.820
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Pero nalulungkot po ako na sukin nyo ako taon-taon.

asr-000531
00:49:46.320 --> 00:49:50.380
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Last year po sa budget hearing natin, nabanggit po ng NEA Administrator, Nani Almeda,

asr-000532
00:49:50.380 --> 00:49:54.740
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: na i-rescind ng NEA ang Memorandum No. 2023-52.

asr-000533
00:49:55.320 --> 00:49:57.960
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Pero alam po natin na hindi ito na-rescind.

asr-000534
00:49:58.000 --> 00:49:59.980
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And in fact, suspended lamang po ito.

asr-000535
00:50:00.480 --> 00:50:05.160
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ang tanong ko po, bakit po hindi pa na-rescind ng NEA ang iligal na memorandum na ito?

asr-000536
00:50:05.500 --> 00:50:07.680
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Tapos kanina po kasi, I was looking at the presentation,

asr-000537
00:50:08.200 --> 00:50:11.200
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: ang dami pong mga linemen na mga electric co-ops,

asr-000538
00:50:11.300 --> 00:50:16.820
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: na siyang bayani natin para ma-restore ang electricity every time merong malaking sakuna sa ating bansa.

asr-000539
00:50:17.280 --> 00:50:21.280
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Pero marami po sa kanila na pagkakaitan ng collective bargaining agreement

asr-000540
00:50:21.280 --> 00:50:24.160
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: dahil po dito sa inyong iligal na memorandum na ito.

asr-000541
00:50:24.160 --> 00:50:27.580
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: So ma, ano po nangyari, Admin Almeda?

asr-000542
00:50:28.000 --> 00:50:29.440
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000543
00:50:30.280 --> 00:50:37.020
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: We have addressed the situation of the collective bargaining agreement issue.

asr-000544
00:50:38.180 --> 00:50:41.740
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Just for the information of the committee,

asr-000545
00:50:42.500 --> 00:50:49.320
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: we have already sat down with the Secretary of Labor and the various groups

asr-000546
00:50:49.320 --> 00:50:57.060
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: and we are coming up with a manualization of the Electric Cooperative Industry Tripartite Council.

asr-000547
00:50:57.520 --> 00:50:57.980
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Okay.

asr-000548
00:50:58.000 --> 00:51:04.760
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Wherein DOLE, the National Mediation Board, NEA, and the labor groups

asr-000549
00:51:04.760 --> 00:51:10.860
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: will work together in a technical working group committee

asr-000550
00:51:10.860 --> 00:51:17.160
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: to come up with the guidelines of the rules that will govern the collective bargaining agreement.

asr-000551
00:51:17.160 --> 00:51:23.540
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: I beg your indulgence, sir.

asr-000552
00:51:24.700 --> 00:51:26.160
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: We cannot...

asr-000553
00:51:26.160 --> 00:51:27.160
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: The memorandum...

asr-000554
00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:30.300
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: The subject memorandum is suspended.

asr-000555
00:51:30.940 --> 00:51:39.800
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: It's suspended for the simple reason that there are peculiarities in the electric cooperative industry.

asr-000556
00:51:39.800 --> 00:51:42.360
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: That has to be considered.

asr-000557
00:51:42.860 --> 00:51:47.520
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: But we are trying to resolve everything through this tripartite council

asr-000558
00:51:47.520 --> 00:51:54.220
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: as well as the due representation of the federation and the labor groups concerned.

asr-000559
00:51:54.800 --> 00:51:57.300
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: And hopefully, we can move forward.

asr-000560
00:51:57.300 --> 00:52:00.300
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: We have already convened two weeks ago.

asr-000561
00:52:00.440 --> 00:52:02.520
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Our next meeting will be on September 10.

asr-000562
00:52:02.960 --> 00:52:08.060
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: And once we are able to come up with a resolution through the tripartite council,

asr-000563
00:52:08.500 --> 00:52:13.860
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: everything will be within the framework of the manualization, sir.

asr-000564
00:52:14.240 --> 00:52:15.220
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000565
00:52:15.320 --> 00:52:17.060
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Maraming salamat po, Admin Almeda.

asr-000566
00:52:17.140 --> 00:52:18.980
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Pasensya na po kayo sa impatience, no?

asr-000567
00:52:19.020 --> 00:52:24.380
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kasi marami po ang mga nakabimbi ng mga CBA ng ating mga unions,

asr-000568
00:52:24.380 --> 00:52:27.280
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: iba't iba mga power cooperatives po sa ating bansa.

asr-000569
00:52:27.300 --> 00:52:31.680
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kung ito po ay sa Senado, sasabihin po sa akin nung kabilang side na asked and answered.

asr-000570
00:52:31.940 --> 00:52:34.020
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: This was the same question I raised last year.

asr-000571
00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:37.020
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And more or less, this is the same answer that I'm getting this year.

asr-000572
00:52:37.760 --> 00:52:44.280
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Mr. Chair, just for the information, there were a lot of CBAs that were already resolved.

asr-000573
00:52:45.720 --> 00:52:54.460
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Medyo dun lang po talaga sa mga CBAs that will affect the very operations of the electric cooperatives.

asr-000574
00:52:54.460 --> 00:52:57.200
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: NEA has been trying to find a way.

asr-000575
00:52:57.300 --> 00:53:00.740
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: On how to give in to the demands in the CBA.

asr-000576
00:53:01.180 --> 00:53:02.180
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Mr. Chair, thank you.

asr-000577
00:53:02.660 --> 00:53:04.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Again, I'll go back to my previous question.

asr-000578
00:53:05.200 --> 00:53:08.060
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Will this illegal memorandum be rescinded?

asr-000579
00:53:10.330 --> 00:53:15.730
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Eventually, sir, if we will be able to come up with resolutions through the Tripartite Council,

asr-000580
00:53:16.050 --> 00:53:17.410
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: it will be rescinded, sir.

asr-000581
00:53:17.750 --> 00:53:18.850
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Not only suspended.

asr-000582
00:53:19.890 --> 00:53:22.150
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: That was the answer last year.

asr-000583
00:53:22.290 --> 00:53:23.670
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And it has been a year after.

asr-000584
00:53:24.170 --> 00:53:26.430
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kawawa naman po yung ating mga manggagawa.

asr-000585
00:53:26.550 --> 00:53:28.290
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sana po sa susunod na budget hearing,

asr-000586
00:53:28.290 --> 00:53:33.950
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: hindi na po ito ating tanong kasi po na-rescind na ang Memorandum No. 2023-52.

asr-000587
00:53:34.350 --> 00:53:41.250
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: We will also forward a comprehensive list of the concerns for our colleagues from Power Centro.

asr-000588
00:53:41.590 --> 00:53:43.790
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ito po yung mga bayani natin sa power sector.

asr-000589
00:53:44.130 --> 00:53:46.030
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At bigyan po natin sila ng tamang pagkilala.

asr-000590
00:53:46.350 --> 00:53:52.170
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At bayan po natin yung mga gagawa na tinitiyak na may kuryenteng dumadaloy sa bawat tahanan po sa mga lugar sa Pilipinas.

asr-000591
00:53:52.510 --> 00:53:53.870
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Maraming pong salamat, Mr. Chair.

asr-000592
00:53:54.190 --> 00:53:55.970
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And maraming salamat po sa DOE family.

asr-000593
00:53:55.970 --> 00:53:58.210
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Congressman Zendaya.

asr-000594
00:53:58.290 --> 00:54:04.430
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

asr-000595
00:54:05.250 --> 00:54:11.010
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Next to interpolate from the majority, Congressman Celso Rehensha.

asr-000596
00:54:11.770 --> 00:54:13.330
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sir, to recognize.

asr-000597
00:54:14.150 --> 00:54:15.710
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000598
00:54:20.490 --> 00:54:28.690
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: I would like to raise this concern on Iligan City regarding the rising electricity costs and supply stability.

asr-000599
00:54:29.030 --> 00:54:36.930
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: Mr. Chair, Iligan's electricity charge increased from 13 pesos and 60 centavos per kilowatt

asr-000600
00:54:37.090 --> 00:54:45.330
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: hour in July 2026 to 15 pesos and 13 centavos per kilowatt hour in August this year also,

asr-000601
00:54:45.650 --> 00:54:52.470
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: an increase of 1 peso and 52 centavos, or an 11.19 percent in just one month.

asr-000602
00:54:53.950 --> 00:55:00.550
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: At this level, Iligan is among the higher rates charged by major distribution utilities in the country.

asr-000603
00:55:00.890 --> 00:55:05.990
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: For comparison, Mr. Chair, reported rates are approximately

asr-000604
00:55:05.990 --> 00:55:22.750
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: 14.96 pesos per kilowatt hour for BICO or Visayas Electric Cooperative and 14 pesos and 78 centavos for Meralco and 12.31 pesos for Cipalco.

asr-000605
00:55:22.750 --> 00:55:38.980
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: This is particularly concerning because Iligan, Mr. Chair, is the host of Agus 5, 6, and 7 with a combined dependable capacity of approximately 279 MW.

asr-000613
00:55:38.980 --> 00:55:53.330
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: Mr. Chair, with this, I would like to address my concern to the PISAM through the help of the Honorable Secretary.

asr-000614
00:55:53.330 --> 00:56:39.960
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: The following points. Number one, Mr. Chair, what was the basis for reducing the firm allocation serving Iligan to 8.75 MW, where the city's actual demand, supply needs, and the possible impact on consumers considered? Number two, can the PISAM consider providing an additional 16.25 MW of firm power, bringing the allocation serving Iligan City back to 25 MW, if feasible as an interim measure while longer-term supply alternatives are being pursued? Those are the two concerns, Mr. Chair. PISAM?

asr-000615
00:56:42.200 --> 00:56:55.120
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: Mr. Chair, regarding the first question on why there were reductions in our capacity allocations for certain cooperatives and distributed utilities, sir,

asr-000616
00:56:55.120 --> 00:56:58.620
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: we implemented a program in 2026, re-evaluation.

asr-000617
00:56:58.640 --> 00:57:20.920
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: We had to reduce the supply requirements because what we provide to our co-ops is based on the actual capacity of the power plants.

asr-000618
00:57:20.920 --> 00:57:28.180
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: And due to the reductions in the dependable capacity of Agus and Pulangi, we also had to correspondingly reduce.

asr-000620
00:57:28.720 --> 00:57:33.900
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: Our capacity allocations for co-ops to use, including illegal light and power.

asr-000621
00:57:34.840 --> 00:57:42.780
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: As to the second question, sir, if it's possible to increase the capacity allocation to illegal light and power, sir,

asr-000622
00:57:43.180 --> 00:57:52.880
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: as I committed to you earlier, sir, on our side meeting, sir, PISAM and our trading team will evaluate the request of illegal light

asr-000623
00:57:52.880 --> 00:57:58.520
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: and we will try to increase the firm and if not non-firm allocation to illegal light and power, sir.

asr-000624
00:57:58.640 --> 00:58:00.860
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: Thank you. Thank you very much, sir. And, Mr. Chair.

asr-000625
00:58:01.880 --> 00:58:10.280
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: Mr. Chair, we understand, Mr. Chair, that the PISAM has limited capacity and must follow its policies.

asr-000626
00:58:10.280 --> 00:58:14.820
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: We are not asking preferential treatment or special treatment.

asr-000627
00:58:15.460 --> 00:58:23.000
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: We are asking for assistance for our consumers, given illegal role as host to major national power assets.

asr-000628
00:58:23.620 --> 00:58:28.440
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: We respectfully seek a fair and practical solution that can provide greater supply,

asr-000629
00:58:28.640 --> 00:58:31.200
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: stability, and more reasonable electricity costs.

asr-000630
00:58:32.420 --> 00:58:38.060
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: Mr. Chair, I also raise this because the issue may not be unique to Iligan.

asr-000631
00:58:39.060 --> 00:58:44.960
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: How firm power is allocated with the local demand and consumer impact are considered.

asr-000632
00:58:45.460 --> 00:58:47.180
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: Could affect other districts as well.

asr-000633
00:58:47.180 --> 00:58:55.140
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: We hope that Iligan's case can also help guide a fair approach for similarly situated communities.

asr-000634
00:58:55.620 --> 00:58:57.980
Rep. Celso G. Regencia: Thank you, Mr. Chair. That's all.

asr-000635
00:58:58.640 --> 00:59:00.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you. Thank you, Kong.

asr-000636
00:59:01.160 --> 00:59:07.740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Next to interpolate, the idol of my mom and mine as well, Congressman Chaldokno.

asr-000637
00:59:09.420 --> 00:59:12.840
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Marami salamat po, Chair. Magandang umaga po sa atin lahat.

asr-000638
00:59:14.120 --> 00:59:20.140
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: I'd like to address my first few questions, Mr. Chair, to Secretary Garin.

asr-000639
00:59:20.840 --> 00:59:23.540
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: My questions relate to Solar Philippines.

asr-000640
00:59:23.760 --> 00:59:28.620
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Recently, may nakita po akong interview ninyo where nabanggit po,

asr-000641
00:59:28.620 --> 00:59:35.680
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: ninyo na ang amount ay na dapat ibabalik sa gobyerno ay umabot ng 24 billion pesos.

asr-000642
00:59:35.800 --> 00:59:37.940
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Did I get that figure correct?

asr-000643
00:59:39.220 --> 00:59:40.940
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-000644
00:59:41.600 --> 00:59:48.060
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Out of the 24 billion pesos, magkano na po ang nakuha o narecover ng ating pamahalaan?

asr-000645
00:59:52.700 --> 00:59:57.420
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The 24 billion, Mr. Chair, is composed of different things.

asr-000646
00:59:58.120 --> 01:00:00.280
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: There was a payment of 80 million

asr-000647
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:05.660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: million for training and development fee mr chair the others are for the penalties on

asr-000648
01:00:05.660 --> 01:00:11.300
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: performance bond which is for the gaya projects mr chair which are not part of the payment

asr-000649
01:00:11.300 --> 01:00:17.090
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: so how much of the 24 billion has been recovered ma'am

asr-000649-split-2
01:00:17.090 --> 01:00:17.740
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: 80 million

asr-000650
01:00:17.740 --> 01:00:32.900
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: mr chair the the issue currently is in the hands of the department of justice and uh

