02:16:35.740 --> 02:16:48.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah. From Karamuan, malapit na lang po kami doon. Actually, meron pong feasibility study na nakuha na kami na gagawa po ng tulay from Karamuan connecting Katanduanes.

asr-002292
02:16:48.760 --> 02:16:58.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And kinausap ko na po yung DPWH, yung ilalim nun. Pwede po tayo maglagay doon ng linya na. So, para hindi na submarine cable, mas mahal po yun.

asr-002293
02:16:58.260 --> 02:17:09.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, yung design na pinapagawa po namin is for the maintenance. It's a long-term plan, no? So, it's one option. I'm just telling you na yung pinakamalapit.

asr-002294
02:17:10.040 --> 02:17:11.440
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: We'll take a look at that, Mr. Chair.

asr-002295
02:17:11.440 --> 02:17:27.600
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, in addition to the schedule of the TDP, Transmission Development Plan of the NGCP, DOE also has issued a circular allowing third-party,

asr-002296
02:17:27.600 --> 02:17:28.120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: allowing third-party,

asr-002297
02:17:28.120 --> 02:17:43.520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: construction. But we have to work closely with NGCP on this. Transcos already identified three projects that they will embark on with the permission or the agreement to NGCP also with DOE.

asr-002298
02:17:44.100 --> 02:17:53.660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We'll try as much as possible makuha yung approval for, para ma-advance po, na transco na yung magpapatayo. We'll work hard on that, sir.

asr-002299
02:17:54.860 --> 02:17:57.580
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Dalawang beses na ako bumalik din dahil sa problema dyan.

asr-002300
02:17:58.120 --> 02:18:00.600
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Maybe we can find a long-term solution, sir.

asr-002301
02:18:00.600 --> 02:18:01.040
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-002302
02:18:01.040 --> 02:18:09.560
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Thank you, Madam Secretary. Alam ko naman na hindi nyo paubayan ng katanduhan. Sabi nga, pabalik-balik ka na nga roon.

asr-002303
02:18:10.040 --> 02:18:22.500
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Yun talagang problema namin. I hope itong aming tulungan ni Kung Fuente Villa na yung sa aming Princip Bridge na talagang pangarap din naman namin yun magkaroon na may tawid.

asr-002304
02:18:23.040 --> 02:18:25.060
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: So, malay mo kung sino lang pumaw na.

asr-002305
02:18:25.700 --> 02:18:27.520
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Salamat po, Mr. Chair.

asr-002306
02:18:28.120 --> 02:18:30.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Mr. Kong Leo.

asr-002307
02:18:30.880 --> 02:18:35.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Basta pag nagsalita si Kong Sharon, Kong Lagrales, maniwala po tayo.

asr-002308
02:18:37.000 --> 02:18:43.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero before I call the next interpreter, kung pwede pong magtanong rin kayo sa PNOC, pwede rin pong magsumagot.

asr-002309
02:18:44.940 --> 02:18:49.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, next interpreter, we have Congressman Presley Dessus.

asr-002310
02:18:54.600 --> 02:18:57.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sinabi mo magtatanong ako, so magtatanong na ako.

asr-002311
02:18:57.160 --> 02:18:58.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: No, in fairness, no.

asr-002312
02:19:00.040 --> 02:19:09.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Two points muna. Una, I'm very grateful, Congressman Dagoque, and I am grateful to Chairman Alvarez and Sen. Erwin Tupo.

asr-002313
02:19:09.200 --> 02:19:17.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Finally, nasa Senate na at madidiscuss na September 10 yung Lineman Workers Appreciation Day.

asr-002314
02:19:18.480 --> 02:19:21.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, maganda yan kasi we recognize them.

asr-002315
02:19:21.240 --> 02:19:25.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As you know, nauubos na yung mga lineman natin. Nagpupunta namin ng New Zealand at Australia.

asr-002316
02:19:25.920 --> 02:19:29.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, yesterday also, kinausap namin ng TESDA.

asr-002317
02:19:29.100 --> 02:19:31.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Para tuloy-tuloy na rin yung kanilang training.

asr-002318
02:19:32.140 --> 02:19:37.700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Secondly, in fairness to Chairman ng Committee on Legislative Franchise,

asr-002319
02:19:38.440 --> 02:19:43.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: basta't meron nagpasa ng mga ganyang prangkisa at may opposition, we give them time.

asr-002320
02:19:44.320 --> 02:19:49.600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But he promised next time, naprubaan din yan. Just like the other electric cooperatives.

asr-002321
02:19:50.740 --> 02:19:51.320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair? Mr. Chair?

asr-002322
02:19:52.340 --> 02:19:53.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Wala pa akong tanong sa 'yo?

asr-002323
02:19:54.060 --> 02:19:56.320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I just wanted to intervene, Mr. Chair.

asr-002324
02:19:56.360 --> 02:19:56.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, yes.

asr-002325
02:19:56.940 --> 02:19:58.940
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: For us, in the Department of Energy

asr-002326
02:19:59.100 --> 02:20:05.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And I think especially for NEA, we don't need a special day for linemen.

asr-002327
02:20:05.800 --> 02:20:08.160
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Every day is a day for linemen, sir.

asr-002328
02:20:08.260 --> 02:20:16.160
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Because not only do they build our infrastructure, but they are the first to go whenever there's a disaster.

asr-002329
02:20:16.480 --> 02:20:17.500
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mga volunteers yan.

asr-002330
02:20:17.600 --> 02:20:19.200
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: They don't have anywhere to sleep.

asr-002331
02:20:19.300 --> 02:20:22.080
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: They just follow where the broken poles are.

asr-002332
02:20:22.520 --> 02:20:23.500
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mga volunteer po yan.

asr-002333
02:20:23.620 --> 02:20:24.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pinapakain lang ng mayor.

asr-002334
02:20:24.820 --> 02:20:28.740
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But I think they really need commendation in that sense.

asr-002335
02:20:28.740 --> 02:20:32.460
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Because they are really the heroes of the energy family, sir.

asr-002336
02:20:33.080 --> 02:20:33.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Well noted.

asr-002337
02:20:34.120 --> 02:20:35.240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Chairman.

asr-002338
02:20:35.560 --> 02:20:36.700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And of course, to Secretary.

asr-002339
02:20:36.900 --> 02:20:45.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, to Secretary, when Kong Percy said a while ago, he asked you personally kung paano baaba ang kuryente.

asr-002340
02:20:45.780 --> 02:20:47.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And you said, there's a formula.

asr-002341
02:20:48.640 --> 02:20:52.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Siguro, nung 18 Congress kami, yan na inaan namin talaga hindi bumaba ba.

asr-002342
02:20:52.600 --> 02:20:54.020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Aside from the inflation rate.

asr-002343
02:20:54.020 --> 02:20:57.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, siguro this time, yun nga, yung system loss natin.

asr-002344
02:20:58.740 --> 02:21:04.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tanong ko, is it time ng generation, the gencos, should be regulated na?

asr-002345
02:21:06.810 --> 02:21:09.210
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Although we know in EPIRA, hindi.

asr-002346
02:21:09.630 --> 02:21:11.350
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Pero, it's high time, is it?

asr-002347
02:21:12.090 --> 02:21:16.850
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, I do not think that we need to regulate.

asr-002348
02:21:17.850 --> 02:21:21.390
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But we need to have safeguards, Mr. Chair.

asr-002349
02:21:21.390 --> 02:21:29.230
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: For example, once you have a COC, you have the permit, you have the permit forever.

asr-002350
02:21:29.230 --> 02:21:31.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Regardless of your performance.

asr-002351
02:21:31.410 --> 02:21:40.930
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And that's why we are issuing new policies now to have more accountability for the gencos.

asr-002352
02:21:41.070 --> 02:21:46.410
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kasi minsan, nakalista yan sa profile natin, sa energy mix natin.

asr-002353
02:21:46.830 --> 02:21:49.910
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pero, mga four months a year lang pala siya nandun.

asr-002354
02:21:50.310 --> 02:21:51.630
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And there has to be accountability.

asr-002355
02:21:52.030 --> 02:21:53.990
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Dapat siya nagahanap ng replacement power.

asr-002356
02:21:53.990 --> 02:21:57.910
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, there are things that have been missing over the years.

asr-002357
02:21:58.610 --> 02:21:58.990
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And we...

asr-002358
02:21:59.230 --> 02:22:06.010
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We need to be more strict in a sense that they have to comply with whatever is required by EPIRA,

asr-002359
02:22:06.090 --> 02:22:10.110
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: whatever is required by ERC, and the PSA or the contract they entered.

asr-002360
02:22:10.250 --> 02:22:13.350
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, papunta na kami dyan, Mr. Chair.

asr-002361
02:22:13.350 --> 02:22:26.090
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And I think if we do regulate, we might dislodge the investment appetite in that sense.

asr-002362
02:22:26.710 --> 02:22:29.130
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pero, kailangan talaga medyo may mga regulator.

asr-002363
02:22:29.230 --> 02:22:30.170
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sorry, powers tayo.

asr-002364
02:22:30.910 --> 02:22:32.670
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002365
02:22:32.750 --> 02:22:38.390
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Of course, when Congressman Jokno asked about this solar para sa bayan,

asr-002366
02:22:39.570 --> 02:22:42.570
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: noong 18th Congress, di pa kami congressman ni Kogdagi.

asr-002367
02:22:42.730 --> 02:22:44.990
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kami ang nagra-rally na huwag pagbigyan yan.

asr-002368
02:22:45.690 --> 02:22:46.790
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi alam namin mangyayari.

asr-002369
02:22:46.910 --> 02:22:49.350
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Look what happened to Occidental Mindoro.

asr-002370
02:22:49.650 --> 02:22:51.210
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kawain lang nilagay nilang poste.

asr-002371
02:22:51.550 --> 02:22:56.430
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, when you said, you know, balitan-balitan, 24 billion nilang ano.

asr-002372
02:22:58.070 --> 02:22:59.210
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I think hindi yun ang problem.

asr-002373
02:22:59.230 --> 02:23:05.670
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ang problema dun, did they deliver what is stated in their service contract na magdi-deliver siya ng supply?

asr-002374
02:23:08.260 --> 02:23:13.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: You're correct, Mr. Chair, in a sense that because of, how many megawatts yun?

asr-002375
02:23:15.700 --> 02:23:18.040
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: These are about 33 contracts.

asr-002376
02:23:18.940 --> 02:23:20.580
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Most of it under GAYA.

asr-002377
02:23:21.300 --> 02:23:26.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And had those, it's about 1.3 gigawatts.

asr-002378
02:23:26.460 --> 02:23:29.340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Had those 1.3 gigawatts been delivered,

asr-002379
02:23:29.340 --> 02:23:35.740
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: according to our simulation, there would have been a decrease in the price, about 2 pesos ba?

asr-002380
02:23:36.520 --> 02:23:37.460
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: 1 peso.

asr-002381
02:23:37.700 --> 02:23:41.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: 1 peso at the very least on the generation rate natin, sir.

asr-002382
02:23:42.220 --> 02:23:49.120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, that's, it's not the penalty itself, but it's the cost to our consumers na nangyari.

asr-002383
02:23:49.280 --> 02:23:52.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: See, that's the problem, Chairman, because you gave the service contract.

asr-002384
02:23:52.560 --> 02:23:56.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, walang pwedeng umago dun until such time na mag-deliver sila ng ano.

asr-002385
02:23:56.540 --> 02:23:59.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, do you see?

asr-002386
02:23:59.100 --> 02:24:04.700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In the foreseeable future, magkakaroon kayo ng cancellation of service contracts na hindi pa na-umpisan?

asr-002387
02:24:05.400 --> 02:24:11.480
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, all the contracts we are being reviewed, we're cleaning it up.

asr-002388
02:24:11.480 --> 02:24:16.680
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We have cancelled so far about 100 plus, 200 contracts already.

asr-002389
02:24:17.240 --> 02:24:19.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That's for the service contracts on renewable energy.

asr-002390
02:24:20.020 --> 02:24:27.320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yung hindi gumagalaw, yung wall, late na siya, or wala siyang, ano tawag dito?

asr-002391
02:24:28.020 --> 02:24:29.080
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Hindi siya may-aral.

asr-002392
02:24:29.100 --> 02:24:29.680
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Hindi siya may-aral ng lote.

asr-002393
02:24:29.800 --> 02:24:31.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Wala siyang tenorial, ano?

asr-002394
02:24:31.680 --> 02:24:32.520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Posesory, right.

asr-002395
02:24:33.180 --> 02:24:35.520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we're cancelling, starting to cancel that.

asr-002396
02:24:35.960 --> 02:24:43.700
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And then, on the, and then next is we issue the GENCO accountability na kailangan may warning naman.

asr-002397
02:24:43.940 --> 02:24:48.160
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pag hindi ka mag-comply ng requirements ng DOE or ERC, strike 1 ka.

asr-002398
02:24:48.540 --> 02:24:56.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Next strike, up to strike 3 ka, we can cancel the COE or blacklist you.

asr-002399
02:24:56.560 --> 02:24:58.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we are trying to have more discipline.

asr-002400
02:24:59.100 --> 02:25:02.200
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: In the generation companies, Mr. Chair.

asr-002401
02:25:03.000 --> 02:25:04.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002402
02:25:04.480 --> 02:25:05.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, maybe in the second round.

asr-002403
02:25:06.420 --> 02:25:08.460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sa ERC, kay Commissioner, no?

asr-002404
02:25:09.160 --> 02:25:14.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As you know, balitang-balita sa besides, you mentioned it's also a while ago na yellow-red alert na naman tayo.

asr-002405
02:25:15.580 --> 02:25:18.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, what happened sa mga plantang sarado doon?

asr-002406
02:25:19.320 --> 02:25:20.440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And how many of them?

asr-002407
02:25:27.120 --> 02:25:27.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yan siya.

asr-002408
02:25:32.560 --> 02:25:33.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

asr-002409
02:25:33.680 --> 02:25:35.400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: If our director for...

asr-002410
02:25:36.400 --> 02:25:37.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ano?

asr-002411
02:25:38.520 --> 02:25:39.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ERC?

asr-002412
02:25:39.400 --> 02:25:49.080
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Ang mga naka-outage po sa Visayas lalo na would include the Therma Visayas at yung PEDC.

asr-002413
02:25:49.600 --> 02:26:01.560
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: But, nag-announce naman ang TVI na it will be resuming operations September 15 at yung Unit 2 na-restore noong August 31.

asr-002414
02:26:02.560 --> 02:26:10.130
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, bukod dito, may mga naka-outage pa ring mga ibang maliliit na planta and tuloy-tuloy.

asr-002415
02:26:10.130 --> 02:26:13.450
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And we will check on the status po of these plants.

asr-002416
02:26:14.730 --> 02:26:19.470
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Alam mo kung ilang planta and how many megawatts na hindi sila nakapag-deliver?

asr-002417
02:26:22.060 --> 02:26:23.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: A big thing.

asr-002418
02:26:27.320 --> 02:26:28.040
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Let me see.

asr-002419
02:26:28.600 --> 02:26:31.840
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Yung each unit of TVI is 176.

asr-002420
02:26:31.940 --> 02:26:32.720
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, dalawa sila.

asr-002421
02:26:32.720 --> 02:26:41.200
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Kaya, nung ngayong naka-outage sila, medyo malaki talaga yung nawawala sa available supplies sa Visayas lalo na.

asr-002422
02:26:41.560 --> 02:26:43.720
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: That's why we are seeing the yellow...

asr-002423
02:26:44.000 --> 02:26:46.020
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: red alerts in the region.

asr-002424
02:26:48.100 --> 02:26:51.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Alam mo, dito tayo naintindihan natin line rental eh.

asr-002425
02:26:51.400 --> 02:26:52.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can you explain yung layman's term?

asr-002426
02:26:53.780 --> 02:26:56.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: You suspended August 16 yung line rental, di ba?

asr-002427
02:26:59.260 --> 02:27:00.700
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Yes po, Mr. Chair.

asr-002428
02:27:00.780 --> 02:27:07.300
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: During periods where the interconnection is congested, Visayas and Mindanao,

asr-002429
02:27:09.860 --> 02:27:13.360
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: dahil doon natin nakikita nagkakaroon ng spike sa line rental,

asr-002430
02:27:14.000 --> 02:27:18.600
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: we asked IMOP to suspend the calculation and collection of the line rental

asr-002431
02:27:18.600 --> 02:27:23.180
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and then just collect the necessary amounts from the customers

asr-002432
02:27:23.180 --> 02:27:25.480
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: para mabayaran yung mga generators.

asr-002433
02:27:25.480 --> 02:27:32.940
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: But as a long-term solution, there is something to be done doon sa data

asr-002434
02:27:32.940 --> 02:27:43.480
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: that will be inputted in the CRSS so that the correct allocation of NSS surplus

asr-002435
02:27:44.000 --> 02:27:47.140
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: to the customers will be done.

asr-002436
02:27:47.880 --> 02:27:55.540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And we also ask IMOP to recalculate, to cost the audit through a third party

asr-002437
02:27:55.540 --> 02:28:04.040
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: of the payments or the NSS allocations made over the period from 2021

asr-002438
02:28:04.040 --> 02:28:11.540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: so that we can determine if there will be a need to order some refunds

asr-002439
02:28:12.140 --> 02:28:13.540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: in favor of...

asr-002440
02:28:14.000 --> 02:28:18.720
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: some distribution utilities who should have received a higher percentage

asr-002441
02:28:18.720 --> 02:28:22.020
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: or higher allocation of the NSS.

asr-002442
02:28:22.920 --> 02:28:23.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you.

asr-002443
02:28:23.600 --> 02:28:24.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I'll just come back with you.

asr-002444
02:28:25.400 --> 02:28:29.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, to Secretary, you know the ER-194 natin, di ba?

asr-002445
02:28:30.320 --> 02:28:32.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: You know how much you have right now?

asr-002446
02:28:32.480 --> 02:28:32.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kung kano?

asr-002447
02:28:34.680 --> 02:28:36.940
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's one centavo per...

asr-002448
02:28:36.940 --> 02:28:37.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I know.

asr-002449
02:28:37.260 --> 02:28:37.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How much in total?

asr-002450
02:28:38.440 --> 02:28:39.240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In totality?

asr-002451
02:28:44.870 --> 02:28:48.010
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Nangyayari kasi, Chair, it's directly remitted.

asr-002452
02:28:48.010 --> 02:28:48.110
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Pwede.

asr-002453
02:28:48.310 --> 02:28:50.150
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So hindi na kami humahawak ng pera.

asr-002454
02:28:50.250 --> 02:28:51.290
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We just issued a...

asr-002455
02:28:51.290 --> 02:28:52.610
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Wala sa inyo yung...

asr-002456
02:28:52.610 --> 02:28:53.650
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Wala sa amin yung pera.

asr-002457
02:28:53.670 --> 02:28:54.910
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kansi kanina, pupunta nga inyo.

asr-002458
02:28:54.950 --> 02:28:56.750
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Nag-i-diretso sa...

asr-002459
02:28:56.750 --> 02:28:57.430
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Host communities.

asr-002460
02:28:57.730 --> 02:28:59.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Host communities, yes.

asr-002461
02:28:59.330 --> 02:29:01.690
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, but before the pandemic,

asr-002462
02:29:06.020 --> 02:29:09.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I think sa policy nyo, si kayo pa rin na tumatanggap.

asr-002463
02:29:09.840 --> 02:29:12.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Because the host community, meron din silang percentage

asr-002464
02:29:12.500 --> 02:29:14.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and then binibigyan sila.

asr-002465
02:29:14.480 --> 02:29:18.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So I think it's under DOE pa rin yung pera.

asr-002467
02:29:20.060 --> 02:29:22.960
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I'll have Yusek Mario answer this, Mr. Chair.

asr-002468
02:29:23.240 --> 02:29:23.800
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Yusek Mario.

asr-002469
02:29:24.760 --> 02:29:26.400
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-002470
02:29:26.660 --> 02:29:29.900
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Thank you very much also to our beloved congressman.

asr-002471
02:29:31.480 --> 02:29:33.520
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: We do audit the releases

asr-002472
02:29:33.520 --> 02:29:36.540
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: because these are directly remitted

asr-002473
02:29:36.540 --> 02:29:39.560
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: benefits to host communities.

asr-002474
02:29:39.900 --> 02:29:42.080
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: And based on the...

asr-002475
02:29:42.080 --> 02:29:47.960
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Based on the audit and monitoring records of our auditing unit,

asr-002476
02:29:47.960 --> 02:29:51.940
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: as of June 20, 2026,

asr-002478
02:29:51.940 --> 02:29:56.560
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: we have remitted for Northern Luzon

asr-002479
02:29:56.560 --> 02:29:58.700
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: 1.8 billion.

asr-002480
02:29:59.320 --> 02:29:59.980
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: That's the total.

asr-002481
02:30:00.000 --> 02:30:18.460
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: total, with electrification at 762 million, development fund at 524 million, and watershed

asr-002482
02:30:18.460 --> 02:30:22.760
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: rural health at 526 million.

asr-002483
02:30:22.760 --> 02:30:29.380
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: For the national capital region, we have 8 million total benefits, with electrification

asr-002484
02:30:29.380 --> 02:30:40.700
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: at 4.5 million, 2 million for DLF, and for water management at almost 2 million.

asr-002485
02:30:40.700 --> 02:30:44.400
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: So we have the record here based only on audits.

asr-002486
02:30:44.400 --> 02:30:45.400
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: So these are post-remittance.

asr-002487
02:30:45.400 --> 02:30:46.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can you submit that to this committee, please?

asr-002488
02:30:46.400 --> 02:30:47.400
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Yes, we will, Mr. Chair.

asr-002489
02:30:47.400 --> 02:30:48.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002490
02:30:49.000 --> 02:30:51.270
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Yes, we will, Mr. Chair.

asr-002491
02:30:51.280 --> 02:30:51.480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002492
02:30:51.480 --> 02:30:53.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tama yan kasi importante ito eh.

asr-002493
02:30:53.640 --> 02:30:56.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Dapat talaga nakikinabang dito yung rural areas.

asr-002494
02:30:56.860 --> 02:31:00.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, [unclear] pala kayo sa NCR?

asr-002499
02:31:01.180 --> 02:31:14.300
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Yes, our new guidelines on the benefits for host communities includes urban cities. So, it's not only NCR but also those that are urbanized cities.

asr-002500
02:31:14.300 --> 02:31:16.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay, thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002501
02:31:16.440 --> 02:31:17.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Balik na lang ako.

asr-002502
02:31:17.100 --> 02:31:19.900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And then to, of course, sa TransCo, no?

asr-002503
02:31:20.980 --> 02:31:29.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kay Atty. Mr. President, yung right of way natin, ilan pa bang hindi n'yo hanggang ngayon pending pa rin na hindi n'yo nababayaran?

asr-002504
02:31:30.720 --> 02:31:33.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi moving forward, since NGCP sila na ang magbabayad, 'di ba?

asr-002505
02:31:34.920 --> 02:31:36.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yung sa inyo pang pending, ilan pa 'yun?

asr-002506
02:31:37.840 --> 02:31:41.160
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Roughly around 160,000 claims pa po 'yun.

asr-002507
02:31:41.980 --> 02:31:43.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 160,000 claims?

asr-002508
02:31:44.040 --> 02:31:44.320
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Yes.

asr-002509
02:31:44.440 --> 02:31:49.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tapos kapag may naniningil, si PSALM, [unclear] kayong pera, 'di ba?

asr-002510
02:31:49.060 --> 02:31:53.020
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Most of our concession fees go to the payment of this right of way.

asr-002511
02:31:53.160 --> 02:31:56.600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, how come hanggang ngayon hindi na-resolve yung kaso niyan? Napakarami.

asr-002512
02:31:56.820 --> 02:32:03.500
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Opo. Well, different reasons. Difficulty of settling the claims.

asr-002513
02:32:03.780 --> 02:32:05.900
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Marami po, siyempre, mas gusto mas mataas ang compensation.

asr-002514
02:32:07.280 --> 02:32:09.060
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: And then, of course, the process in court.

asr-002515
02:32:09.760 --> 02:32:12.840
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: However, we have a program now that we will begin.

asr-002516
02:32:13.220 --> 02:32:15.680
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: I-outsource po namin nationwide yung ROW settlement.

asr-002517
02:32:15.680 --> 02:32:19.040
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: We have a target to clean out all of these claims

asr-002518
02:32:19.060 --> 02:32:23.300
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: by 2034 before the concession agreement with the NGCP ends.

asr-002519
02:32:24.020 --> 02:32:28.740
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: So, we begin with a 50,000-claim target in two years po

asr-002520
02:32:28.940 --> 02:32:32.580
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: with this nationwide outsourcing of ROW settlement.

asr-002521
02:32:33.140 --> 02:32:35.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, it came to my attention also, right?

asr-002522
02:32:36.180 --> 02:32:40.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: yung iba, yung dinaanan ng linya, actually hindi naman daw siya nagke-claim.

asr-002523
02:32:40.280 --> 02:32:41.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Parang may lumalapit na taga-loob,

asr-002524
02:32:42.240 --> 02:32:46.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: sinasabi na mag-claim kayo kasi nadaanan ng transmission line.

asr-002525
02:32:46.640 --> 02:32:49.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, have you encountered this?

asr-002526
02:32:49.060 --> 02:32:51.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: May mga ilan po?

asr-002527
02:32:51.060 --> 02:32:55.260
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Yes, we've received some complaints, but we're already handling that.

asr-002528
02:32:55.260 --> 02:32:58.700
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Kaya nga po nagkaroon po ng reporma with our processes.

asr-002529
02:32:58.700 --> 02:33:02.500
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: We will now do only court processes.

asr-002530
02:33:02.500 --> 02:33:08.000
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Wala na po 'yung negotiated or out-of-court so that we can avoid these possible abuses.

asr-002531
02:33:08.000 --> 02:33:10.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah. Thank you. Thank you, [unclear].

asr-002532
02:33:10.000 --> 02:33:14.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, the 160,000 claimants, so in the next two years, it will go down?

asr-002533
02:33:14.820 --> 02:33:19.020
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: We plan to reduce it easily by 50,000 with this outsourcing program po.

asr-002534
02:33:19.060 --> 02:33:29.660
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: So, hire a lot of lawyers, real estate brokers nationwide so that we can validate and settle these claims and, of course, file the necessary court cases.

asr-002535
02:33:29.660 --> 02:33:34.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Those 160,000 claimants, how much in totality when it comes to pesos?

asr-002536
02:33:34.060 --> 02:33:41.060
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Yun pong nga 'yan, there's a new program din po. We will not pay for unregistered land kasi public land na po 'yun.

asr-002537
02:33:41.060 --> 02:33:45.060
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: So, there's a total of 220 billion po yung cost na 'yan.

asr-002538
02:33:45.060 --> 02:33:48.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, kailangan pa ng 220 billion?

asr-002539
02:33:48.060 --> 02:33:48.560
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Yes.

asr-002540
02:33:48.560 --> 02:33:49.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes.

asr-002541
02:33:49.060 --> 02:33:50.560
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: To pay all those claimants.

asr-002542
02:33:50.560 --> 02:33:52.560
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Well, of course, that's an estimate.

asr-002543
02:33:52.560 --> 02:33:55.560
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: That's according to a 2016 zonal valuation po.

asr-002544
02:33:55.560 --> 02:33:57.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah, 2026 na 'yun.

asr-002545
02:33:57.060 --> 02:34:00.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, sige, sigurado tataas ako.

asr-002546
02:34:00.060 --> 02:34:03.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And I don't think PISAM has that much money.

asr-002547
02:34:03.060 --> 02:34:04.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Wala na kayo, no?

asr-002548
02:34:04.060 --> 02:34:05.060
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: No.

asr-002549
02:34:05.060 --> 02:34:06.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: PSALM?

asr-002550
02:34:06.060 --> 02:34:07.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Chair.

asr-002551
02:34:07.060 --> 02:34:08.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kindly wind up.

asr-002552
02:34:08.060 --> 02:34:11.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, sige lang.

asr-002553
02:34:13.060 --> 02:34:14.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ay, hindi, hindi, hindi.

asr-002554
02:34:14.060 --> 02:34:15.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Tumatakbo.

asr-002555
02:34:15.060 --> 02:34:16.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ikaw pa.

asr-002556
02:34:16.060 --> 02:34:17.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Gusto mo.

asr-002557
02:34:17.060 --> 02:34:18.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Second round, third round, fourth round.

asr-002558
02:34:18.560 --> 02:34:19.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Fifth round.

asr-002559
02:34:19.560 --> 02:34:20.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Twenty-seven.

asr-002560
02:34:20.580 --> 02:34:22.280
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: So, Mr. Chair, correct.

asr-002561
02:34:23.600 --> 02:34:28.340
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: Our funding sources is, if not borrowings, is also from our direct revenue, sir.

asr-002562
02:34:28.380 --> 02:34:32.440
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: And part of our responsibility is to fund the transmission requirements of Transco.

asr-002563
02:34:33.460 --> 02:34:38.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, how many more pending na owned by Gencos na pag-aari ng gobyerno natin?

asr-002564
02:34:38.560 --> 02:34:45.940
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: For PSALM, sir, we have three more assets: Agus Pulangi, Mindanao Coal, and the

asr-002565
02:34:45.940 --> 02:34:46.940
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: Bakun Hydro Power Plant.

asr-002566
02:34:46.940 --> 02:34:47.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sige,

asr-002567
02:34:47.940 --> 02:34:48.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: most of the time, talagang binibenta n'yo,

asr-002568
02:34:48.940 --> 02:34:49.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: including Agus Pulangi,

asr-002569
02:34:49.940 --> 02:34:50.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: [unclear] n'yo o sineparate n'yo rin sila?

asr-002570
02:34:50.940 --> 02:34:51.940
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: Agus Pulangi is not for sale, Mr. Chair.

asr-002571
02:34:51.940 --> 02:34:52.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay,

asr-002572
02:34:52.940 --> 02:34:53.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: thank you.

asr-002573
02:34:58.120 --> 02:34:59.600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Of course, to my friend,

asr-002574
02:34:59.780 --> 02:35:00.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: sabi mo nga,

asr-002575
02:35:00.960 --> 02:35:04.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: pag tinanong ko si Coco, laging sagot na ito, laging totoo eh.

asr-002576
02:35:04.500 --> 02:35:12.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sa UCME, how many nag-apply sa inyo ng mga pending co-ops para sa kanilang subsidy?

asr-002577
02:35:15.600 --> 02:35:25.380
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Mr. Chair, Honorable De Jesus, wala po kaming pending applications. Meron, they're all applied na po.

asr-002578
02:35:25.420 --> 02:35:27.840
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: So they're applied, pero lahat sila napagbigyan n'yo o hindi?

asr-002598
02:35:29.440 --> 02:35:51.280
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Nabibigyan po namin yung mga UCME allocations as far as the funds collected can accommodate. Para po ma-isagot ko ng tama, yung wala pong increase ng UCME rate since last year.

asr-002599
02:35:51.460 --> 02:36:09.760
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: So ibig sabihin po, lumaki po yung cost to generate electricity at paglaki ng cost to generate electricity, mas kakaunti yung kayang mabayaran ng cash na nakokolek para sa UCME.

asr-002600
02:36:10.440 --> 02:36:25.120
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: So kung dati-dati, kung dalawang buwan yung revolving fund, ngayon kailangan anim na buwan na yung revolving fund para continuous po yung operation.

asr-002601
02:36:25.120 --> 02:36:36.360
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Ito po ay dulot sa panawagan na hindi natin bigla-biglain ang pag-pass on ng mga ito.

asr-002602
02:36:36.960 --> 02:36:40.880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So in short, yung budget mo last year and

asr-002603
02:36:40.880 --> 02:36:43.520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 2026-2027, almost the same?

asr-002604
02:36:44.740 --> 02:36:53.420
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Sa UCME po, yung nako-collect po sa grid consumers ay pareho lang po.

asr-002605
02:36:53.420 --> 02:37:02.940
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Pero pagdating sa budget ng NAPOCOR itself, which is not part of the UCME naman, so meron pong konting increase.

asr-002606
02:37:03.060 --> 02:37:05.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: You have three seconds, so last question, sir.

asr-002607
02:37:05.360 --> 02:37:07.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kay Chikuy sana, kaso three seconds lang.

asr-002608
02:37:07.800 --> 02:37:09.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002609
02:37:09.880 --> 02:37:11.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: May natira ko at least may natira akong three seconds.

asr-002610
02:37:12.020 --> 02:37:13.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Akong kay Chikuy? I will allow it.

asr-002611
02:37:13.860 --> 02:37:15.240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ayun, then I'll give you a job.

asr-002612
02:37:16.260 --> 02:37:16.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Go ahead.

asr-002613
02:37:17.180 --> 02:37:17.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002614
02:37:18.160 --> 02:37:18.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

asr-002615
02:37:20.780 --> 02:37:23.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Next to interpelate, Congressman Mark Cojuangco.

asr-002616
02:37:23.660 --> 02:37:24.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sir, you have the floor.

asr-002617
02:37:25.580 --> 02:37:28.020
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002618
02:37:29.060 --> 02:37:34.840
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: My question is for the DOE regarding all the solar projects.

asr-002619
02:37:34.840 --> 02:37:34.940
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Yes.

asr-002620
02:37:36.040 --> 02:37:39.860
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Dung po sa distrito ko, sa bayan ng Bugalyon,

asr-002621
02:37:39.880 --> 02:37:47.020
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: at Aguilar, matindi po ang kalawakan ng solar projects po doon.

asr-002622
02:37:47.960 --> 02:37:55.280
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Ginawa po yan sa hillsides at itong matinding pagdating ng tagulan,

asr-002623
02:37:56.540 --> 02:38:07.900
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: ang lahat ng putik po ay bumaba sa mga bundok at nagbara sa mga creeks at rivers ng bayan.

asr-002624
02:38:07.900 --> 02:38:08.900
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Unprecedented.

asr-002625
02:38:09.880 --> 02:38:13.480
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Pwede ba po ang pagbabaha ng poblasyon ng Bugalyon?

asr-002626
02:38:14.520 --> 02:38:24.720
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Pwede ba pong malaman kung ang DOE o ang DNR ang magahanap po ng solusyon sa problema nito?

asr-002627
02:38:26.540 --> 02:38:37.960
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, I'll pass on the mic to Yusef Guevara on the process, but we will have our Bureau

asr-002628
02:38:37.960 --> 02:38:39.860
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: of the Renewable Energy Management.

asr-002629
02:38:39.920 --> 02:38:42.480
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: he will have our Bureau of the Environment Bureau to check on this.

asr-002630
02:38:42.480 --> 02:38:44.140
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's beyond the...

asr-002631
02:38:44.380 --> 02:38:53.020
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's beyond the mandate of DOE, but we can, if there's any violation, we can reprimand

asr-002632
02:38:53.020 --> 02:38:56.780
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: or take action on the GENCO itself under permit.

asr-002633
02:38:57.140 --> 02:38:57.940
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yusef Guevara, please.

asr-002634
02:38:57.940 --> 02:39:06.300
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Kasi po, Mr. Chairman, ang DOE ang nagtulak nito, itong mga project na to.

asr-002635
02:39:06.300 --> 02:39:07.280
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: They're the ones who imposed the DOE.

asr-002636
02:39:07.280 --> 02:39:08.880
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: At sila po ang nagsasabi na...

asr-002637
02:39:08.880 --> 02:39:09.440
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: They're the ones who are saying you should not do this.

asr-002638
02:39:09.440 --> 02:39:09.680
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: They're the ones who are saying you should not do this.

asr-002639
02:39:09.680 --> 02:39:20.400
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Dapat mag-50% solar and wind ang ating generating capacity by next year.

asr-002640
02:39:21.680 --> 02:39:30.300
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: So, sa palagay ko po, may konti silang pananagutan sa mga problema ang idinudulot po nito.

asr-002641
02:39:31.420 --> 02:39:35.480
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: So, ulitin ko po, paano po ang LGU?

asr-002642
02:39:35.480 --> 02:39:49.180
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: So, tignan niyo po, i-check niyo po sa BSWD, record po ang pagbigay ng relief ngayon sa bayan ng Bugalyon.

asr-002643
02:39:51.360 --> 02:39:53.280
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Yusek Guevara, please.

asr-002644
02:39:53.620 --> 02:39:55.400
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Mr. Chair, magandang hapon po.

asr-002645
02:39:56.360 --> 02:40:00.180
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Yung pong binanggit ninyo na pagbaha po sa inyong lugar,

asr-002646
02:40:01.080 --> 02:40:04.160
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: at titingnan po namin yung mga hydrological studies.

asr-002647
02:40:04.160 --> 02:40:06.160
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Kasi po, bago magtayo ng planta,

asr-002648
02:40:07.020 --> 02:40:10.100
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: itong mga solar plants and any other kind of plants,

asr-002649
02:40:10.600 --> 02:40:13.140
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: iba't-ibang klaseng studies po ang ginagawa nila.

asr-002650
02:40:13.740 --> 02:40:15.400
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Sa kaso po na binanggit ninyo,

asr-002651
02:40:15.840 --> 02:40:18.300
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: kailangan ma-tingnan yung hydrological studies.

asr-002652
02:40:18.720 --> 02:40:24.080
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Malaman kung dahil sa pagtatayo nila ng mga solar power plant na yan,

asr-002653
02:40:24.540 --> 02:40:27.480
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: ina-divert ba yung tubig at nag-cost po ng baha.

asr-002654
02:40:28.040 --> 02:40:34.080
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Gagawin po namin niya ang pagtatanong na yan dun sa mismong power supply generator po.

asr-002655
02:40:34.080 --> 02:40:35.860
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: When can you commit to do that, ma'am?

asr-002656
02:40:37.020 --> 02:40:39.020
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Pagkatanong po namin kaagad sila.

asr-002657
02:40:39.020 --> 02:40:42.020
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Next week po tatanungin na namin and then we will report back to you.

asr-002658
02:40:42.020 --> 02:40:43.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you very much.

asr-002659
02:40:43.020 --> 02:40:46.020
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Hindi po nasasagot ang aking katanungan.

asr-002660
02:40:46.020 --> 02:40:52.020
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Sino po ang sasagot sa lahat po ng remedial works na kailangan

asr-002661
02:40:52.020 --> 02:41:02.020
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: sa pagtanggal ng putik ng mga ilog at mga creek na nagbarana sa bayan ng Bugalyon?

asr-002662
02:41:03.020 --> 02:41:06.600
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Mr. Chair, iticheck po natin kung ang generator or ang developer,

asr-002663
02:41:06.600 --> 02:41:09.600
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: ang may kasalanan, siya po dapat ang sumagot.

asr-002664
02:41:09.600 --> 02:41:12.600
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: At i-co-coordinate po namin ito dun sa local government unit po.

asr-002665
02:41:12.600 --> 02:41:14.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And I think DPWH, ma'am.

asr-002666
02:41:14.600 --> 02:41:15.600
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: And DPWH, of course.

asr-002667
02:41:15.600 --> 02:41:16.600
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Thank you.

asr-002668
02:41:16.600 --> 02:41:25.600
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Mr. Chairman, punta po tayo sa issue ng TransCo at NGCP.

asr-002669
02:41:25.600 --> 02:41:34.600
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Itong chairman po ay ng Nuclear Energy Committee ay gustong malaman kung alo ba po

asr-002670
02:41:34.600 --> 02:41:40.600
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: ang naging issue between TransCo and NGCP.

asr-002671
02:41:40.600 --> 02:41:56.600
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Hila iyong karapatan ng NGCP ay unilaterally diniside ng sekretary ng DOE na bawiin.

asr-002672
02:41:56.600 --> 02:42:01.600
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Ano ba po ang totoong storya nito?

asr-002673
02:42:01.600 --> 02:42:03.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Before you answer TransCo, no?

asr-002674
02:42:04.600 --> 02:42:08.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I'd like to inform lang kung markuhan ko na only TransCo is here.

asr-002675
02:42:08.600 --> 02:42:10.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Wala po yung NGCP dito.

asr-002676
02:42:10.600 --> 02:42:11.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sir?

asr-002677
02:42:11.600 --> 02:42:20.060
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Mr. Chair, ano pong particular right na was taken away from NGCP?

asr-002678
02:42:20.060 --> 02:42:25.660
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Tinatanong ko po sa inyo. Ano ba po iyon?

asr-002679
02:42:25.660 --> 02:42:32.660
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: To our knowledge, Mr. Chair, we continue to respect the concession agreement.

asr-002680
02:42:32.660 --> 02:42:37.660
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Wala po kaming tinatanggal o binabawi among the obligations and rights of NGCP.

asr-002681
02:42:38.660 --> 02:42:46.660
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: If you are referring to an arbitral case, that was decided po noong February 2025.

asr-002682
02:42:46.660 --> 02:42:51.660
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: At nakumpirma naman po ang mga posisyon ng NGCP in that arbitration case.

asr-002683
02:42:51.660 --> 02:42:56.660
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: And some matters also confirms the position of TransCo and the government.

asr-002684
02:42:56.660 --> 02:43:02.660
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: So, we are implementing that arbitral ruling kasi napagdesisyonan naman po yun ng arbitration court.

asr-002685
02:43:02.660 --> 02:43:07.660
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Mr. Chairman, this representation would like to request that,

asr-002686
02:43:07.660 --> 02:43:15.660
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: DOE and TransCo write an explanation to the committee.

asr-002687
02:43:15.660 --> 02:43:21.660
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Copy-furnish this representation on these matters.

asr-002688
02:43:21.660 --> 02:43:25.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Madam Secretary.

asr-002689
02:43:25.660 --> 02:43:26.660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-002690
02:43:26.660 --> 02:43:27.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: You are directed to…

asr-002691
02:43:27.660 --> 02:43:28.660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, we will comply.

asr-002692
02:43:28.660 --> 02:43:29.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

asr-002693
02:43:29.660 --> 02:43:32.660
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Mr. Chairman, last point.

asr-002694
02:43:32.660 --> 02:43:38.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Alam niyo hindi ko po maintindihan kung bakit…

asr-002695
02:43:38.390 --> 02:43:55.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Itinatago ng DOE ang risulta ng feasibility study na ginawa ng KHNP regarding the PNPP Unit 1 Nuclear Power Plant.

asr-002696
02:43:55.390 --> 02:44:01.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Matagal na po hinihingi nitong representation.

asr-002697
02:44:01.390 --> 02:44:06.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: In fact, ako po ang nag-instigate nito.

asr-002698
02:44:06.390 --> 02:44:07.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Three years ago.

asr-002699
02:44:07.390 --> 02:44:09.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Three years ago.

asr-002700
02:44:09.390 --> 02:44:12.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: With KHMP.

asr-002701
02:44:12.390 --> 02:44:21.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Bakit ayaw po bigyan ang Committee of Nuclear Energy ng kopya ng feasibility study

asr-002702
02:44:21.390 --> 02:44:31.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: when it is a key information piece regarding legislation being crafted at the moment.

asr-002703
02:44:31.390 --> 02:44:35.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: House Bill 08567.

asr-002704
02:44:35.390 --> 02:44:53.390
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: It needs the information to make intelligent policy decisions regarding the disposition of PNPP 1 and subsequent nuclear power plants in the country.

asr-002705
02:44:53.390 --> 02:44:58.500
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Noong last committee meeting po namin sa

asr-002710
02:44:58.500 --> 02:45:11.760
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Committee on Nuclear Energy, may nag-motion po na mag-issue ang committee ng subpoena

asr-002711
02:45:11.760 --> 02:45:20.740
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: demanding the production by the DOE of said feasibility study.

asr-002712
02:45:20.740 --> 02:45:29.880
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: The House was divided. The vote to have a subpoena prevailed.

asr-002713
02:45:31.700 --> 02:45:46.120
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: I have here a copy of a fully signed up to the Secretary General of a subpoena.

asr-002714
02:45:47.120 --> 02:45:50.120
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: However, since...

asr-002715
02:45:50.740 --> 02:45:58.660
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: there have been parties at DOE who have promised to produce these studies,

asr-002716
02:45:59.340 --> 02:46:11.520
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: the Speaker has decided to intervene in the interest of preserving cooperation between the Legislature and the Executive.

asr-002717
02:46:11.960 --> 02:46:20.520
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: So he has ordered the Secretary General and the Sergeant-at-Arms to not serve.

asr-002718
02:46:20.740 --> 02:46:28.540
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: I am submitting a copy of this subpoena to the committee, to you, Mr. Chairman,

asr-002719
02:46:28.960 --> 02:46:33.440
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: so that you know that this in fact happened.

asr-002720
02:46:34.460 --> 02:46:41.840
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: We would like to receive a copy of the feasibility study at the soonest possible time.

asr-002721
02:46:42.180 --> 02:46:43.880
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Not from Korea.

asr-002722
02:46:45.140 --> 02:46:49.020
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: The copy from the DOE, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002723
02:46:49.020 --> 02:46:49.700
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Okay.

asr-002724
02:46:50.740 --> 02:46:52.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Last question. Kindly answer, Mr. Guevara.

asr-002725
02:46:53.520 --> 02:46:54.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002726
02:46:55.460 --> 02:47:01.860
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Mr. Chair, the hard copy is the only kind of copy that is issued by KHNP,

asr-002727
02:47:02.060 --> 02:47:05.720
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: and it is controlled on who is the recipient of the copy.

asr-002728
02:47:06.500 --> 02:47:11.340
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: The hard copy that will be submitted to the committee will arrive by Friday or Monday,

asr-002729
02:47:11.580 --> 02:47:14.300
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: and we will submit to the committee right away.

asr-002730
02:47:14.460 --> 02:47:15.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So wala pa po sa inyo?

asr-002731
02:47:15.980 --> 02:47:17.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Wala pa po sa amin eh.

asr-002732
02:47:17.160 --> 02:47:18.420
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: So on the way na po.

asr-002733
02:47:18.420 --> 02:47:20.660
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Sa inyo, Friday.

asr-002752
02:47:21.880 --> 02:47:23.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can you submit to this committee?

asr-002753
02:47:23.660 --> 02:47:24.600
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-002754
02:47:24.700 --> 02:47:24.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

asr-002755
02:47:25.200 --> 02:47:26.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So this Friday?

asr-002756
02:47:27.080 --> 02:47:28.620
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Friday or Monday po ang dating?

asr-002757
02:47:28.860 --> 02:47:29.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: O, ganyan mo.

asr-002758
02:47:29.520 --> 02:47:29.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Monday.

asr-002759
02:47:29.780 --> 02:47:30.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Chairman,

asr-002760
02:47:30.800 --> 02:47:31.640
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Mr. Chairman,

asr-002761
02:47:31.920 --> 02:47:35.540
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: mukhang may confusion po, no?

asr-002762
02:47:35.780 --> 02:47:37.560
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: May kopya sila ngayon.

asr-002763
02:47:40.110 --> 02:47:42.210
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Kopya nila ng DOE.

asr-002764
02:47:43.210 --> 02:47:46.950
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Bakit ayaw kaming bigyan ng kopya ng DOE?

asr-002765
02:47:47.050 --> 02:47:48.230
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can you clarify that?

asr-002766
02:47:48.390 --> 02:47:49.170
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Do you have a copy?

asr-002767
02:47:49.170 --> 02:47:51.930
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: This is a copy or certified through copy na?

asr-002768
02:47:51.930 --> 02:47:53.210
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kasi it's hard rin na,

asr-002769
02:47:53.270 --> 02:47:54.170
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I understand, ma'am.

asr-002770
02:47:54.550 --> 02:47:55.830
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It's hard na magbigay

asr-002771
02:47:55.830 --> 02:47:58.590
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: na hindi pa rin certified through copy.

asr-002772
02:47:59.670 --> 02:48:00.450
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair,

asr-002773
02:48:00.610 --> 02:48:02.630
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: it's part of the agreement with KHNP.

asr-002774
02:48:02.770 --> 02:48:04.130
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sila yung nagbibigay ng hard copy.

asr-002775
02:48:04.570 --> 02:48:06.090
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We're constrained with that.

asr-002776
02:48:06.170 --> 02:48:06.530
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: No, but,

asr-002777
02:48:07.010 --> 02:48:08.250
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: by,

asr-002778
02:48:08.530 --> 02:48:10.450
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: there's an MDE on our part.

asr-002779
02:48:10.470 --> 02:48:11.030
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The commitment is

asr-002780
02:48:11.030 --> 02:48:13.150
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: to submit to this committee by?

asr-002781
02:48:13.930 --> 02:48:14.810
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: By Monday, sir,

asr-002782
02:48:14.850 --> 02:48:16.390
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: because we have already requested

asr-002783
02:48:16.390 --> 02:48:16.590
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: a request by the...

asr-002784
02:48:16.590 --> 02:48:17.830
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, that's acceptable.

asr-002785
02:48:17.970 --> 02:48:18.310
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir.

asr-002786
02:48:18.550 --> 02:48:18.810
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes.

asr-002787
02:48:18.930 --> 02:48:20.790
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's on its way already.

asr-002788
02:48:20.790 --> 02:48:21.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Okay.

asr-002789
02:48:21.550 --> 02:48:21.790
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you.

asr-002790
02:48:21.790 --> 02:48:21.850
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you.

asr-002791
02:48:21.930 --> 02:48:22.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-002792
02:48:23.190 --> 02:48:24.570
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: I object strongly

asr-002793
02:48:24.570 --> 02:48:25.570
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: because

asr-002794
02:48:25.570 --> 02:48:28.190
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: why should we open ourselves

asr-002795
02:48:28.190 --> 02:48:29.410
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: to the possibility

asr-002796
02:48:29.410 --> 02:48:32.570
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: that Korea will send us

asr-002797
02:48:32.570 --> 02:48:33.870
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: a different copy?

asr-002798
02:48:34.790 --> 02:48:36.010
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Why can't this

asr-002799
02:48:36.010 --> 02:48:38.130
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: chairman

asr-002800
02:48:38.130 --> 02:48:39.090
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: and this

asr-002801
02:48:39.090 --> 02:48:40.950
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: nuclear energy committee

asr-002802
02:48:40.950 --> 02:48:43.710
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: get a copy

asr-002803
02:48:43.710 --> 02:48:45.030
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: of exactly

asr-002804
02:48:45.030 --> 02:48:46.690
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: what is with DOE?

asr-002805
02:48:48.270 --> 02:48:50.450
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: They have committed already

asr-002806
02:48:50.450 --> 02:48:51.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: that they will

asr-002807
02:48:51.790 --> 02:48:53.050
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: submit the copy

asr-002808
02:48:53.050 --> 02:48:54.970
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: of what you have requested.

asr-002809
02:48:55.570 --> 02:48:57.410
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: They have committed, sir,

asr-002810
02:48:57.590 --> 02:48:59.090
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: that they will submit

asr-002811
02:48:59.090 --> 02:49:01.290
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: a copy that is still

asr-002812
02:49:01.290 --> 02:49:03.150
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: arriving from Korea.

asr-002813
02:49:03.490 --> 02:49:04.850
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: That is unacceptable.

asr-002814
02:49:05.750 --> 02:49:08.790
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, but they will submit it

asr-002815
02:49:08.790 --> 02:49:10.470
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: once they get it by Monday.

asr-002816
02:49:10.590 --> 02:49:11.390
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's a few days,

asr-002817
02:49:11.590 --> 02:49:12.650
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Congressman Marco Anco.

asr-002818
02:49:13.310 --> 02:49:15.070
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I think we just have to be

asr-002819
02:49:15.070 --> 02:49:16.210
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: a little bit patient.

asr-002820
02:49:16.430 --> 02:49:16.990
Rep. Mark O. Cojuangco: Mr. Chair.

asr-002821
02:49:17.390 --> 02:49:17.990
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Suspended.

asr-002845
02:50:03.290 --> 02:50:04.410
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Do you have a copy?

asr-002846
02:50:04.670 --> 02:50:05.190
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes or no?

asr-002847
02:50:07.580 --> 02:50:08.340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-002848
02:50:09.040 --> 02:50:10.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Why can't you submit that copy?

asr-002849
02:50:11.080 --> 02:50:12.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's part of the agreement,

asr-002850
02:50:12.580 --> 02:50:12.980
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair.

asr-002851
02:50:13.000 --> 02:50:13.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Part of the agreement?

asr-002852
02:50:13.940 --> 02:50:14.320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir.

