asr-003869
03:15:27.630 --> 03:15:32.050
Rep. Jan "Atty. JP" Padiernos: Last about, with regard to the fuel issue.

asr-003870
03:15:32.050 --> 03:15:38.990
Rep. Jan "Atty. JP" Padiernos: As of April 2026, DOE reported approximately 49 days of diesel

asr-003871
03:15:38.990 --> 03:15:42.030
Rep. Jan "Atty. JP" Padiernos: and 54 days of gasoline supply.

asr-003872
03:15:42.590 --> 03:15:46.090
Rep. Jan "Atty. JP" Padiernos: But those figures largely represent overall national inventories

asr-003873
03:15:46.090 --> 03:15:49.750
Rep. Jan "Atty. JP" Padiernos: rather than necessarily government-owned strategic stocks.

asr-003874
03:15:50.670 --> 03:15:54.270
Rep. Jan "Atty. JP" Padiernos: Of the countries reported 49 days of diesel inventory,

asr-003875
03:15:54.370 --> 03:15:57.170
Rep. Jan "Atty. JP" Padiernos: how many days are actually owned or controlled by the government?

asr-003876
03:15:57.790 --> 03:16:01.850
Rep. Jan "Atty. JP" Padiernos: And where will PNOC physically store the reserve?

asr-003877
03:16:02.050 --> 03:16:08.850
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Yes, actually, the government doesn't normally buy stock, no?

asr-003878
03:16:09.390 --> 03:16:12.130
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: We did this in this time of emergency.

asr-003879
03:16:12.310 --> 03:16:15.350
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: We bought, essentially, the government's hold, the one we bought,

asr-003880
03:16:16.110 --> 03:16:18.430
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: five days of diesel stock only.

asr-003881
03:16:19.330 --> 03:16:22.670
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: And then less than a day of stock of gasoline.

asr-003882
03:16:23.770 --> 03:16:27.030
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: At the present time, the government doesn't have its own facility.

asr-003883
03:16:27.030 --> 03:16:29.630
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: We rented storage.

asr-003884
03:16:30.290 --> 03:16:32.030
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: In one of the private areas.

asr-003885
03:16:32.050 --> 03:16:33.890
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Private storage companies.

asr-003886
03:16:34.650 --> 03:16:41.490
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: And, in fact, there was a discussion about strategic petroleum reserve,

asr-003887
03:16:41.490 --> 03:16:45.270
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: which the Congress is now looking into.

asr-003888
03:16:45.530 --> 03:16:46.770
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: There are committee hearings.

asr-003889
03:16:47.010 --> 03:16:47.770
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: There are drafts.

asr-003890
03:16:48.110 --> 03:16:53.290
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Because we have seen the importance of the government role.

asr-003891
03:16:53.450 --> 03:16:55.910
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: But we have to define what is the role of the government.

asr-003892
03:16:56.430 --> 03:17:01.130
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Because we still don't want to intrude too much private enterprise.

asr-003893
03:17:01.670 --> 03:17:01.750
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Because,

asr-003894
03:17:02.050 --> 03:17:06.350
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: we need a lot of money for the negotiation of the fuel.

asr-003895
03:17:06.930 --> 03:17:13.090
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: So, we have to be strategic about where to allocate the money of the government

asr-003896
03:17:13.090 --> 03:17:17.030
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: when we establish the strategic petroleum reserve.

asr-003897
03:17:17.370 --> 03:17:17.950
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair.

asr-003898
03:17:18.190 --> 03:17:18.450
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes.

asr-003899
03:17:18.950 --> 03:17:19.950
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So that Chico can recite.

asr-003900
03:17:21.090 --> 03:17:26.570
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: He's the one embarking on the strategic reserve, on the government.

asr-003901
