asr-004334
03:43:31.010 --> 03:43:37.070
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: lane expansions, I'll make sure that it will be first among the list.

asr-004335
03:43:37.550 --> 03:43:42.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, the pole relocation funding is actually through the DPWH

asr-004336
03:43:42.890 --> 03:43:44.530
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: and we have a MOA, no?

asr-004337
03:43:44.730 --> 03:43:51.250
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: With them, na kahit na yan na yung mag-implement, basta i-refund lang yung gastos.

asr-004338
03:43:51.830 --> 03:43:55.710
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Thank you and good news siguro yun na at least ma-accelerate na natin.

asr-004339
03:43:55.710 --> 03:43:59.710
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: I will be coordinating with the office of the administrator

asr-004340
03:43:59.710 --> 03:44:00.710
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: for the...

asr-004341
03:44:01.010 --> 03:44:03.470
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: relocation of the poles.

asr-004342
03:44:04.050 --> 03:44:04.290
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: And,

asr-004343
03:44:04.390 --> 03:44:06.690
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Mr. Chair,

asr-004344
03:44:07.130 --> 03:44:10.090
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: I would also like to raise an issue also.

asr-004345
03:44:10.350 --> 03:44:16.790
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: There is one barangay na very near lang sa mainland,

asr-004346
03:44:16.790 --> 03:44:17.870
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: but however,

asr-004347
03:44:18.710 --> 03:44:21.270
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: since bagyohin yung lugar namin,

asr-004348
03:44:21.850 --> 03:44:23.970
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: parati siya napuputol yung...

asr-004349
03:44:23.970 --> 03:44:25.750
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: natutumba yung pole.

asr-004350
03:44:26.370 --> 03:44:29.850
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: So if we can request that this island,

asr-004351
03:44:29.970 --> 03:44:30.790
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: para hindi na siya nagparatay,

asr-004352
03:44:31.010 --> 03:44:32.410
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: that constantly nagba-burnout,

asr-004353
03:44:32.530 --> 03:44:37.630
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: kasi mga roughly 1.5 kilometers lang from the mainland,

asr-004354
03:44:37.830 --> 03:44:39.690
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: baka pwede natin maging submersible,

asr-004355
03:44:39.850 --> 03:44:42.910
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: is it possible po ba na may mga programa pa kayong na

asr-004356
03:44:42.910 --> 03:44:47.430
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: ma-convert natin yung pole nila into a submersible nila

asr-004357
03:44:47.430 --> 03:44:50.770
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: so that it will be more resilient sa mga typhoons?

asr-004358
03:44:50.950 --> 03:44:51.790
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir, it's possible.

asr-004359
03:44:51.930 --> 03:44:55.070
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We just need to do a cost-benefit analysis.

asr-004360
03:44:55.070 --> 03:44:59.730
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Baka naman continuing consumption tapos malaki yung investment.

asr-004361
03:45:00.000 --> 03:45:11.120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If it does not work, nalagyan natin ng submarine cables, then we can deploy a different technology in the area.

asr-004362
03:45:11.260 --> 03:45:12.480
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We'll have it checked, sir.

asr-004363
03:45:12.640 --> 03:45:16.740
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We'll talk to your team para makuha lang namin yung mga pangalan ng area, sir.

asr-004364
03:45:17.000 --> 03:45:17.340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you.

asr-004365
03:45:17.640 --> 03:45:18.740
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-004366
03:45:18.740 --> 03:45:33.260
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: And there is also a solar project in the Samalcoan that the European Union has donated, like roughly 60 million.

asr-004367
03:45:34.620 --> 03:45:43.360
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: So at least we get to enjoy na free na makatulong din siya na mababa na yung rate natin sa per kilowatt hour.

asr-004368
03:45:43.360 --> 03:45:48.220
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: But however, is it possible that we can waive the fees?

asr-004369
03:45:48.360 --> 03:45:51.360
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Kasi nagbabayad po yung Samalcoan.

asr-004370
03:45:51.880 --> 03:46:00.040
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Ako din ng roughly 100,000 a month sa mga, although kahit libre lang na binigay yung,

asr-004371
03:46:00.940 --> 03:46:06.180
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: dinonate lang yung, tawag nito, solar plant.

asr-004372
03:46:07.060 --> 03:46:10.720
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: But however, medyo nagsisingil din yung DOA.

asr-004373
03:46:10.720 --> 03:46:14.000
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Is it possible po ba na we can waive?

asr-004374
03:46:14.660 --> 03:46:18.620
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sir, we'll have NEA check muna the status of the co-op.

asr-004375
03:46:18.840 --> 03:46:20.860
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, and then we'll work on it, Mr. Chair.

asr-004376
03:46:20.940 --> 03:46:21.860
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Yeah, Mr. Chair.

asr-004377
03:46:21.880 --> 03:46:37.480
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Maybe offhand, maybe I would suppose any collection or any spending should cover the operation and maintenance of the solar plant.

asr-004378
03:46:37.560 --> 03:46:42.660
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: But we will check on it, Mr. Chair Kong, on how to go about your request.

asr-004379
03:46:42.660 --> 03:46:51.640
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Okay, and I would like also to check the status of the upgrading of the Luzon-Visayas transmission line.

asr-004380
03:46:51.880 --> 03:46:59.060
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Because malaking tulong din ito to avoid power shedding in Region 8 and probably Region 6 also.

asr-004381
03:47:00.060 --> 03:47:09.780
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Ito yung primary reason talaga na mayroon tayong MLD and mas higher na line rental.

asr-004382
03:47:10.620 --> 03:47:20.940
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: So probably the problem talaga yung NGCP that medyo ma-upgrade talaga nila yung transmission line nila the soonest possible time.

asr-004383
03:47:20.940 --> 03:47:25.520
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: But however, per plan, it will be upgraded on 2032.

asr-004384
03:47:26.200 --> 03:47:31.720
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Ano kaya yung possibility na it will be mas malapit pa, Madam?

asr-004385
03:47:31.720 --> 03:47:33.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you for the last question.

asr-004386
03:47:33.680 --> 03:47:35.900
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you for the question.

asr-004387
03:47:38.040 --> 03:47:41.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We're trying to figure out the long-term solution for this.

asr-004388
03:47:43.500 --> 03:47:48.260
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: What we are working on today, we've finished Mindoro and Palawan.

asr-004389
03:47:48.560 --> 03:47:50.840
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We are doing a master plan for Visayas.

asr-004390
03:47:50.940 --> 03:47:59.720
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The best solution for Visayas is for each island to be independent on their energy needs.

asr-004391
03:48:00.220 --> 03:48:03.960
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Dapat ang base load, kung anumang kailangan nila, nandyan sa isla mismo.

asr-004392
03:48:04.100 --> 03:48:07.740
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Hindi yung mag-i-import kapag galing Luzon or even from Cebu.

asr-004393
03:48:08.120 --> 03:48:10.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So we are doing the analysis now.

asr-004394
03:48:11.160 --> 03:48:17.500
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We're just trying to balance the cost per kilowatt as to what is needed to be constructed.

asr-004395
03:48:17.500 --> 03:48:20.900
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It will be a long-term solution, but it is a solution, sir.

asr-004396
03:48:20.940 --> 03:48:24.180
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, iniisa-isa namin yung isla.

asr-004397
03:48:24.620 --> 03:48:27.180
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Major islands would be five.

asr-004398
03:48:27.660 --> 03:48:30.920
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Panay, Negros, Cebu, Bohol, late summer.

asr-004399
03:48:31.560 --> 03:48:36.340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we can present it to the Honorable Congressman.

asr-004400
03:48:36.800 --> 03:48:39.000
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Once we finish, give us one more month.

asr-004401
03:48:39.440 --> 03:48:41.540
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kasi kailangan namin isimulate at simulate.

asr-004402
03:48:41.640 --> 03:48:48.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Because we cannot rely on the connection of Luzon to Visayas and Visayas to Mindanao all the time.

asr-004403
03:48:48.220 --> 03:48:50.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It should just be a reserve.

asr-004404
03:48:50.940 --> 03:48:53.420
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kung kailangan, pwede tayong mag-i-import.

asr-004405
03:48:53.580 --> 03:48:56.600
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But I think that is the best solution for all the islands.

asr-004406
03:48:56.740 --> 03:49:02.120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I mean, I'm from Panay and we pay about three pesos per four-line rental at one point.

asr-004407
03:49:02.300 --> 03:49:06.120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, kailangan talaga may independence ang kada isa.

asr-004408
03:49:06.420 --> 03:49:08.260
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we're doing the master plan.

asr-004409
03:49:08.440 --> 03:49:10.540
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And in due time, sir, we will present the solution.

asr-004410
03:49:10.540 --> 03:49:12.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, can this be submitted to the committee?

asr-004411
03:49:12.880 --> 03:49:13.860
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mga October, sir.

asr-004412
03:49:14.060 --> 03:49:14.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

asr-004413
03:49:14.500 --> 03:49:15.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, ma'am.

asr-004414
03:49:15.340 --> 03:49:18.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And I think that's the last question.

asr-004415
03:49:18.320 --> 03:49:20.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But may yung first question about the...

asr-004416
03:49:20.940 --> 03:49:21.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Island.

asr-004417
03:49:21.920 --> 03:49:23.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I would like to recognize si Koko.

asr-004418
03:49:25.180 --> 03:49:27.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: President Koko, nag-release to answer.

asr-004419
03:49:27.420 --> 03:49:28.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi ata nakasagot yun.

asr-004420
03:49:28.880 --> 03:49:30.280
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-004421
03:49:30.380 --> 03:49:33.200
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Regarding the concern of the Honorable Tan,

asr-004422
03:49:33.740 --> 03:49:39.200
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: the island actually has sufficient generators and is operating at eight hours at the moment.

asr-004423
03:49:39.760 --> 03:49:44.380
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: So, on the part of NAPO Corps, we commit to study the economics of it and try to increase it.

asr-004424
03:49:44.380 --> 03:49:48.660
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: The current peak demand is 108 kilowatts.

asr-004425
03:49:49.000 --> 03:49:50.920
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: So, pag-aralan po natin yun.

asr-004426
03:49:50.940 --> 03:49:58.960
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: And kung kaya po ng MOE natin, then we will expand it para umunlad lalo yung inyong isla.

asr-004427
03:49:59.080 --> 03:49:59.840
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Salamat po, Mr. Chair.

asr-004428
03:49:59.840 --> 03:50:01.980
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Thank you, Congresswoman President Koko.

asr-004429
03:50:02.840 --> 03:50:03.220
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Thank you.

asr-004430
03:50:03.320 --> 03:50:13.660
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: And I agree also with the good Secretary that each region naman, like in Region 8, we have a geothermal source of energy.

asr-004431
03:50:14.220 --> 03:50:17.580
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: So, mas better siguro na we utilize the local source natin.

asr-004432
03:50:17.580 --> 03:50:20.280
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: So, anyway, thank you, Madam Secretary.

asr-004433
03:50:20.480 --> 03:50:20.820
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Thank you.

asr-004434
03:50:20.940 --> 03:50:21.800
Rep. Stephen James T. Tan: Thank you, Mr. Chair, for the time.

asr-004435
03:50:22.020 --> 03:50:23.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Congressman Tan.

asr-004436
03:50:23.760 --> 03:50:28.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Next, to interpolate from the majority, Congressman John Chan.

asr-004437
03:50:30.240 --> 03:50:31.440
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Salamat po, Mr. Chair.

asr-004438
03:50:31.660 --> 03:50:33.380
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: And magandang hapon po sa inyong lahat.

asr-004439
03:50:33.600 --> 03:50:33.900
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Hello po.

asr-004440
03:50:34.500 --> 03:50:37.800
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, may onting katanungan lang po ako na malapit po sa puso ko.

asr-004441
03:50:38.440 --> 03:50:41.820
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, yung pinakauna po ay tungkol po sa poverty rule.

asr-004442
03:50:42.620 --> 03:50:51.620
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, Madam Secretary, sa Special Provision No. 1 of the May chapter in Volume 3 of the very budget before this committee po,

asr-004443
03:50:52.440 --> 03:50:56.620
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: naka-direct po ang NEA to prioritize yung mga sityo where, quoting the provision,

asr-004444
03:50:56.780 --> 03:51:00.780
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: the absolute number of indigents and the incidence of poverty are high.

asr-004445
03:51:00.780 --> 03:51:05.380
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, as identified in the latest official poverty statistics of the PSA.

asr-004446
03:51:06.100 --> 03:51:13.080
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, yung mga statistics po, meron po tayo yung sa 2023 na full-year official poverty statistics,

asr-004447
03:51:13.520 --> 03:51:22.280
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: which count 1,735,690 poor Filipinos and 279,220 poor families in the Bicol region.

asr-004449
03:51:22.440 --> 03:51:27.940
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, so far, it's the largest absolute count of any region in the country.

asr-004450
03:51:28.520 --> 03:51:37.460
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, yung tanong ko lang po, how will the NEA apply Special Provision No. 1 in the 2027 rollout, Madam Secretary?

asr-004451
03:51:38.400 --> 03:51:45.180
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: And of the sityos program for energization next year, how many are in the regions with the highest poverty counts po?

asr-004452
03:51:45.320 --> 03:51:45.780
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Thank you.

asr-004453
03:51:45.780 --> 03:51:51.760
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So far, following that also, but also as a priority,

asr-004454
03:51:51.760 --> 03:51:58.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: one of the first instructions I've given to NEA is prioritize Mindanao, actually.

asr-004455
03:51:59.280 --> 03:52:01.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's one of the most in need, actually.

asr-004456
03:52:01.980 --> 03:52:06.360
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But on the side of Bicol area, Admin can further explain.

asr-004457
03:52:06.840 --> 03:52:07.260
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you.

asr-004458
03:52:08.840 --> 03:52:09.980
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Tama po yun.

asr-004459
03:52:10.100 --> 03:52:11.640
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: I was given direction.

asr-004460
03:52:12.500 --> 03:52:20.560
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Hinahabol po namin ang Mindanao, especially on those geographically isolated and disadvantageous areas.

asr-004461
03:52:20.560 --> 03:52:30.560
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: And so far, majority of the funding of the SEP was dedicated for the island of Mindanao.

asr-004462
03:52:30.980 --> 03:52:36.660
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: However, dun po sa mga, especially on Region 5, meron din naman po.

asr-004463
03:52:37.480 --> 03:52:44.580
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Medyo, hindi ko lang ko alam ang exact figures, but meron din nung allocation ng Kasoreko 1, 2, 3, and 4,

asr-004464
03:52:44.880 --> 03:52:47.320
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: and even especially Aleko, Albay.

asr-004465
03:52:47.320 --> 03:52:50.320
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: And we are trying to...

asr-004466
03:52:50.560 --> 03:52:59.400
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: stretch the limited funding, having as a national policy, habulin ho namin ang Mindanao.

asr-004467
03:52:59.500 --> 03:53:06.660
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Because when I assume office, ang energization level po ng Mindanao is only at 75%.

asr-004468
03:53:06.660 --> 03:53:10.220
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: So, yun po ang aming hinahabol.

asr-004469
03:53:10.520 --> 03:53:19.400
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: That's why way back 2023, ang Luzon po ay nasa 95,

asr-004470
03:53:19.400 --> 03:53:24.600
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: ang Visayas ay nasa 94, pero we ended up at 89%.

asr-004471
03:53:24.600 --> 03:53:28.940
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Only on the franchise areas of electric cooperatives because of Mindanao.

asr-004472
03:53:29.440 --> 03:53:35.040
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: So, nakita naman po namin, pinuntahan po namin yung mga areas na yan, talaga pong kailangan nila ng kuryente ron.

asr-004473
03:53:35.540 --> 03:53:36.940
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: So, wag po kayo magalala.

asr-004474
03:53:37.320 --> 03:53:45.820
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: At lahat po yan ay ginagawa namin ng plano sa yung tinatawag naming ELTER.

asr-004475
03:53:46.440 --> 03:53:49.380
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Lahat po yan ay pinipili po namin talaga.

asr-004476
03:53:49.400 --> 03:53:51.580
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Yung talagang matindi ang pangangailangan.

asr-004477
03:53:51.780 --> 03:53:52.500
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Marami salamat po.

asr-004478
03:53:53.240 --> 03:53:54.380
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Marami salamat po.

asr-004479
03:53:55.140 --> 03:53:56.700
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Isa rin pong tanong po.

asr-004480
03:53:57.160 --> 03:54:01.420
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Actually, natuwa po ako nakita na nung start of 2026, Secretary,

asr-004481
03:54:01.980 --> 03:54:06.240
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: nag-issue po kayo ng update dun sa ER 1-94

asr-004482
03:54:06.240 --> 03:54:12.840
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: na in-upget po natin from 1% to 3% yung makukuha po ng mga geothermal, yung mga plants po,

asr-004483
03:54:12.880 --> 03:54:15.360
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: within the communities who are supposed to benefit from them.

asr-004484
03:54:16.020 --> 03:54:17.980
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, gusto ko lang po malaman, Secretary,

asr-004485
03:54:17.980 --> 03:54:18.980
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: mayroon po ba tayong...

asr-004486
03:54:19.400 --> 03:54:26.580
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: ...intention or plan in the future na mas palakasin po itong pataasin?

asr-004487
03:54:26.580 --> 03:54:30.120
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Kasi napansin ko po tuwing umiikot po ako sa Region 5,

asr-004488
03:54:30.120 --> 03:54:34.380
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: ang lagi po nila sinasabi ay nandito po sa atin ang mga geothermal plants,

asr-004489
03:54:34.380 --> 03:54:38.780
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: yung mga hydropower plants, pero bakit ang taas pa rin daw po ng kuryente sa kanila.

asr-004490
03:54:38.780 --> 03:54:42.520
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, yung isang gusto po nila mangyari sana ay mas mag-benefit po

asr-004491
03:54:42.520 --> 03:54:46.280
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: pag nasa community nila yung mga ganong planta po.

asr-004492
03:54:46.280 --> 03:54:47.020
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir.

asr-004493
03:54:47.020 --> 03:54:49.180
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That's really the irony.

asr-004494
