04:07:21.730 --> 04:07:23.050
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Now, let me point out

asr-004864
04:07:23.050 --> 04:07:25.190
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: that 1994 pa po,

asr-004865
04:07:25.630 --> 04:07:26.850
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung Republic Act

asr-004866
04:07:26.850 --> 04:07:29.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ano nga ba to?

asr-004867
04:07:29.530 --> 04:07:29.850
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Oh,

asr-004868
04:07:30.990 --> 04:07:33.130
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 1832, the Anti-Pilferage

asr-004869
04:07:33.130 --> 04:07:35.210
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Act, Section 10.

asr-004870
04:07:35.790 --> 04:07:36.950
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nakalagay na po roon,

asr-004871
04:07:38.250 --> 04:07:41.670
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: may mandato na po.

asr-004872
04:07:43.790 --> 04:07:45.230
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Rationalization of system

asr-004873
04:07:45.230 --> 04:07:47.350
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: losses by phasing out of

asr-004874
04:07:47.350 --> 04:07:49.390
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pilferage losses as a component

asr-004875
04:07:49.390 --> 04:07:51.430
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: thereof. So, 1994 pa po

asr-004876
04:07:51.430 --> 04:07:53.470
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sinasabi, tanggalin na at least yung

asr-004877
04:07:53.470 --> 04:07:55.490
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: tinatawag na non-technical

asr-004878
04:07:55.490 --> 04:07:57.410
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa system laws, tapos sinisihil.

asr-004879
04:07:58.130 --> 04:07:59.070
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, 1994 pa yun.

asr-004880
04:07:59.070 --> 04:08:00.970
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Correct. 2026 na tayo.

asr-004881
04:08:00.990 --> 04:08:03.170
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ang sinasabi nyo, yung non-technical,

asr-004882
04:08:03.770 --> 04:08:04.610
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: gano'ng katagal po?

asr-004883
04:08:05.650 --> 04:08:06.570
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Non-technical?

asr-004884
04:08:07.350 --> 04:08:08.070
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pilferage.

asr-004885
04:08:08.290 --> 04:08:11.150
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Four phases, maximum would be one year,

asr-004886
04:08:11.410 --> 04:08:11.790
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair.

asr-004887
04:08:12.050 --> 04:08:14.710
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: One year. So, yung atas ng Pangulo,

asr-004888
04:08:15.470 --> 04:08:17.750
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2027 pa

asr-004889
04:08:17.750 --> 04:08:18.390
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ma-implement.

asr-004890
04:08:18.570 --> 04:08:19.390
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Before the next SONA.

asr-004891
04:08:20.130 --> 04:08:22.370
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Before the next SONA. Okay.

asr-004892
04:08:22.490 --> 04:08:24.910
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung technical, yun ba yung kailangan

asr-004893
04:08:24.910 --> 04:08:25.650
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pa ng budget?

asr-004894
04:08:26.750 --> 04:08:27.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun po ba?

asr-004895
04:08:27.250 --> 04:08:29.490
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We need, Mr. Chair,

asr-004896
04:08:29.550 --> 04:08:30.970
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: we need to see,

asr-004897
04:08:30.990 --> 04:08:34.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: the optimization, optimal plan nila muna

asr-004898
04:08:34.210 --> 04:08:36.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: bago kami mag-decide on this

asr-004899
04:08:36.210 --> 04:08:37.310
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: because we don't want to,

asr-004900
04:08:37.650 --> 04:08:39.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: you cannot just rush this eh.

asr-004901
04:08:39.370 --> 04:08:41.470
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kailangan talaga aral ito kasi very

asr-004902
04:08:41.470 --> 04:08:43.130
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: technical siya.

asr-004903
04:08:43.450 --> 04:08:43.590
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-004904
04:08:45.110 --> 04:08:47.150
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: But yun ba yung pinakita nyo kanina?

asr-004905
04:08:47.330 --> 04:08:49.150
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: You propose a budget of

asr-004906
04:08:49.150 --> 04:08:50.710
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 7.5 billion

asr-004907
04:08:50.710 --> 04:08:53.070
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: over four phases

asr-004908
04:08:53.070 --> 04:08:55.790
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: para ma-tanggal

asr-004909
04:08:55.790 --> 04:08:56.390
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang

asr-004910
04:08:56.390 --> 04:08:59.350
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: this is a technical system loss.

asr-004911
04:08:59.350 --> 04:09:00.410
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that correct?

asr-004912
04:09:00.990 --> 04:09:03.110
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's, it's for the non-technical.

asr-004913
04:09:03.110 --> 04:09:04.410
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: For the non-technical.

asr-004914
04:09:04.410 --> 04:09:05.750
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I, I, I want to explain.

asr-004915
04:09:05.750 --> 04:09:09.290
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The pilferage should be zero right away.

asr-004916
04:09:09.290 --> 04:09:10.110
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes.

asr-004917
04:09:10.110 --> 04:09:11.130
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yun yung ano namin.

asr-004918
04:09:11.130 --> 04:09:13.930
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yun yung, that's our, our idea na

asr-004919
04:09:13.930 --> 04:09:17.270
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: dapat from day one, once we issue this,

asr-004920
04:09:17.270 --> 04:09:19.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: zero na siya kaagad.

asr-004921
04:09:19.050 --> 04:09:22.970
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: May mga non-technical na minsan nami-mix siya,

asr-004922
04:09:22.970 --> 04:09:29.330
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: kaya bantayan ng maayos ng DOE, NEA, and the electric co-op and ERC,

asr-004923
04:09:29.330 --> 04:09:30.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: ah,

asr-004924
04:09:30.210 --> 04:09:32.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: na namin-mix dyan sa non-technical,

asr-004925
04:09:32.050 --> 04:09:33.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: dapat bawal yan.

asr-004926
04:09:33.210 --> 04:09:34.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, this is,

asr-004927
04:09:34.210 --> 04:09:36.710
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: this is for us to reinforce, no?

asr-004928
04:09:36.710 --> 04:09:37.550
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ah,

asr-004929
04:09:37.550 --> 04:09:39.310
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: now, the, the other side of it

asr-004930
04:09:39.310 --> 04:09:41.970
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: is like, kailangan ang inefficiency

asr-004931
04:09:41.970 --> 04:09:45.090
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: na kinukos, ang cost niya is non-technical.

asr-004932
04:09:45.090 --> 04:09:47.510
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yun yung mga kailangan ayusin yung mga linya

asr-004933
04:09:47.510 --> 04:09:49.190
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: or yung mga metro nila.

asr-004934
04:09:49.190 --> 04:09:50.490
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ah, that will take some money.

asr-004935
04:09:50.490 --> 04:09:52.110
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Like what they did in Zamboanga.

asr-004936
04:09:52.110 --> 04:09:54.670
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: For example, pinalitan lahat, naayos nila,

asr-004937
04:09:54.670 --> 04:09:58.370
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: nabawasan yung, nabawasan ang non-technical loss nila.

asr-004938
04:09:58.370 --> 04:10:00.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, that's, that's easier to implement.

asr-004939
04:10:00.050 --> 04:10:03.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: This will not be an additional budget, Mr. Chair.

asr-004940
04:10:03.050 --> 04:10:08.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ah, we will find a way how to assist the electric co-ops

asr-004941
04:10:08.050 --> 04:10:12.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: without asking for, ah, from the National Fund, Mr. Chair.

asr-004942
04:10:12.050 --> 04:10:14.050
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Could you elaborate on that?

asr-004943
04:10:14.050 --> 04:10:18.050
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasi may pinakita kayo, 7.5 billion yung nandun,

asr-004944
04:10:18.050 --> 04:10:20.050
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pero sinasabi niyo hindi manggagaling sa budget.

asr-004945
04:10:20.050 --> 04:10:21.050
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Saan manggagaling ito?

asr-004946
04:10:21.050 --> 04:10:24.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It could come from the cooperative itself.

asr-004947
04:10:24.050 --> 04:10:27.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It could also come, because they have earnings na rin, ano?

asr-004948
04:10:27.050 --> 04:10:29.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It could come also from a loan that, ah,

asr-004949
04:10:29.890 --> 04:10:30.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: we can facilitate.

asr-004950
04:10:30.890 --> 04:10:34.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ah, we are studying, still studying the, ah, several options.

asr-004951
04:10:34.890 --> 04:10:37.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ang, ang, the main point is, ah,

asr-004952
04:10:37.890 --> 04:10:40.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: dapat ang tao hindi nagbabayad pabalik nito.

asr-004953
04:10:40.890 --> 04:10:43.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yung binawas mo, hindi dapat bayaran nila ulit.

asr-004954
04:10:43.890 --> 04:10:45.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-004955
04:10:45.890 --> 04:10:46.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, thank you.

asr-004956
04:10:46.890 --> 04:10:51.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pwedeng manggaling sa co-op, ah, pwedeng, sabi niyo, loan.

asr-004957
04:10:51.890 --> 04:10:53.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ultimately, babayaran din yan.

asr-004958
04:10:53.890 --> 04:10:55.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, yun nga ang concern.

asr-004959
04:10:55.890 --> 04:10:57.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Siguro, mas, ah, ah, um,

asr-004960
04:10:57.890 --> 04:11:01.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: magsabit na lang in writing, mahirap ngayon, eh.

asr-004961
04:11:01.890 --> 04:11:06.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasi nagtataka tayo, bakit kailangan ng 7.5 billion para ma-implement?

asr-004962
04:11:06.890 --> 04:11:13.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Are you talking about yung mga co-op kailangan tulungan para mag-upgrade ng kanilang facilities?

asr-004963
04:11:13.890 --> 04:11:14.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that it?

asr-004964
04:11:14.890 --> 04:11:16.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, ah, not necessarily.

asr-004965
04:11:16.890 --> 04:11:20.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Some co-ops can, can afford to facilitate that also.

asr-004966
04:11:20.890 --> 04:11:25.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But there are also a cluster of co-ops na medyo, medyo ailing na rin.

asr-004967
04:11:25.890 --> 04:11:26.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: At baka hindi kaya.

asr-004968
04:11:26.890 --> 04:11:27.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: At baka hindi kaya.

asr-004969
04:11:27.890 --> 04:11:29.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And that's where we come in also, Mr. Chair.

asr-004970
04:11:29.890 --> 04:11:30.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That's a case-to-case basis.

asr-004971
04:11:30.890 --> 04:11:36.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That's 130 co-ops na kailangan i-assess namin isa-isa, Mr. Chair.

asr-004972
04:11:36.890 --> 04:11:39.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Plus the, ah, the private distribution utilities.

asr-004973
04:11:39.890 --> 04:11:40.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Okay.

asr-004974
04:11:40.890 --> 04:11:42.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Chair.

asr-004975
04:11:42.890 --> 04:11:43.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Another topic muna.

asr-004976
04:11:43.890 --> 04:11:50.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Um, so, yung repeated yellow and red alerts, lalo na sa Visayas at Mindanao.

asr-004977
04:11:50.890 --> 04:11:55.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Um, ano-ano po ba yung mga planta?

asr-004978
04:11:55.890 --> 04:11:56.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit po?

asr-004979
04:11:56.890 --> 04:11:57.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano?

asr-004980
04:11:57.890 --> 04:12:01.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At mukhang, ah, of course, the answer there is extended maintenance.

asr-004981
04:12:01.890 --> 04:12:02.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mga ganon.

asr-004982
04:12:02.890 --> 04:12:03.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Down yung mga planta.

asr-004983
04:12:03.890 --> 04:12:05.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano-anong mga generators ito?

asr-004984
04:12:05.890 --> 04:12:12.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At anong ginagawa nyo para, ah, ma-address yung situation?

asr-004985
04:12:12.890 --> 04:12:16.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Including possible, ah, penalties for these, ah, plants.

asr-004986
04:12:16.890 --> 04:12:17.890
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-004987
04:12:17.890 --> 04:12:18.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-004988
04:12:18.890 --> 04:12:23.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ah, ah, I'll, I'll have, ah, you should give her, ah, the, the two experts in the,

asr-004989
04:12:23.890 --> 04:12:28.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: ah, on this and, ah, ah, ah, Usec, ah, Maracigan to, to address the issue.

asr-004990
04:12:28.890 --> 04:12:30.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: This is a very, very important issue.

asr-004991
04:12:30.890 --> 04:12:31.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes.

asr-004992
04:12:31.890 --> 04:12:32.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Yes.

asr-004993
04:12:32.890 --> 04:12:33.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Usec Maracigan, you are recognized.

asr-004994
04:12:33.890 --> 04:12:35.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-004995
04:12:35.890 --> 04:12:42.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Well, first, let me, ah, let me present what the cases are in the Visayas, which is really

asr-004996
04:12:42.890 --> 04:12:44.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: the main concerns that we have at the moment.

asr-004997
04:12:44.890 --> 04:12:51.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: For the Visayas, ah, it so happens that the planned maintenance happens at the site of

asr-004998
04:12:51.890 --> 04:12:58.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: our small facilities like biomass and hydropower generations.

asr-004999
04:12:58.890 --> 04:13:05.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: We understand that summer, we are in the middle of the summer, so there is reduced water capacity.

asr-005000
04:13:05.890 --> 04:13:08.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Plus, it's an out-milling season for biomass.

asr-005001
04:13:08.890 --> 04:13:10.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: So, reduced capacity.

asr-005002
04:13:10.890 --> 04:13:17.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Unfortunately, aside from the planned maintenance program of some of our facilities, there was

asr-005003
04:13:17.890 --> 04:13:19.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: a lack of water.

asr-005004
04:13:19.890 --> 04:13:20.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah, ah, ah, ah.

asr-005005
04:13:20.890 --> 04:13:21.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah, ah, ah.

asr-005006
04:13:21.890 --> 04:13:26.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: So, we have a major incident that happened that two major units of coal facilities in

asr-005007
04:13:26.890 --> 04:13:32.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: the Visayas gave way one after the other, belonging to the same company.

asr-005008
04:13:32.890 --> 04:13:37.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: And, ah, upon our discovery, the defect was on the manufacturing.

asr-005009
04:13:37.890 --> 04:13:43.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: It was the turbine rotor that had a major concern.

asr-005010
04:13:43.890 --> 04:13:48.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: And they had to ship out the turbine, ah, to be able to be repaired.

asr-005011
04:13:48.890 --> 04:13:50.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: We also lacked the capacity to test the energy.

asr-005012
04:13:50.890 --> 04:13:51.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: So, they sent it to India just for calibration.

asr-005013
04:13:51.890 --> 04:13:52.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: So, it took a while.

asr-005014
04:13:52.890 --> 04:14:01.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: But here, now and then, ah, since much of the facilities are being forced to run outside

asr-005015
04:14:01.890 --> 04:14:06.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: their operating procedures, then one after the other, the other facilities gave way.

asr-005016
04:14:06.890 --> 04:14:14.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Now, in the last month, it so happens that this, Big Danau also has a scheduled maintenance

asr-005017
04:14:14.890 --> 04:14:15.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: program for some of their facilities.

asr-005018
04:14:15.890 --> 04:14:16.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah, ah, ah.

asr-005019
04:14:16.890 --> 04:14:17.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah, ah, ah.

asr-005020
04:14:17.890 --> 04:14:18.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah, ah, ah.

asr-005021
04:14:18.890 --> 04:14:19.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah, ah, ah.

asr-005022
04:14:19.890 --> 04:14:20.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah, ah, ah.

asr-005023
04:14:20.890 --> 04:14:29.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: We are now providing additional capacities to Visayas to the tune of up to 450 megawatts.

asr-005024
04:14:29.890 --> 04:14:38.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: With the reduced capacity of the Visayas, the import from Big Danau was forced at full

asr-005025
04:14:38.890 --> 04:14:39.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: 450.

asr-005026
04:14:39.890 --> 04:14:44.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Even Incluson is also assisting at 250 megawatts.

asr-005027
04:14:44.890 --> 04:14:45.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah, ah, ah.

asr-005028
04:14:45.890 --> 04:14:46.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah.

asr-005029
04:14:46.890 --> 04:14:47.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah.

asr-005030
04:14:47.890 --> 04:14:48.890
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Ah.

asr-005031
04:14:48.890 --> 04:14:51.130
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: the magnitude of the reduction in capacity.

asr-005032
04:14:51.690 --> 04:14:55.090
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: But with the scheduled maintenance program in Mindanao,

asr-005033
04:14:55.490 --> 04:14:59.150
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: the transfer of capacity to Visayas is also reduced.

asr-005034
04:15:00.370 --> 04:15:10.170
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: Unfortunately, coinciding again, there were first outages also of other coal facilities in Mindanao.

asr-005035
04:15:10.870 --> 04:15:16.090
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: For the capacity for Visayas, poor Mindanao is further reduced to almost zero.

asr-005036
04:15:17.270 --> 04:15:26.430
DOE Undersecretary Mario Marasigan: That is the reason why currently we have red and yellow alerts for Visayas and a long yellow alerts for Mindanao.

asr-005037
