asr-006163
05:39:39.860 --> 05:39:46.500
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ang una ko pong katanungan, ito po ba ay input ng Department of Energy?

asr-006164
05:39:50.830 --> 05:39:55.110
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sir, I think the question is whether we follow it or not.

asr-006165
05:39:55.510 --> 05:39:55.710
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: No.

asr-006166
05:39:56.070 --> 05:39:57.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Whether it is an input.

asr-006167
05:39:57.550 --> 05:40:01.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Because I believe that every policy, major policy, should be…

asr-006168
05:40:01.550 --> 05:40:03.370
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Meron po stop work.

asr-006169
05:40:03.690 --> 05:40:06.870
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Nakagawa po ba ng stop work dito ang DOE?

asr-006170
05:40:07.970 --> 05:40:12.170
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sir, we have submitted several suggestions.

asr-006171
05:40:12.350 --> 05:40:15.570
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Included na rin yung system loss, but on system loss also.

asr-006172
05:40:15.570 --> 05:40:21.610
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Meron po kayong suggestion sa ating Pangulo na tanggalin ang systems loss.

asr-006173
05:40:21.630 --> 05:40:22.510
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: On the VAT, sir.

asr-006174
05:40:23.370 --> 05:40:24.050
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: On the VAT.

asr-006175
05:40:24.150 --> 05:40:24.430
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir.

asr-006176
05:40:24.430 --> 05:40:26.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ang pangako ng Pangulo ay the whole…

asr-006177
05:40:26.750 --> 05:40:27.370
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Correct, sir.

asr-006178
05:40:27.450 --> 05:40:29.330
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: There was discussion also of system loss.

asr-006179
05:40:30.670 --> 05:40:31.370
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: On our side…

asr-006180
05:40:31.550 --> 05:40:32.910
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: On our side, it's the VAT.

asr-006181
05:40:33.070 --> 05:40:36.530
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And then we also had discussions about system loss.

asr-006182
05:40:36.670 --> 05:40:40.230
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But we leave it to the Office of the President for the decision.

asr-006183
05:40:40.390 --> 05:40:41.110
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But, for example, merong figures.

asr-006184
05:40:41.370 --> 05:40:49.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: May mga figures involved in, for example, in the decision to eliminate systems loss.

asr-006185
05:40:49.930 --> 05:40:51.650
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: May figures po.

asr-006186
05:40:51.750 --> 05:40:52.450
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Nakakatapat yan.

asr-006187
05:40:52.450 --> 05:40:53.030
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Iyan po.

asr-006188
05:40:53.150 --> 05:40:58.790
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Aware po ba ang Pangulo kung ano yung mga mangyayari after eliminating the whole systems loss?

asr-006189
05:41:00.050 --> 05:41:01.030
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kahit na po yung ano lang.

asr-006190
05:41:01.130 --> 05:41:01.450
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yung nakatapat.

asr-006191
05:41:01.550 --> 05:41:02.390
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ang technical lang.

asr-006192
05:41:02.510 --> 05:41:06.330
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Huwag na natin pag-usapan yung technical systems loss.

asr-006193
05:41:06.630 --> 05:41:09.970
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We submit all documents, sir.

asr-006194
05:41:10.270 --> 05:41:15.190
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But not all the discussion in the SONA.

asr-006195
05:41:16.090 --> 05:41:17.410
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's something that's…

asr-006196
05:41:17.410 --> 05:41:18.770
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's instructions to us.

asr-006197
05:41:18.930 --> 05:41:20.250
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, hindi siya…

asr-006198
05:41:20.250 --> 05:41:24.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yung ini-discuss muna namin and then we say, eto po ilagay ninyo.

asr-006199
05:41:24.090 --> 05:41:25.510
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It doesn't work like that.

asr-006200
05:41:25.610 --> 05:41:28.810
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's more of the assessment of the Office of the President.

asr-006201
05:41:29.010 --> 05:41:30.270
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: What should be our priority?

asr-006202
05:41:30.470 --> 05:41:30.830
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But rather…

asr-006203
05:41:31.550 --> 05:41:32.570
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's not the other way around.

asr-006204
05:41:32.650 --> 05:41:34.450
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Na kami magsasabi, eto dapat priority.

asr-006205
05:41:34.550 --> 05:41:35.970
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, I cannot really answer that, sir.

asr-006206
05:41:35.970 --> 05:41:39.950
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sa stop work nyo, there's technical systems loss and non-technical.

asr-006207
05:41:40.290 --> 05:41:41.050
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes, sir.

asr-006208
05:41:41.150 --> 05:41:41.870
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: We have a…

asr-006209
05:41:41.870 --> 05:41:47.690
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At ang recommendation ngayon, malamang ito yung maging policy ng government, yung non-technical

asr-006210
05:41:47.690 --> 05:41:48.430
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: lang ang alisin.

asr-006211
05:41:48.570 --> 05:41:49.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Tama po ba?

asr-006212
05:41:49.590 --> 05:41:57.230
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The discussion, as we understand it from the directive and the further discussions to that,

asr-006213
05:41:57.710 --> 05:41:58.510
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: it's…

asr-006214
05:41:58.510 --> 05:42:01.070
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We will really work hard to eliminate…

asr-006215
05:42:01.550 --> 05:42:02.910
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Eliminate both, sir.

asr-006216
05:42:03.090 --> 05:42:03.490
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir.

asr-006217
05:42:04.350 --> 05:42:06.910
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If it's possible, then we will tell you, sir.

asr-006218
05:42:07.670 --> 05:42:14.130
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The plan is that we will have the optimal distribution plan of each cooperative.

asr-006219
05:42:14.870 --> 05:42:22.250
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We will give them six months to make the preparation so that we can quantify the effort, the funding

asr-006220
05:42:22.250 --> 05:42:24.410
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: and everything, the time that we need.

asr-006221
05:42:24.710 --> 05:42:25.410
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We need…

asr-006222
05:42:25.410 --> 05:42:27.810
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: They need about six months to finalize.

asr-006223
05:42:27.870 --> 05:42:30.030
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's not an easy work for them to do.

asr-006224
05:42:30.030 --> 05:42:31.210
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: For example, Metro Manila.

asr-006225
05:42:31.550 --> 05:42:33.850
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: All the clients of Meralco.

asr-006226
05:42:35.230 --> 05:42:38.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Masyadong madali po yan dahil 5.6% yung kanilang systems loss.

asr-006227
05:42:39.630 --> 05:42:40.410
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Tama po?

asr-006228
05:42:41.290 --> 05:42:45.230
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Their non-technical is 1% and our…

asr-006229
05:42:45.230 --> 05:42:45.930
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's very low.

asr-006230
05:42:46.190 --> 05:42:50.650
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Meralco actually has one of the lowest, but they're willing naman to lower it pa.

asr-006231
05:42:51.350 --> 05:42:52.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But we haven't finished…

asr-006232
05:42:52.890 --> 05:42:53.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: May pangako ang pangulo.

asr-006233
05:42:53.870 --> 05:42:55.050
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Alisin ang systems loss.

asr-006234
05:42:55.110 --> 05:42:55.350
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes, sir.

asr-006235
05:42:55.350 --> 05:42:55.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Meralco.

asr-006236
05:42:56.050 --> 05:42:57.310
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Will they comply with that?

asr-006237
05:42:58.270 --> 05:42:59.350
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We are…

asr-006238
05:43:00.030 --> 05:43:01.470
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I want to qualify.

asr-006239
05:43:01.550 --> 05:43:05.210
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I want to qualify the answer na hindi pa tapos yung usapan namin with the private.

asr-006240
05:43:05.310 --> 05:43:07.130
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Inuna namin yung electric co-ops kasi.

asr-006241
05:43:07.790 --> 05:43:13.270
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, you said you have actually a meeting with all of them next week, tomorrow, to finalize

asr-006242
05:43:13.270 --> 05:43:14.170
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: kung ano yung guidelines.

asr-006243
05:43:14.370 --> 05:43:16.390
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kasi iba yung guideline for electric co-ops.

asr-006244
05:43:16.530 --> 05:43:18.390
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: They're in a different financial situation.

asr-006245
05:43:18.850 --> 05:43:20.190
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And then the private utility.

asr-006246
05:43:20.350 --> 05:43:24.530
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, I cannot really commit right now kung ano yung finalize namin.

asr-006247
05:43:24.830 --> 05:43:29.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sa aking pong pag-aaral, sa buong mundo, doon sa mga non-private…

asr-006248
05:43:29.550 --> 05:43:30.430
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: non-private…

asr-006249
05:43:30.430 --> 05:43:38.890
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: sa mga privatized power generation and distribution, lahat yan may systems loss.

asr-006250
05:43:40.070 --> 05:43:46.730
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, ang ibig sabihin, kung mawawala yung systems loss, ang Pilipinas lang ang bansa na walang systems loss.

asr-006251
05:43:46.850 --> 05:43:47.450
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Tama po ba yan?

asr-006252
05:43:48.050 --> 05:43:49.830
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That will be the case, sir.

asr-006253
05:43:50.570 --> 05:43:57.250
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, right now, what we are more confident about is the non-technical.

asr-006254
05:43:57.670 --> 05:43:58.550
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yan tatanggalin kami.

asr-006255
05:43:58.550 --> 05:43:59.550
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kasi po, yung sustainability…

asr-006256
05:44:00.430 --> 05:44:07.110
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: napakalaking question yan, na hindi ko malaman kung saan kukunin yung technical systems loss.

asr-006257
05:44:07.430 --> 05:44:13.390
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At pagdating naman po, mas maliit na portion, sabi nyo nga, yung non-technical systems loss.

asr-006258
05:44:13.770 --> 05:44:18.270
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kung sasagutin po yan ang gobyerno, ayuda po yan.

asr-006259
05:44:18.470 --> 05:44:18.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir.

asr-006260
05:44:18.890 --> 05:44:20.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I think we would rather…

asr-006261
05:44:21.690 --> 05:44:22.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We are actually…

asr-006262
05:44:23.570 --> 05:44:28.030
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ang kailangan kasi hindi yung gagastos tayo ng sobrang laki tapos yung beneficio.

asr-006263
05:44:28.150 --> 05:44:28.890
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ikaw, ikaw…

asr-006264
05:44:28.890 --> 05:44:30.410
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sisingilin mo lang naman.

asr-006265
05:44:30.430 --> 05:44:36.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At mas makikinabang po yan, yung mas malaki ang konsumo.

asr-006266
05:44:37.730 --> 05:44:43.050
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yung mga mahihirap, mas maliit ang pakinabang dahil maliit lang yung kanila konsumo.

asr-006267
05:44:43.130 --> 05:44:43.930
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir. We do understand.

asr-006268
05:44:44.030 --> 05:44:47.490
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we're treading carefully, making sure that our co-ops are steady.

asr-006269
05:44:47.990 --> 05:44:48.430
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pero they make…

asr-006270
05:44:49.010 --> 05:44:52.390
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: This is not business as usual for electric co-ops anymore.

asr-006271
05:44:52.890 --> 05:44:54.470
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kailangan ayusin nila yung trabaho nila.

asr-006272
05:44:54.930 --> 05:44:59.330
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That private, I cannot commit yet kung ano pa yung plan, sir.

asr-006273
05:44:59.330 --> 05:45:00.330
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Because we're still working on it

asr-006274
05:45:00.000 --> 05:45:25.260
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Very tricky po yan. Kasi imagine, for this budget, daming pinangako ni ating kaibigan na gusto nating matupad, pero ang ating fiscal space for capital outlay is only 16% of 7.2 trillion, 1.1 trillion.

asr-006275
05:45:25.260 --> 05:45:36.720
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ngayon, yung mga new projects, kasama na po dyan, yung mga allocation per district ng mga congressmen, baka pag pinagbigyan kayo ni Chairman Rupus, baka mawalan kami ng mga projects.

asr-006276
05:45:37.860 --> 05:45:39.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, sir. Mr. Chair.

asr-006277
05:45:39.980 --> 05:45:52.840
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Saan dyan pa rin po yung mga foreign-assisted projects? Parang sobrang sikip na eh. Hindi ko malaman kung saan kukunin. For example, 10 billion for systems law, saan kukunin yun?

asr-006278
05:45:52.840 --> 05:45:55.240
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, Mr. Chair. We don't understand.

asr-006279
05:45:55.260 --> 05:46:07.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But we will work out that we will not ask for additional budget, sir. We'll find a way na para ma-fundingan yung improvements sa mga electric co-ops natin. And Mr. Guevara wants to add something, sir.

asr-006280
05:46:07.840 --> 05:46:20.060
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Opo. Pero, hindi. Nangunawaan ko na po. Okay na po. Ang pangalawang tanong ko. So, itong taon na to, hindi matutupad yung pangako ng Pangulo na matatanggal ang systems laws.

asr-006281
05:46:21.540 --> 05:46:25.140
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Partial lang, sir. Baka our target really is like before the next summer.

asr-006282
05:46:25.260 --> 05:46:26.520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, now we will finish this, sir.

asr-006283
05:46:27.180 --> 05:46:29.780
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Before the next summer. Okay. Thank you.

asr-006284
05:46:29.780 --> 05:46:50.780
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, pagdating naman po sa nung nakaraan po, let me congratulate you dahil talaga naman hindi tayo nagkaroon ng kakulangan sa supply ng diesel. Pero iyan pong crisis sa Middle East, ano yan eh, anytime pwedeng bumalik eh. Wala pong katapusan yan.

asr-006285
05:46:51.540 --> 05:46:54.640
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Hindi pang nawawala at pwede pang lumubha.

asr-006286
05:46:55.260 --> 05:47:18.700
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ang karamihan po ng mga bansa na hindi masyadong naapektuhan in terms of prices, yung may malalaking reserve. At least diesel. Kasi po, pinakamalaking pangakailangan natin, diesel. Ilan po ba ang reserve natin for, sa ngayon, yung capacity ng reserve natin for diesel. At least for diesel lang.

asr-006287
05:47:18.700 --> 05:47:21.200
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yan ang pinakamahalaga sa akin.

asr-006288
05:47:21.200 --> 05:47:22.780
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If you indulge me lang.

asr-006289
05:47:23.380 --> 05:47:25.240
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If you can indulge me.

asr-006290
05:47:25.260 --> 05:47:55.000
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We actually created, formulated a fuel transition plan. Because, you're correct, we cannot be dependent on imported fuel. We are 100% dependent on that. Well, 99%. So, our plan is by 2040, bawasan natin ang 50% yan. And how do we get there? We have several plans. There are several components, electric vehicles, more exploration, electrification of our appliances.

asr-006291
05:47:55.260 --> 05:48:13.300
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Lahat-lahat po, we're working on that. And in addition to that, we need reserves in the country. Unfortunately, our storage facilities are private. Ginagamit lang natin yung binibilang natin. When we tell you in the news there's 50 days, it's in the private facilities.

asr-006292
05:48:13.300 --> 05:48:23.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: PNOC, headed by President Chico Alvarez, is setting up, and hopefully within this term, we can set up 1 billion barrels.

asr-006293
05:48:23.220 --> 05:48:25.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Enough for 1 million barrels.

asr-006294
05:48:25.260 --> 05:48:54.720
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The storage facility na government-owned. Para over time, we increase and increase. It is true that we are protected if we have reserves. Kasi I think it was Yusek Sandy who told me that having reserves not only protects you from the unpredictability or volatility of whatever war there is in the rest of the world, it also shields us, it affects our growth.

asr-006295
05:48:55.260 --> 05:49:06.140
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kasi nasi-shield tayo sa currency exchange, sa volatility of the price. So malaki talaga yung advantage sa atin pag meron tayo. So we're working on it already.

asr-006296
05:49:06.140 --> 05:49:15.200
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes, I do understand. Pero sa ngayon po, ilan yung capacity natin, whether public or private storage?

asr-006297
05:49:16.320 --> 05:49:16.840
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: 47?

asr-006298
05:49:17.520 --> 05:49:19.640
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 47 million?

asr-006299
05:49:20.220 --> 05:49:25.140
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 47 days, which is about how many?

asr-006300
05:49:25.260 --> 05:49:26.120
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 47 days which would be about how many million liters?

asr-006301
05:49:31.040 --> 05:49:32.160
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: That would be about...

asr-006302
05:49:32.160 --> 05:49:32.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Just a figure.

asr-006303
05:49:33.680 --> 05:49:34.780
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: This one.

asr-006304
05:49:36.100 --> 05:49:36.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Give an estimate.

asr-006305
05:49:37.480 --> 05:49:44.620
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: About 2.7 billion liters.

asr-006306
05:49:45.620 --> 05:49:52.620
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But that includes yung mga private na owners. Kasi sila, ano naman sila, 15 days lang ang kanilang...

asr-006307
05:49:52.620 --> 05:49:53.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kasama.

asr-006308
05:49:53.220 --> 05:49:59.120
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yung private, 15 days lang ang nire-reserve nila. Kasi syempre, yung kapital, tama.

asr-006309
05:49:59.160 --> 05:50:02.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay. Recognize. Sino ba?

asr-006310
05:50:02.360 --> 05:50:02.660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Go ahead

asr-006311
05:50:03.800 --> 05:50:08.660
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Lahat po ng storage ngayon, private. Kasi ang industry po natin, deregulate.

asr-006312
05:50:08.740 --> 05:50:17.980
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: I mean yung mga oil distributors. Kasi meron talaga na private na nagpaparenta lang.

asr-006313
05:50:18.520 --> 05:50:20.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you for the last question.

asr-006314
05:50:20.080 --> 05:50:26.220
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pero meron naman na mga private companies, meron silang mga estasyon ng gasolina.

asr-006315
05:50:27.040 --> 05:50:29.080
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yung kanilang, ang sinasabi nila, ang kanilang kapatid,

asr-006316
05:50:29.160 --> 05:50:36.040
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 15 days lang na reserve. Kasi hindi nila kaya yung kapital.

asr-006317
05:50:37.000 --> 05:50:39.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kindly answer the last question

asr-006318
05:50:41.300 --> 05:50:52.220
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Yes. When we quote yung, actually, total country volume po yun, yung regional na storage, tama po, hindi ganong kalalaki.

asr-006319
05:50:52.720 --> 05:50:56.640
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Ang kinu-quote natin yung entire country storage volume.

asr-006320
05:50:57.280 --> 05:50:58.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay. Thank you.

asr-006321
05:50:58.160 --> 05:50:59.060
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Just one follow-up.

asr-006322
05:50:59.160 --> 05:51:00.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay. I will allow you.

asr-006323
05:51:01.120 --> 05:51:06.080
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Hindi ba pwedeng magkaroon tayo ng target na within government control?

asr-006324
05:51:06.080 --> 05:51:12.500
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: For example, si Alvarez, meron siyang 1 million, public owned.

asr-006325
05:51:12.780 --> 05:51:23.420
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pero dapat meron tayong target na kahit privately owned, pero exclusive yung ownership ng Philippine government dun sa reserve.

asr-006326
05:51:23.840 --> 05:51:29.080
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Para sa ganon, hindi tayo nakadepende sa presyo ng mga private companies.

asr-006327
05:51:29.160 --> 05:51:45.880
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Mr. Chair, yes. Yes, kasama po yan ng planning. In terms of the strategic petroleum reserve, kailangan merong regional distribution din.

asr-006328
05:51:46.420 --> 05:51:57.080
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Kasi nakikita rin natin yung importance ng regional distribution. And kung ano ang i-store natin, kung crude oil, diesel, gasoline, anong proportion?

asr-006329
05:51:57.980 --> 05:52:00.040
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ngayon po, ilan yung reserve natin?

asr-006330
05:52:00.140 --> 05:52:00.860
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Government?

asr-006331
05:52:00.860 --> 05:52:01.420
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Government controlled

asr-006332
05:52:01.600 --> 05:52:02.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's going to be the last?

asr-006333
05:52:02.860 --> 05:52:03.060
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes.

asr-006334
05:52:03.060 --> 05:52:04.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pwede pa tayo mag-second round, boss?

asr-006335
05:52:04.620 --> 05:52:04.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Last.

asr-006336
05:52:06.580 --> 05:52:10.640
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ano yung reserve na talagang within the control of the government?

asr-006337
05:52:10.660 --> 05:52:12.360
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay. That's the second last question.

asr-006338
05:52:13.740 --> 05:52:19.520
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Yung 5 days po na nabili ni PNOC, naka-store po ngayon sa isang private storage.

asr-006339
05:52:19.760 --> 05:52:20.160
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: 5 days.

asr-006340
05:52:20.420 --> 05:52:21.260
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Okay. Thank you.

asr-006341
05:52:21.440 --> 05:52:21.860
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Thank you.

asr-006342
05:52:22.160 --> 05:52:23.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But sir, we can have a second round.

asr-006343
05:52:26.060 --> 05:52:26.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Huwag naman.

asr-006344
05:52:27.200 --> 05:52:27.720
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Masaya na.

asr-006345
05:52:27.720 --> 05:52:28.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Masaya ka na?

asr-006346
05:52:28.980 --> 05:52:30.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So next to interpellate

asr-006347
05:52:30.860 --> 05:52:34.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: From the majority, Congressman Art Yap, my idol, sir.

asr-006348
05:52:37.760 --> 05:52:39.500
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006349
05:52:40.200 --> 05:52:43.300
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Kanina po pagpasok ko, hindi ko alam kung doon ako uupo dito.

asr-006350
05:52:43.760 --> 05:52:45.580
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Kasi puro congressman rin po doon eh.

asr-006351
05:52:47.520 --> 05:52:48.000
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Diba?

asr-006352
05:52:48.480 --> 05:52:49.120
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Nahanap ko yung...

asr-006353
05:52:49.120 --> 05:52:49.720
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Ito yung si Chico yung daw.

asr-006354
05:52:50.080 --> 05:52:50.520
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Ha?

asr-006355
05:52:50.780 --> 05:52:51.480
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Si Chico yung...

asr-006356
05:52:51.480 --> 05:52:52.580
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: O, isang congressman.

asr-006357
05:52:53.840 --> 05:52:55.520
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Si Chico yung daw gusto mong salita.

asr-006358
05:52:56.100 --> 05:52:56.780
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Isa pa.

asr-006359
05:52:58.240 --> 05:53:00.500
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Si Nani Almeda, congressman rin po yan eh.

asr-006360
05:53:01.600 --> 05:53:02.040
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: O.

asr-006361
05:53:03.160 --> 05:53:06.640
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: At hinahanap ko po yung ano, yung the better Fuentebella

asr-006362
05:53:07.420 --> 05:53:07.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: May sakit.

asr-006363
05:53:08.200 --> 05:53:08.860
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: May sakit.

asr-006364
05:53:09.300 --> 05:53:09.380
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Ah.

asr-006365
05:53:10.680 --> 05:53:10.900
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Ah.

asr-006366
05:53:13.140 --> 05:53:13.340
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Hindi.

asr-006367
05:53:14.200 --> 05:53:16.680
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Yung takeaway ko po sa...

asr-006368
05:53:16.680 --> 05:53:17.240
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Sa ano?

asr-006369
05:53:17.700 --> 05:53:19.360
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Sa proceedings this...

asr-006370
05:53:19.360 --> 05:53:21.600
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Today is...

asr-006371
05:53:22.640 --> 05:53:31.600
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Very much ano naman, pro-active yung DOE at they believe in the power of solar energy.

asr-006372
05:53:31.600 --> 05:53:33.600
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: In fact, Yusek Guevara...

asr-006373
05:53:34.600 --> 05:53:35.600
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: He mentioned that.

asr-006374
05:53:35.600 --> 05:53:44.820
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: And I'd like to congratulate and thank Secretary Sharon Garin for releasing the Circular on Zero Export Renewable Solar System.

asr-006375
05:53:44.940 --> 05:53:45.960
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Thank you very much, ma'am po.

asr-006376
05:53:47.620 --> 05:53:51.740
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: But in the same way, may tanong lang po ako doon.

asr-006377
05:53:51.840 --> 05:53:59.440
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: As much as we are now advocating for solar power, dahil ang positive noon, we hope that it will lower consumer cost.

asr-006378
05:54:00.940 --> 05:54:04.440
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Ano po ang mangyayari doon sa stranded cost ng mga...

asr-006379
05:54:04.600 --> 05:54:08.420
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Na mga distribution utilities.

asr-006380
05:54:08.820 --> 05:54:14.060
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Kasi syempre, nanguntrata po sila for a certain capacity.

asr-006381
05:54:14.800 --> 05:54:22.240
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: And in their areas, pag bumababa na po yung requirement doon sa power, then papano po yung stranded cost?

asr-006382
05:54:22.240 --> 05:54:29.080
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Hindi pa po pwedeng sabihin natin sa ERC, Madam Secretary, na i-review po yung mga ano.

asr-006383
05:54:29.280 --> 05:54:31.300
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: At pwede po nilang ano...

asr-006384
05:54:31.300 --> 05:54:33.360
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Can I please ask Chairman Juan that?

asr-006385
05:54:33.860 --> 05:54:34.340
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Mr. Chairman?

asr-006386
05:54:35.200 --> 05:54:40.040
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Posible kaya yun na pag-review nyo, tanggayin nyo po yung stranded cost ng mga distribution utilities.

asr-006387
05:54:48.120 --> 05:54:51.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kindly use the other mic now, siguro, if it's not functioning.

asr-006388
05:54:52.560 --> 05:54:53.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pakiayos yung mic

asr-006389
05:55:02.060 --> 05:55:02.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ...

asr-006390
05:55:02.500 --> 05:55:03.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah, let's...

asr-006391
05:55:03.380 --> 05:55:07.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Siguro siya sabi lang nung ano, be concise and brief sa answer mo.

asr-006392
05:55:07.060 --> 05:55:12.060
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: The situation will be akin to the current implementation of the ARCOA,

asr-006393
05:55:13.120 --> 05:55:16.060
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: where we have actually advised our distribution...

asr-006394
05:55:16.440 --> 05:55:18.800
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: utilities entering power supply contracts

asr-006395
05:55:18.800 --> 05:55:22.280
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: to include in their power supply agreements a carve-out provision.

asr-006396
05:55:22.960 --> 05:55:25.600
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Also, if there are no carve-out provisions,

asr-006397
05:55:25.860 --> 05:55:31.840
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and the distribution utilities will be left with excess contracted capacities,

asr-006398
05:55:31.840 --> 05:55:37.840
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: if the distribution utilities will be able to unload or renegotiate with their suppliers

asr-006399
05:55:38.400 --> 05:55:42.140
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: so that they can have a lowering of the contracted volume,

asr-006400
05:55:42.560 --> 05:55:46.420
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: or unload these excess contracted volumes,

asr-006401
05:55:46.440 --> 05:55:48.460
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: to an affiliate RES,

asr-006402
05:55:48.660 --> 05:55:55.400
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: so that it will be the RES that will be selling this contracted capacity,

asr-006403
05:55:55.640 --> 05:56:00.920
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: or for these distribution utilities to participate in WESM

asr-006404
05:56:00.920 --> 05:56:05.040
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: by offloading these excess contracted capacities in the WESM.

asr-006405
05:56:07.120 --> 05:56:10.520
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: But, Chairman, pag hindi po pumayag yung providers,

asr-006406
05:56:11.680 --> 05:56:16.120
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: wala na po pang recourse ang distribution utilities?

asr-006407
05:56:16.440 --> 05:56:27.540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Because, Sir, ang issue dito, Chairman, is

asr-006408
05:56:27.540 --> 05:56:31.860
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: we always hear the words in the hearings,

asr-006409
05:56:32.340 --> 05:56:33.820
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: non-impairment, non-impairment.

asr-006410
05:56:34.300 --> 05:56:37.100
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: But, pag hindi po natin gagawin yung police power,

asr-006411
05:56:37.580 --> 05:56:40.480
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: hindi po natin gagamitin yun, the police power of the state,

asr-006412
05:56:41.100 --> 05:56:45.940
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: to lift and to suspend these so-called non-impairment of contracts,

asr-006413
05:56:46.760 --> 05:56:50.480
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: then, yung stranded cost na po yun,

asr-006414
05:56:50.480 --> 05:56:53.480
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: i-charge rin po sa lahat ng consumers na maiiwi,

asr-006415
05:56:53.520 --> 05:56:58.360
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: So, in the one hand, pinopromote po natin sila mag-solar power.

asr-006416
05:56:59.260 --> 05:57:01.980
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Pagkatapos, yung stranded cost,

asr-006417
05:57:02.080 --> 05:57:06.280
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: maiiwan doon sa mga consumers that do not have the ability

asr-006418
05:57:06.280 --> 05:57:08.960
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: to procure and to buy their solar power systems.

asr-006419
05:57:09.300 --> 05:57:10.840
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Mataas pa rin yung singil sa kanila.

asr-006420
05:57:11.780 --> 05:57:13.880
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: At ang sabi po, eh, non-impairment po eh.

asr-006421
05:57:14.520 --> 05:57:17.380
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: But, if we will continue to reason that way,

asr-006422
05:57:17.960 --> 05:57:21.640
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: then the effects, the positive effects of disruptive technologies

asr-006423
05:57:21.640 --> 05:57:23.480
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: will never be, will never be, will never be,

asr-006424
05:57:23.480 --> 05:57:23.500
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: will never be, will never be, will never be,

asr-006425
05:57:23.500 --> 05:57:25.460
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: will never be enjoyed by the people.

asr-006426
05:57:25.960 --> 05:57:30.560
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We will look into that, Mr. Chair.

asr-006427
05:57:31.060 --> 05:57:38.020
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Although, for PSAs that were contracted after the CSP policy of the DOE

asr-006428
05:57:38.020 --> 05:57:41.980
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and after we issued the CSP rules in 2023,

asr-006429
05:57:42.400 --> 05:57:45.600
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: we've already prescribed a template for a PSA

asr-006430
05:57:45.600 --> 05:57:48.000
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: where there's an automatic carve-out provision.

asr-006431
05:57:48.480 --> 05:57:53.340
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, kung ang magiging stranded capacities na lang

asr-006432
05:57:53.340 --> 05:57:56.000
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: ay yung mga hindi na-cover nito mga bagong PSAs,

asr-006433
05:57:56.020 --> 05:57:57.240
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: na walang carve-out,

asr-006434
05:57:57.620 --> 05:58:05.160
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: we will look into how we will be able to assist the distribution utilities

asr-006435
05:58:05.160 --> 05:58:09.280
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: para ma-offload nila itong kontratang ito

asr-006436
05:58:09.280 --> 05:58:13.020
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: at hindi naman ma-apekto ang remaining captive customers niya.

asr-006437
05:58:13.840 --> 05:58:14.940
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Thank you, Chairman.

asr-006438
05:58:15.500 --> 05:58:19.020
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: And you may want to refer to the Supreme Court case,

asr-006439
05:58:19.780 --> 05:58:21.940
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: yung NDC versus Philippine Veterans Bank

asr-006440
05:58:21.940 --> 05:58:25.960
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: because narecognize po doon na yung sinasabing sanctity

asr-006441
05:58:25.960 --> 05:58:26.860
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: of non-impairment,

asr-006442
05:58:27.040 --> 05:58:28.660
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: pwede po natin i-override yun.

asr-006443
05:58:30.140 --> 05:58:38.260
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: If the impact is so embedded in public welfare,

asr-006444
05:58:38.560 --> 05:58:39.620
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: pwede po natin gawin yun.

asr-006445
05:58:41.600 --> 05:58:44.460
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Yung issue rin po sa systems loss,

asr-006446
05:58:46.060 --> 05:58:47.300
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: napag-usapan po natin,

asr-006447
05:58:47.420 --> 05:58:49.780
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: sabi po ni Madam Secretary at least,

asr-006448
05:58:49.780 --> 05:58:53.760
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: yung mga non-technical systems loss will automatically be,

asr-006449
05:58:54.220 --> 05:58:54.600
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: ah,

asr-006450
05:58:55.960 --> 05:58:58.300
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: will solve that problem within one year po.

asr-006451
05:58:59.200 --> 05:58:59.800
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Pero,

asr-006452
05:59:00.400 --> 05:59:04.660
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: may existing policy po yung National Electrification Administration

asr-006453
05:59:04.660 --> 05:59:11.760
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: na yung mga distribution utilities are required doon sa sityo electrification

asr-006454
05:59:11.760 --> 05:59:14.460
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: that they have to keep on increasing

asr-006455
05:59:14.460 --> 05:59:18.240
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: yung pag-electrify sa mga sityos.

asr-006456
05:59:19.640 --> 05:59:20.640
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Posible kaya,

asr-006457
05:59:20.840 --> 05:59:23.020
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: tanong ko sa Department of Energy ito

asr-006458
05:59:23.020 --> 05:59:25.140
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: or sa NEA,

asr-006459
05:59:25.140 --> 05:59:27.120
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: pwede kayang ma-suspend yun?

asr-006460
05:59:27.880 --> 05:59:28.280
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Dahil,

asr-006461
05:59:29.100 --> 05:59:31.920
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: kung yung mga distribution utilities,

asr-006462
05:59:32.060 --> 05:59:34.720
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: ipapagpatuloy po natin yung challenge sa kanila,

asr-006463
05:59:35.260 --> 05:59:39.800
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: yung pressure na you keep on electrifying all of those sityos,

asr-006464
05:59:39.920 --> 05:59:43.320
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: aakyat rin po yung technical systems losses.

asr-006465
05:59:43.500 --> 05:59:43.640
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: So,

asr-006466
05:59:44.240 --> 05:59:46.800
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: yung sinasabing yung bababa yung non-technical,

asr-006467
05:59:46.940 --> 05:59:48.380
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: pero aakyat naman yung technical

asr-006468
05:59:48.380 --> 05:59:52.740
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: dahil puro tayo patayin ang patayin ng sityo electrification,

asr-006469
05:59:53.520 --> 05:59:53.860
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: eh di,

asr-006470
05:59:54.260 --> 05:59:55.120
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: the right hand,

asr-006471
05:59:55.140 --> 05:59:58.460
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: is taking away what the left hand is giving out.

asr-006472
06:00:00.500 --> 06:00:01.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, sir.

asr-006473
06:00:06.000 --> 06:00:09.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can you pass the mic, please? Sorry.

asr-006474
06:00:12.960 --> 06:00:20.960
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Mr. Chair, yes, with all the developments surrounding the electric coffee industry,

asr-006475
06:00:21.100 --> 06:00:26.640
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: as in fact, about 30 minutes ago, pinag-uusapan namin ni Congressman Dago,

asr-006476
06:00:26.640 --> 06:00:35.060
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: to give it further study that we, instead of extension, line extension of the city electrification,

asr-006477
06:00:35.300 --> 06:00:42.000
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: only unserviceable and unviable, baka pwede namin i-substitute na lang ng photovoltaic beam streaming

asr-006478
06:00:42.000 --> 06:00:50.460
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: because it might not really be worthwhile to extend the lines for city electrification

asr-006479
06:00:50.460 --> 06:00:54.640
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: if it would just add up to the technical systems loss.

asr-006480
06:00:54.640 --> 06:00:56.580
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: And we will do.

asr-006481
06:00:56.640 --> 06:01:05.140
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: We will do a rundown, a study on those pending programs in NEA,

asr-006482
06:01:05.420 --> 06:01:10.540
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: and we will check and we will do a simulation of whether or not it would be better

asr-006483
06:01:10.540 --> 06:01:15.960
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: just to provide a solar home system rather than line extension

asr-006484
06:01:15.960 --> 06:01:21.040
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: to arrest the increase of the technical systems loss.

asr-006485
06:01:22.660 --> 06:01:24.640
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Salamat po, Congressman Aloneta.

asr-006486
06:01:26.060 --> 06:01:26.620
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: At yung...

asr-006487
06:01:26.620 --> 06:01:32.580
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: sa ancillary charges po, ito lang po sa ERC.

asr-006488
06:01:33.580 --> 06:01:40.900
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Yung ancillary charges po natin, Chairman Juan, Mr. Chairman, Madam Secretary,

asr-006489
06:01:41.480 --> 06:01:43.460
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: hindi ba masyadong mahal po ito?

asr-006490
06:01:44.340 --> 06:01:50.060
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Like 60% of our transmission charges are ancillary charges.

asr-006491
06:01:50.480 --> 06:01:54.060
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: When this can be brought down to only about 10 or 15%,

asr-006492
06:01:54.060 --> 06:01:56.480
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: ang laki-laki na binabayad po sa ancillary charges.

asr-006493
06:01:56.620 --> 06:01:58.280
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Hindi po pinag-uusapan yun?

asr-006494
06:01:58.620 --> 06:02:00.480
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Hindi po po pwedeng maibaba po yun?

asr-006495
06:02:01.280 --> 06:02:03.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay, thank you for the last question.

asr-006496
06:02:03.780 --> 06:02:08.760
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Opo, yung pong pinagkukuna ng NGCP na ancillary services,

asr-006497
06:02:09.180 --> 06:02:13.780
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: dalawa po kasi yun, through ASPA o yung kontrata or through the reserve market.

asr-006498
06:02:14.180 --> 06:02:20.660
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Yung through ASPA, ito po ay dumadaan sa CSP and sa approval ng ERC.

asr-006499
06:02:20.660 --> 06:02:26.160
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, stable yung presyo dyan pagdating sa mga contracted volumes.

asr-006500
06:02:26.620 --> 06:02:33.560
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Ang hindi matiyak ay yung presyohan sa reserve market dahil this is market-based

asr-006501
06:02:33.560 --> 06:02:41.220
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and ang existing offer cap dyan sa reserve market ay 25 pesos per kilowatt hour.

asr-006502
06:02:42.120 --> 06:02:48.600
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: At ang nakikita natin, meron nga po kaming pending na proposal sa ERC

asr-006503
06:02:48.600 --> 06:02:53.660
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: dahil nakikita rin natin na parang napakataas yung lumalabas ng presyo sa reserve market

asr-006504
06:02:53.660 --> 06:02:56.600
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: at initially ang pinag-propose nga namin ay,

asr-006505
06:02:56.620 --> 06:02:59.840
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: iba ba ito to 9 pesos from 25 to 9 pesos.

asr-006506
06:03:00.000 --> 06:03:05.800
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, pinag-aaralan na lang namin yung mga sinubmit na comments and yung mga inputs

asr-006507
06:03:05.800 --> 06:03:09.100
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: during the public consultation and we will soon decide on this.

asr-006508
06:03:09.480 --> 06:03:15.980
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And hopefully, kung magkakaroon na ng ibang offer cap na which will be lower than the existing,

asr-006509
06:03:16.480 --> 06:03:19.940
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: it will help temper yung pricing in the reserve market.

asr-006510
06:03:19.940 --> 06:03:25.560
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And at the same time, it will also signify na yung mga ibang may,

asr-006511
06:03:25.560 --> 06:03:32.120
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: may capacity na pwedeng pang ancillary ay i-offer na lang nila ito sa NGCP

asr-006512
06:03:32.120 --> 06:03:35.360
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: under the contract markets through the ASPA

asr-006513
06:03:35.360 --> 06:03:39.640
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and mag-participate sila sa mga CSP yung ipapatawag ng NGCP.

asr-006514
06:03:41.620 --> 06:03:46.340
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Madam Secretary and to the entire DOE family, we wish you the best of luck.

asr-006515
06:03:46.760 --> 06:03:49.360
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: Congress is here to support all of you.

asr-006516
06:03:49.360 --> 06:03:55.360
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: From what I hear, you have a lot of realistic and exciting possible solutions.

asr-006517
06:03:55.560 --> 06:03:58.480
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: So, the challenge is to see it through.

asr-006518
06:03:59.200 --> 06:04:02.060
Rep. Arthur C. Yap: So, thank you to all the resource people.

asr-006519
06:04:02.840 --> 06:04:04.500
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you, Congressman.

asr-006520
06:04:05.240 --> 06:04:11.000
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Hearing that from you, former Cabinet Secretary, former Governor, Congressman,

asr-006521
06:04:11.220 --> 06:04:13.340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: it's a big compliment for the DOE family.

asr-006522
06:04:13.900 --> 06:04:14.440
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you, boss.

asr-006523
06:04:15.520 --> 06:04:17.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Next, to interpolate from the majority.

asr-006524
06:04:18.240 --> 06:04:24.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Before that, I would like to acknowledge the presence of our Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations,

asr-006525
06:04:24.420 --> 06:04:25.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Congresswoman.

asr-006526
06:04:25.560 --> 06:04:26.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mika Suansing.

asr-006527
06:04:27.440 --> 06:04:28.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, ma'am, for being here.

asr-006528
06:04:29.400 --> 06:04:32.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, next to interpellate is Congressman Javi.

asr-006529
06:04:33.940 --> 06:04:35.220
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair, Madam Secretary.

asr-006530
06:04:35.820 --> 06:04:36.640
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Yes, thank you so much.

asr-006531
06:04:37.100 --> 06:04:38.000
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Alam ko mahabang araw.

asr-006532
06:04:38.160 --> 06:04:41.140
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, I'd like to start with thanking Secretary Guerin and the whole DOE.

asr-006533
06:04:42.260 --> 06:04:47.260
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Nakikita po natin na household electrification is now at 94.93%, di ba?

asr-006534
06:04:47.800 --> 06:04:54.580
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And collected since 2022, in July, we are 3.3 million homes.

asr-006535
06:04:54.580 --> 06:04:54.900
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: No?

asr-006546
06:04:55.560 --> 06:04:56.680
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, that's a great feat.

asr-006547
06:04:56.880 --> 06:05:04.300
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And during the energy emergency, nagita po natin, the department had 1,847 megawatts online.

asr-006548
06:05:04.840 --> 06:05:10.080
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And especially sa ka-region po namin, sa Sikihore, it's a 24-hour power back.

asr-006549
06:05:10.220 --> 06:05:13.140
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, congratulations, Madam Secretary and the whole team.

asr-006550
06:05:13.820 --> 06:05:22.240
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Gusto ko rin i-commend ang napakagaling na at matapang nating Administrator Almeda ng NEA,

asr-006551
06:05:22.240 --> 06:05:24.240
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: na accounts 91 cooperatives rated at AAA.

asr-006552
06:05:25.480 --> 06:05:32.600
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: May 154,000 solar home systems on the way. So, congratulations po.

asr-006553
06:05:33.260 --> 06:05:39.720
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I'm not sure kung na-tanong po ito kanina, pero gusto kong i-clear po yung nangyari sa May 13,

asr-006554
06:05:39.720 --> 06:05:43.260
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: about sa Tower 17, na may corroded na insulators.

asr-006555
06:05:44.080 --> 06:05:47.900
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Yung repairs kasi was never finished, if I'm not mistaken.

asr-006556
06:05:48.560 --> 06:05:50.800
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And then, millions paid for that delay.

asr-006557
06:05:51.080 --> 06:05:53.920
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: First po, in darkness, sa ating mga kababayan.

asr-006558
06:05:53.920 --> 06:06:00.120
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, four months on, wala pa yatang case ang na-file.

asr-006559
06:06:00.360 --> 06:06:01.300
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Is that correct?

asr-006560
06:06:01.440 --> 06:06:08.260
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, I wanted to ask, clearly, if failure in repair, which is a known defect,

asr-006561
06:06:08.380 --> 06:06:11.680
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: which is in one of our country's most critical corridor, no?

asr-006562
06:06:12.240 --> 06:06:16.480
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Is that a violation of NGCP's concession obligations?

asr-006563
06:06:17.320 --> 06:06:22.380
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And has the department formally referred this matter to the ERC, Madam Secretary?

asr-006564
06:06:23.920 --> 06:06:30.600
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, that was critical, but the regulation is under ERC.

asr-006565
06:06:30.600 --> 06:06:40.060
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And I think the discipline of the stakeholders is under the ERC.

asr-006566
06:06:43.430 --> 06:06:47.610
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Yes, Mr. Chair, we will look into that incident involving that tower,

asr-006567
06:06:48.110 --> 06:06:55.250
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: and we'll check if that has affected NGCP's performance, reliability performance,

asr-006568
06:06:55.470 --> 06:06:56.610
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: and we will act accordingly.

asr-006569
06:06:57.050 --> 06:06:57.170
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Okay.

asr-006570
06:06:57.170 --> 06:07:03.010
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair, ito kasi sa Das Marinas, Elysia, na 500 kilowatt line na na-trip.

asr-006571
06:07:03.390 --> 06:07:04.830
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: But, thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-006572
06:07:05.690 --> 06:07:11.690
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I'd like to go on to something that's sa amin, sa Negro Simpanay.

asr-006573
06:07:11.790 --> 06:07:13.730
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Madam Secretary, it's from Iloilo.

asr-006574
06:07:15.630 --> 06:07:21.450
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: I'm sure you know what I'm going to, but Negro Simpanay only carries 90 megawatts.

asr-006575
06:07:21.750 --> 06:07:27.150
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And now that there's 68 billion in Cebu-Negros-Panay backbone that was finished in 2024,

asr-006576
06:07:27.170 --> 06:07:31.570
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: and I want to credit the administration and department for that.

asr-006577
06:07:32.330 --> 06:07:36.630
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: But line 2, I think, still remains unapproved, if that's correct.

asr-006578
06:07:37.310 --> 06:07:44.110
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And just days ago, we were able to see that ERC pushed for the Amlan-Dumaguete line

asr-006579
06:07:44.110 --> 06:07:47.850
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: back to March 2027.

asr-006580
06:07:48.330 --> 06:07:54.130
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, sa amin po, nag-host po kami ng about 500 megawatts of renewable power.

asr-006581
06:07:54.850 --> 06:07:57.150
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Pero, 3 out of every 4 megawatts of renewable power,

asr-006582
06:07:57.170 --> 06:08:00.770
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: 4 kilowatt hours we consume, still comes outside of our island.

asr-006583
06:08:01.510 --> 06:08:06.190
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, we generate clean power, we export it, and ang nangyayari po sa amin,

asr-006584
06:08:06.370 --> 06:08:09.590
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: we import ang expensive na kuryente.

asr-006585
06:08:09.790 --> 06:08:14.430
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, gusto ko lang po itanong, meron bang timeline na pagfunding sa line 2

asr-006586
06:08:14.430 --> 06:08:16.530
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: and the final CNP approval?

asr-006587
06:08:16.830 --> 06:08:20.610
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And I just want to share na, specifically po sa aming distrito, Mr. Chair,

asr-006588
06:08:20.730 --> 06:08:25.530
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: kasi ang challenges po namin, ang daming renewable energy projects na pumapasok,

asr-006589
06:08:25.530 --> 06:08:26.410
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: which we're very happy.

asr-006590
06:08:27.170 --> 06:08:30.810
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Kailangan ng pag-process mas smooth, mas mabilis.

asr-006591
06:08:31.510 --> 06:08:34.850
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Pero, yung kailangan po namin, Cebu-Negro submarine cable.

asr-006592
06:08:35.390 --> 06:08:39.810
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And number 2, yung sa upgrading ng Granada 230 KV A-line.

asr-006593
06:08:40.470 --> 06:08:46.810
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And then, yung estimates po natin, there's about 1,300 megawatts projects sa Negros,

asr-006594
06:08:47.310 --> 06:08:48.610
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: highly to enter 2030.

asr-006595
06:08:49.410 --> 06:08:54.130
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Pero, ang problema is, meron po tayong post-potential curtailment risks,

asr-006596
06:08:54.130 --> 06:08:56.130
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: which is about most likely 10%.

asr-006597
06:08:57.170 --> 06:09:01.250
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Ito po na rin sa Luzon, that there are about 20% to 30% curtailments na.

asr-006598
06:09:01.350 --> 06:09:04.330
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, we'd like to hear your answer, Madam Secretary.

asr-006599
06:09:04.590 --> 06:09:09.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, unfortunately, how the pace that we're going,

asr-006600
06:09:09.530 --> 06:09:11.690
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: generation seems faster than transmission.

asr-006601
06:09:12.510 --> 06:09:18.150
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But I leave it to President Jomar to answer the two issues,

asr-006602
06:09:18.710 --> 06:09:22.250
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: the CNP, I think that's Cebu-Negro-Spanay, and then the…

asr-006603
06:09:22.250 --> 06:09:23.550
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Please go ahead, Mr. Chair.

asr-006604
06:09:23.590 --> 06:09:24.830
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-006605
06:09:25.010 --> 06:09:25.830
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: To respond, the…

asr-006606
06:09:27.170 --> 06:09:31.650
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: The Granada KV substation line is part of the priority projects listed by the department.

asr-006607
06:09:32.090 --> 06:09:38.070
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: So, we are working with NGCP on how they can fast-track and complete that project as soon as possible.

asr-006608
06:09:38.850 --> 06:09:43.670
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: For the CNP line, I think you're correct, it's set for 2027.

asr-006609
06:09:44.190 --> 06:09:48.670
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: We continue to monitor the TDP as committed by NGCP.

asr-006610
06:09:48.830 --> 06:09:51.650
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: In fact, currently, we are in consultation with them.

asr-006611
06:09:51.650 --> 06:09:56.730
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: The DOE will also have a session on the TDP of NGCP.

asr-006612
06:09:57.170 --> 06:09:58.070
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: So, next week.

asr-006613
06:09:58.450 --> 06:10:01.630
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: So, we can report back to you on that, on the status of those projects.

asr-006614
06:10:02.730 --> 06:10:07.550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair, please, dahil ang na-delay na po ito eh, from dapat 2030,

asr-006615
06:10:07.930 --> 06:10:13.510
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: ang projected 2034, and sayang po yung mga potential projects sa amin.

asr-006616
06:10:14.190 --> 06:10:17.830
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Actually, may mga pumapasok pa, pero kung hindi kaya ng transmission,

asr-006617
06:10:18.530 --> 06:10:21.070
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: mukhang may curtailment na naman na iakit.

asr-006618
06:10:21.550 --> 06:10:26.550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Mr. Chair, gusto ko lang itanong siguro kung magkano po ba yung profits ng NGCP?

asr-006619
06:10:27.170 --> 06:10:31.350
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Ano ba yung pwede nilang, kasi alam ko may mga dividends din yan.

asr-006620
06:10:32.390 --> 06:10:35.550
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Hindi yata nag-pull through ang dapat na board seats ng Maharlika.

asr-006621
06:10:35.690 --> 06:10:41.310
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Ano po yung, Madam Secretary, pwede ba natin i-fast-track?

asr-006622
06:10:41.490 --> 06:10:44.150
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Or baka pwedeng mas maaga yung upgrades na po ito?

asr-006623
06:10:45.850 --> 06:10:51.670
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, before I answer the question, Mr. Chair,

asr-006624
06:10:52.150 --> 06:10:57.150
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: that's why we're pushing also for more, like 50 megawatts of batteries in Negros.

asr-006625
06:10:57.170 --> 06:11:02.190
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Para i-store pag umaga kasi sobra yung power ninyo.

asr-006626
06:11:02.310 --> 06:11:05.370
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So i-store siya para pag gabi, then you can use it.

asr-006627
06:11:05.550 --> 06:11:09.170
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So that could be one solution alternative because fortunately,

asr-006628
06:11:10.090 --> 06:11:14.150
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: or unfortunately, Negros Island doesn't want any fossil-based power.

asr-006629
06:11:16.050 --> 06:11:21.930
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: On the part of, ano yun, yung profit of NGCP,

asr-006630
06:11:21.930 --> 06:11:22.010
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: NGCP,

asr-006631
06:11:22.010 --> 06:11:28.350
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: it's a work in progress.

asr-006632
06:11:29.530 --> 06:11:34.010
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But they do have, reportedly though, reportedly, if I'm not mistaken,

asr-006633
06:11:34.390 --> 06:11:37.350
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: this was based in last year's research,

asr-006634
06:11:37.730 --> 06:11:42.290
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: they reportedly have dividends of 20 billion a year on average.

asr-006635
06:11:45.850 --> 06:11:50.370
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And so I cannot tell you what the exact profit of that,

asr-006636
06:11:50.470 --> 06:11:51.970
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: but that's a dividends and it shows.

asr-006637
06:11:52.070 --> 06:11:56.950
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That there is 20 billion at the very minimum in NGCP.

asr-006638
06:11:57.190 --> 06:11:59.410
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Now, for their performance,

asr-006639
06:12:01.070 --> 06:12:04.610
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: ERC has the power to regulate.

asr-006640
06:12:05.430 --> 06:12:09.670
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: DOE can issue the policies that concerns them.

asr-006641
06:12:10.170 --> 06:12:15.470
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But I think, Mr. Chair, if Congress is willing to do so, the legislative,

asr-006642
06:12:15.470 --> 06:12:21.470
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: the powers of the committee and then the Permitting Energy Committee on Franchise

asr-006643
06:12:22.010 --> 06:12:30.870
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: and also the Joint Committee on Energy also has the power to regulate that.

asr-006644
06:12:30.870 --> 06:12:37.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So it would, if we have a request concerning NGCP,

asr-006645
06:12:37.050 --> 06:12:42.770
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I think that would be the better avenue if the Congress can review their performance

asr-006646
06:12:42.770 --> 06:12:45.050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: on the franchise that is given to them.

asr-006647
06:12:45.910 --> 06:12:48.230
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Thank you, Madam Secretary and Mr. Chair.

asr-006648
06:12:48.470 --> 06:12:49.790
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: One last question before I close.

asr-006649
06:12:49.790 --> 06:12:50.430
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Rigo, ano yung?

asr-006654
06:12:51.990 --> 06:12:55.010
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: AI and tech, you mentioned that, nandun din po sa inyong presentation.

asr-006655
06:12:55.310 --> 06:13:00.390
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Ano po yung bago niyong ginagawa sa DOE na makakatulong para sa inyong departamento?

asr-006656
06:13:00.930 --> 06:13:05.170
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you for asking because this is one of our most exciting projects.

asr-006657
06:13:06.890 --> 06:13:09.170
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Now, with us here, is Yusek Sasa.

asr-006658
06:13:10.430 --> 06:13:15.990
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: She's new to the DOE but she's helping us in full automation of DOE.

asr-006659
06:13:16.010 --> 06:13:16.910
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: From DBM, yeah.

asr-006660
06:13:17.130 --> 06:13:17.870
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sa ano na.

asr-006661
06:13:18.150 --> 06:13:18.590
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Na pirate.

asr-006662
06:13:19.730 --> 06:13:20.610
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yusek Sasa.

asr-006663
06:13:20.610 --> 06:13:22.610
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Nakita ko sa TV po kanina.

asr-006664
06:13:22.610 --> 06:13:23.110
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I'll press.

asr-006665
06:13:28.390 --> 06:13:45.970
DBM Undersecretary Maria Francesca M. Del Rosario: Alright, Mr. Chair, for the Department of Energy, as you know, one of the marching orders of the Secretary is to automate and make the stakeholders' lives easier with respect to their dealing with the DOE.

asr-006666
06:13:45.970 --> 06:13:49.970
DBM Undersecretary Maria Francesca M. Del Rosario: So, we're setting up a digital front.

asr-006667
06:13:50.610 --> 06:14:00.110
