Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Now, instead of extending the line, ay lagyan na lang natin ng solar doon, panel, lagyan natin ng battery storage na equivalent doon sa requirement nung sitio na yan, o yung bayan na yan, atuturuan natin, itrain natin na mag-operate sila, without extending the line, nagkaroon din tayo ng sitio electrification program.

asr-006820
06:27:43.940 --> 06:27:46.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That is a very practical solution.

asr-006821
06:27:46.100 --> 06:27:46.840
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yes.

asr-006822
06:27:46.840 --> 06:28:03.040
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Mr. Chair, yung area ninyo, area namin, Eastern Samar, ay doon po dumadaan ang bagyo, pero nakita ko po sa NIP, 200 million pa rin yung iserp, 200 million pa rin yung iserp.

asr-006823
06:28:03.040 --> 06:28:16.260
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, I think NIA should, again, request the speaker, the leadership, na dagdagan yan, kasi pag nag-transforce, libre na nga yung mga line money, pero yung pagkain na Manila doon,

asr-006824
06:28:16.840 --> 06:28:25.420
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, napakaliit po yung 200 million, dalawang bagyo lang yun, tapos na po.

asr-006825
06:28:25.420 --> 06:28:46.420
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, if the NIA will agree on my proposal, pwede nasing maglagyan doon in the proper time yung special provision na the NIA may opt to use new technology instead of extending the line in the case of sitio electrification.

asr-006826
06:28:46.420 --> 06:28:47.640
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Okay.

asr-006827
06:28:48.900 --> 06:28:49.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Agree.

asr-006828
06:28:50.200 --> 06:28:50.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Agree.

asr-006829
06:28:50.860 --> 06:28:51.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yun lang.

asr-006830
06:28:52.320 --> 06:28:52.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

asr-006831
06:28:52.780 --> 06:28:53.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

asr-006832
06:28:54.100 --> 06:28:55.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you sa Congressman Dagoog.

asr-006833
06:28:55.200 --> 06:28:56.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ma'am, last term na po ni Congressman Dagoog.

asr-006834
06:29:01.460 --> 06:29:07.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, kung kailangan nyo sa NIA, kahit saan, energy family, mapapakinabangan nyo po yan.

asr-006835
06:29:07.300 --> 06:29:09.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: No, we will miss them, boss.

asr-006836
06:29:09.000 --> 06:29:11.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I salute you, actually.

asr-006837
06:29:11.280 --> 06:29:11.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah.

asr-006838
06:29:11.600 --> 06:29:11.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ma'am?

asr-006839
06:29:11.900 --> 06:29:12.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah.

asr-006849
06:29:12.200 --> 06:29:13.180
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I salute you, actually.

asr-006850
06:29:13.180 --> 06:29:14.720
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yeah, ma’am?

asr-006851
06:29:14.720 --> 06:29:17.840
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yeah, just for the last,

asr-006852
06:29:17.840 --> 06:29:19.420
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: just to wrap up the...

asr-006853
06:29:20.880 --> 06:29:22.520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ayun, ah, meron pa, mamaya na lang.

asr-006854
06:29:22.520 --> 06:29:24.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay, thank you.

asr-006855
06:29:24.120 --> 06:29:25.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, for the second round,

asr-006856
06:29:25.900 --> 06:29:27.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: we have Congressman Tinio.

asr-006857
06:29:27.120 --> 06:29:28.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sir, you have the floor.

asr-006858
06:29:28.600 --> 06:29:30.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Chair.

asr-006859
06:29:31.200 --> 06:29:32.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Last, kanina I asked

asr-006860
06:29:32.200 --> 06:29:34.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: for a status report on yung

asr-006861
06:29:36.120 --> 06:29:39.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: direct purchase ng DOE for diesel

asr-006862
06:29:39.880 --> 06:29:41.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at the height of the energy crisis.

asr-006863
06:29:41.220 --> 06:29:44.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi, nandiyan pa pero partly

asr-006864
06:29:44.500 --> 06:29:44.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: binigay sa NAPOCOR.

asr-006865
06:29:45.800 --> 06:29:47.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Baka pwedeng mapakinggan lang natin.

asr-006866
06:29:47.540 --> 06:29:48.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nakita ko ang kasamahan natin,

asr-006867
06:29:48.880 --> 06:29:50.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: si former Congressman Coco,

asr-006868
06:29:50.880 --> 06:29:52.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: now President of NAPOCOR.

asr-006869
06:29:52.860 --> 06:29:56.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano pong nangyari doon sa

asr-006870
06:29:57.060 --> 06:29:57.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: binili ninyo? Tama ba?

asr-006871
06:29:57.860 --> 06:29:58.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Binili ba? At anong presyo?

asr-006872
06:29:58.640 --> 06:30:00.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Etcetera.

asr-006887
06:30:00.580 --> 06:30:18.940
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, when we purchased diesel na ginagamit ng Napocor ang diesel sa mga isla niya, they were affected. They would be directly affected. Iaakit yung presyo doon ng electricity.

asr-006888
06:30:18.940 --> 06:30:36.900
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, as a directive, I gave PNOC the authority to sell it to Napocor for generation of electricity at a preferential rate para hindi naman mag-suffer yung mga taga-isla natin.

asr-006889
06:30:36.900 --> 06:30:46.900
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And that worked with them for a while. I think about, siguro kung mga 80 yung presyo, 60 pesos ba yung binigay.

asr-006890
06:30:47.640 --> 06:30:48.900
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: At a loss naman na binigay.

asr-006891
06:30:48.940 --> 06:30:57.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Binenta ng PNOC. But I think that's a sacrifice that we were willing to do para hindi naman mag-suffer yung mga consumers ng isla.

asr-006892
06:30:58.640 --> 06:31:04.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, actually, itong magkatabi pala yung nag-deal. PNOC to Napocor, correct?

asr-006893
06:31:06.880 --> 06:31:08.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: PNOC is easy. Hindi pala, siko.

asr-006894
06:31:08.540 --> 06:31:19.170
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. President Nograles, ibig ba sabihin nito?

asr-006895
06:31:20.250 --> 06:31:28.270
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nakamura sa kuryente yung pagbili ng diesel from PNOC easy?

asr-006896
06:31:28.950 --> 06:31:42.290
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Thank you, Mr. Chair, for the question. Opo, nakamura po sa kuryente dahil yung pagbili po ng Napocor sa PNOC easy ay mas mura po sa mga current suppliers ng Napocor.

asr-006897
06:31:42.290 --> 06:31:50.190
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Ang impact po niyan ay hindi po malaki yung strain sa UCME na napupunta.

asr-006898
06:31:50.250 --> 06:31:51.190
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Doon sa mga consumers.

asr-006899
06:31:52.250 --> 06:31:55.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And how much was purchased by Napocor?

asr-006900
06:31:55.410 --> 06:31:57.850
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Umiiba po yung presyo dahil dynamic po yung pricing.

asr-006901
06:31:57.850 --> 06:32:00.910
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: From PNOC?

asr-006902
06:32:00.910 --> 06:32:10.330
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Opo, umiiba po yung presyo but all in all yung na-drawdown po namin sa PNOC easy is 27 million liters.

asr-006903
06:32:10.730 --> 06:32:12.170
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 27 million liters?

asr-006904
06:32:12.310 --> 06:32:12.490
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opo.

asr-006905
06:32:12.910 --> 06:32:17.570
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, yan yung para sa mga diesel.

asr-006906
06:32:19.150 --> 06:32:20.230
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano na po ba yung mga?

asr-006907
06:32:20.250 --> 06:32:22.430
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa Napocor plants niyo pa?

asr-006908
06:32:22.590 --> 06:32:31.170
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Nag-serve po yan doon sa aming mga diesel power plants sa mga isla, sa missionary electrification areas. So, doon po sa mga areas na yun.

asr-006909
06:32:31.190 --> 06:32:33.090
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung mga barges? Is that it?

asr-006910
06:32:34.470 --> 06:32:38.250
NAPOCOR President and CEO Jericho Jonas B. Nograles: Mostly mga small generators po. Sub 500 kilowatts.

asr-006911
06:32:39.170 --> 06:32:44.870
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Sige. Anyway, I asked for a report on that. Thank you po.

asr-006912
06:32:48.250 --> 06:32:49.970
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang sunod na mga tanong ko.

asr-006913
06:32:50.250 --> 06:32:52.810
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, this has to do with the Luzon Economic Corridor.

asr-006914
06:32:53.190 --> 06:33:10.510
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And makita namin sa website ng U.S. Embassy, meron silang mga announcements about energy-related projects na actually parang mas narinig pa natin ito sa U.S. Embassy kaysa sa Philippine government.

asr-006915
06:33:11.070 --> 06:33:17.290
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kaya gusto natin marinig yung direkta sa gobyerno natin.

asr-006916
06:33:17.290 --> 06:33:19.470
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, yan nakalagay dito.

asr-006917
06:33:21.560 --> 06:33:34.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That yung mga involvement daw ng U.S. in one, nuclear, two, in yung mga fuel pipeline, hydro, and so on and so forth.

asr-006918
06:33:34.100 --> 06:33:41.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, with regard to nuclear energy, binanggit po dito yung 1-2-3 agreement.

asr-006919
06:33:42.280 --> 06:33:51.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At saka may mga pinupondohan ng U.S. like an SMR feasibility study, a nuclear reactor control room study.

asr-006920
06:33:51.560 --> 06:33:58.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Simulator, study tour for Philippine legislators on nuclear, and so on and so forth.

asr-006921
06:33:58.900 --> 06:33:59.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nandiyan po.

asr-006922
06:34:01.580 --> 06:34:09.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam ko po si Sec. Garin, when she was still U.S. Sec., was closely involved with the 1-2-3 agreement.

asr-006923
06:34:09.840 --> 06:34:18.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pwede po bang makapagbigay kayo ng updates and ano ba talaga ang status ng mga...

asr-006924
06:34:18.380 --> 06:34:25.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: nuclear energy sa plano ng Pilipinas?

asr-006925
06:34:26.400 --> 06:34:28.040
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-006926
06:34:29.340 --> 06:34:40.720
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Actually, the activity, the nuclear-related activities mentioned here, that's not necessarily just because of the Luzon Economic Corridor.

asr-006927
06:34:40.980 --> 06:34:42.680
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We've been doing this for a long time already.

asr-006928
06:34:43.560 --> 06:34:47.920
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Some of the studies, like feasibility study, are done with private entities.

asr-006929
06:34:48.380 --> 06:34:49.120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, wala kami dyan.

asr-006930
06:34:49.320 --> 06:34:54.920
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: They talk directly to the types of Miralco, or I don't know if they talk to Aboitis and all the other companies.

asr-006931
06:34:55.640 --> 06:34:58.020
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sila kasi interested din sa nuclear.

asr-006932
06:34:59.520 --> 06:35:03.920
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But some of these activities, yes, we do the simulator.

asr-006933
06:35:04.100 --> 06:35:06.440
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We're trying to lock that in.

asr-006934
06:35:07.160 --> 06:35:10.180
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Also, the trade mission, we do that every year.

asr-006935
06:35:10.780 --> 06:35:13.180
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Not only with the U.S., but all the other countries.

asr-006936
06:35:13.180 --> 06:35:17.360
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, tama naman yung marami dito, Mr. Chair.

asr-006937
06:35:18.380 --> 06:35:20.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Now, what is the status of nuclear?

asr-006938
06:35:20.420 --> 06:35:23.240
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Nuclear is, currently, we already have a roadmap.

asr-006939
06:35:24.580 --> 06:35:31.800
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But, unfortunately, our original roadmap was based on SMR, which could have entailed shorter construction.

asr-006940
06:35:32.100 --> 06:35:37.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pero ngayon, parang it seems like limited yung options on SMR.

asr-006941
06:35:37.420 --> 06:35:38.980
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And maybe we'll go for conventional.

asr-006942
06:35:39.140 --> 06:35:41.140
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But that's something that we have to study further.

asr-006943
06:35:42.360 --> 06:35:44.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But our target is still steady.

asr-006944
06:35:44.560 --> 06:35:47.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We want nuclear energy by...

asr-006945
06:35:48.380 --> 06:35:49.280
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The next decade.

asr-006946
06:35:49.780 --> 06:35:52.700
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It will take time, depending on where it will be.

asr-006947
06:35:53.120 --> 06:35:54.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, kumpleto na po yan.

asr-006948
06:35:54.300 --> 06:36:00.140
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We are complying with the international requirements on safety, security, and safeguards.

asr-006949
06:36:00.220 --> 06:36:07.620
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: At that, training ng tao, supply chain assess, evaluation, legal, international cooperation.

asr-006950
06:36:08.000 --> 06:36:10.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Everything else, we're trying to complete.

asr-006951
06:36:10.820 --> 06:36:15.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And, in fact, we have been reviewed by IAEA na pumasa na kami sa...

asr-006952
06:36:16.500 --> 06:36:16.780
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Ano ba?

asr-006953
06:36:17.500 --> 06:36:18.360
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: In your mission.

asr-006954
06:36:18.380 --> 06:36:18.800
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: In year two, ba?

asr-006955
06:36:20.220 --> 06:36:21.180
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: In year two.

asr-006956
06:36:21.760 --> 06:36:23.280
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, papunta na tayo sa...

asr-006957
06:36:23.280 --> 06:36:25.680
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pag pumasa tayo sa next level, pwede na tayo mag-construct.

asr-006958
06:36:26.300 --> 06:36:33.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: What's lacking now is the regulatory on the safety, which is the fill atom na pinasa natin last year.

asr-006959
06:36:34.040 --> 06:36:37.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It has to be organized and the IRR has to be issued.

asr-006960
06:36:38.140 --> 06:36:44.540
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, once that's there, I think the interested parties can already apply na sa fill atom.

asr-006961
06:36:44.540 --> 06:36:47.040
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And sa amin kasi, it's more on energy lang.

asr-006962
06:36:47.180 --> 06:36:48.140
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pero the safety.

asr-006963
06:36:48.380 --> 06:36:52.480
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: The technology has to go through rigorous evaluation through fill atom.

asr-006964
06:36:52.720 --> 06:36:58.820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang nasa plano ng DOE initially is SMR.

asr-006965
06:36:59.440 --> 06:37:03.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero ngayon sinasabi nyo, baka hindi na SMR conventional.

asr-006966
06:37:04.100 --> 06:37:06.320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It depends, Mr. Chair.

asr-006967
06:37:07.100 --> 06:37:10.260
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It depends on the appetite of the investor.

asr-006968
06:37:10.560 --> 06:37:11.480
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kasi wala namang...

asr-006969
06:37:12.280 --> 06:37:15.720
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Let's just say, I'll give you a ballpark of how much it will cost.

asr-006970
06:37:16.160 --> 06:37:18.000
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pag conventional, mga 10 billion dollars.

asr-006971
06:37:18.380 --> 06:37:20.780
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pag SMR, mga 4 billion.

asr-006972
06:37:21.120 --> 06:37:21.720
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Malaki pa rin.

asr-006973
06:37:22.040 --> 06:37:22.520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Billion.

asr-006974
06:37:22.660 --> 06:37:23.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Billion dollars.

asr-006975
06:37:24.040 --> 06:37:25.320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, it's still big.

asr-006976
06:37:26.480 --> 06:37:29.140
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, you need enough funding.

asr-006977
06:37:30.720 --> 06:37:36.140
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And I don't think government, even in a regular power plant, di naman tayo yung nag-invest.

asr-006978
06:37:36.420 --> 06:37:37.240
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Private na money.

asr-006979
06:37:37.240 --> 06:37:43.240
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we will rely solely on the decision of the private.

asr-006980
06:37:43.420 --> 06:37:45.400
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sa funding, mostly.

asr-006981
06:37:46.540 --> 06:37:48.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung 10 billion and 4 billion.

asr-006982
06:37:48.380 --> 06:37:50.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung 10 billion, US yung provider.

asr-006983
06:37:51.420 --> 06:37:52.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: No, no, no.

asr-006984
06:37:53.160 --> 06:37:54.440
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's an average.

asr-006985
06:37:55.060 --> 06:37:57.340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: All the technologies, yes.

asr-006986
06:37:57.480 --> 06:38:00.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kino-consider nyo rin ba yung China as a provider?

asr-006987
06:38:00.840 --> 06:38:03.280
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We actually invited China for our next forum.

asr-006988
06:38:03.500 --> 06:38:05.060
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we can talk to them what's to offer.

asr-006989
06:38:06.680 --> 06:38:11.660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We're just exploring so we would know what are the technologies available and how much it will cost.

asr-006990
06:38:11.660 --> 06:38:18.000
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, Korea, China, Japan, Canada, US.

asr-006991
06:38:18.380 --> 06:38:21.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: France, those are the main players right now.

asr-006992
06:38:21.820 --> 06:38:22.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-006993
06:38:23.160 --> 06:38:32.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dito po sa, again, US Embassy site, meron daw Energy Secure Philippines program with 24 million dollars funding,

asr-006994
06:38:33.480 --> 06:38:40.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: which includes upgrading power systems at military installations, deploying backup power solutions,

asr-006995
06:38:40.340 --> 06:38:43.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and investing in microgrids and energy storage.

asr-006996
06:38:44.220 --> 06:38:45.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Involved po ba kayo dito?

asr-006997
06:38:45.860 --> 06:38:48.780
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: 24 million.

asr-006998
06:38:49.140 --> 06:38:50.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nabanggit siyo kayo?

asr-006999
06:38:50.100 --> 06:38:50.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 24 million.

asr-007000
06:38:50.140 --> 06:38:52.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kanina sa Visayas, nag-deploy kayo ng energy storage.

asr-007001
06:38:53.020 --> 06:38:54.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is this part of it?

asr-007002
06:38:54.740 --> 06:39:00.220
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: These are, if I understand correctly, Mr. Chair, these are mostly technical assistance.

asr-007003
06:39:01.120 --> 06:39:07.300
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mga, they study, we ask them to study something and then, yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-007004
06:39:08.120 --> 06:39:08.660
